## Targets (`clock.lisp`, `decision 114`)
- `sim-target`: nil or a key: a place of `*places*` (`:skua-yard` is its drop point) or a towable object (`:skua-yard-1` … `:skua-yard-6`, `:pod-14`); copied and compared with the sim.
- `(target-candidates sim)`: the five places in `*places*` order, then the towable objects not already a place in `*objects*` order; removed and latched objects skipped; the rock mover never. `(sim-cycle-target! sim direction)` (+1 `]`, −1 `[`, wrapping; from none `]` the first, `[` the last), `(sim-set-target! sim key)` (nil clears; the map click of `task 164` and `:target` of `task 162` call it), returning the key.
- `(target-state-into! r v sim)`: the target''s r, v at the sim''s t (`place-target-state-into!` or `object-state-into!`); nil without one.
- After each step''s removals and captures (`plan 23`, `plan 24`): a target whose object is removed or latched is cleared, an active target hold goes to rate damping, notice "TARGET LOST: <NAME>".

## Target holds (`controls.lisp`, `clock.lisp`, `decision 114`)
- `hold-kind` gains `:target`, `:anti-target`, `:relative-prograde`, `:relative-retrograde`; `(controls-set-target-hold controls kind q)` engages with the ship''s attitude Q as the start of the transport, or releases when that hold is active (as holds 1–6). Without a target the key is refused with "NO TARGET" (the caller''s message).
- `controls` gains the target scratch: r_T, v_T, a_T (point-mass gravity at r_T) and their time, and the last target attitude (quat); `controls-assign!` copies them, so checkpoints and the prediction''s copy carry the transport. `sim-step-ticks!` writes r_T, v_T, a_T at the step''s start while a target hold is active (a rails target: one Kepler solve per step).
- Direction d: 7 / 8 ± (r_T − r), 9 / 0 ± (v − v_T). Attitude: the shortest-arc rotation from the last target attitude''s nose to d̂, applied to it, then the roll offset; frozen (last attitude kept) below 1 m range for 7 / 8 and 0.01 m/s for 9 / 0 (`*target-hold-min-range*`, `*target-hold-min-speed*`). Frame rate fed forward: d × ḋ / |d|², ḋ = v_rel (7, 8) or the point-mass gravity difference (9, 0). `hold-attitude-into!` takes the controls'' target scratch and τ (time − its time).
- Kinematic (above ×4): `kinematic-hold-attitude` takes the target at τ as r_T + v_T τ + a_T τ²/2, v_T + a_T τ; the step''s end attitude is stored as the last target attitude.
- Settling, the 80 % slew and the settled flags as `decision 70`; the readout''s MODE: "HOLD TARGET", "HOLD ANTI-TARGET", "HOLD REL PROGRADE", "HOLD REL RETROGRADE".

## The target for instruments (`controls.lisp`, `render.lisp`)
- `(target-relative-into! out r v q r-t v-t)`: range |r_T − r|, closing speed −(r_rel · v_rel)/|r_rel| (positive closing), the ship''s velocity relative to the target v − v_T in body axes (F, R, D), the target''s direction in body axes (for the ATTITUDE plot''s ◆); conses nothing.
- The render state gains the target''s key, r and v at t_r (rails exactly; a promoted target from its state at the sim''s t with r + v τ + a τ²/2, τ = t_r − t ≤ 0) and the relative values above; `render-state-update!` fills them.

## Planned burns (`controls.lisp`, `clock.lisp`, `decision 115`)
- `planned-burn` (read-only): label (keyword), `hold-at` and `start` (grid t), attitude (quat, body → inertial), throttle (0.1–1, or 0 for an RCS burn), `rcs` (nil, +1 or −1 along body x), Δv (m/s). `burn-plan` (read-only): the burns (simple-vector) and the coast hold (`:prograde`).
- `sim-plan` (nil or a `burn-plan`, shared by copies) and the cursor (`sim-plan-index`, `sim-plan-phase` `:pending` / `:holding` / `:burning` / `:done`, `sim-plan-rcs-target` the odometer value); copied by `sim-assign!`, consing nothing.
- `plan-step-controls!` at the start of `sim-step-ticks!`, before the cut-off check: at `hold-at` the inertial hold at the burn''s attitude (roll offset 0); at `start` the throttle and `sim-cutoff` = odometer + Δv (engine), or the ±x translation key held (RCS); an RCS burn ends at the first step start where the odometer reaches its target, keys released; after a cut the coast hold, the next burn `:pending`, after the last `:done`. `step-h` lands on the next `hold-at` and `start`.
- The autopilot (`task 160`) builds plans, sets and replaces `sim-plan`, and keeps the pilot''s input off the controls while engaged; this part only flies a given plan, open-loop.

## The prediction (`prediction.lisp`, `decision 116`)
- Horizon: two osculating periods while coasting, one while the throttle is on (`prediction-periods` becomes the coasting horizon; the clock''s prediction is made with 2).
- The copy runs the plan: at ×4 while an RCS burn runs (`sim-plan-phase` `:burning` with `rcs`), else at `*prediction-level*`; `:burn-start` events (value: the burn index) and the existing `:cutoff`.
