INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (26, 3, 'Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety', 670, 'Part 4 of `plan 3: masterplan`: the autopilot''s planner, the orbit manoeuvres of `milestone 3`, flying them and the safety rules. The planner turns a preset and a goal into a `burn-plan` by Kepler first guesses refined by shooting with the flight''s own step function; the sim flies it through `plan 25: Predicted trajectories, targets and target holds`''s executor, with this part''s checks in the same step; the preset menu is a model driven by O and the arrow keys, drawn later by the cockpit and the overlay. It stands on `plan 25` (`sim-target`, `sim-plan` and its cursor, `plan-step-controls!`, `planned-burn`, `burn-plan`, the prediction running the plan, `:burn-start`, the relative nodes, `*prediction-work-per-frame*`), `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling` (the sim''s notices, `checkpoint-request`, `clock-checkpoint`) and `plan 23: Objects on rails and the Earth-orbit places` (`target-state-into!` reads its objects). Later parts read it: rendezvous and station-keeping (`task 161`) add their rows and searches to this planner; the flight scripts'' `:autopilot` and `:burn` expects (`task 162`); the map''s burn markers and goal orbit (`task 164`); the AUTOPILOT screen and AUTO lamp (`task 166`); the overlay''s panel (`task 167`).

The specification: `docs/design.md` "The autopilot", "Controls" (O, Up/Down, Return, Backspace), "Time warp" (the burn''s lead time, ×100 during burns), "Control modes" (the slew rule), "Mass budget and Δv" (burn times), "Instruments" (Burn, More alarms), "Instruments and how each is drawn" (AUTOPILOT: Burn, presets); `docs/architecture.md` "Trajectory prediction", "The clock", "Time warp", "Checkpoints", "Determinism", "Testing". Decisions: `decision 32: Autopilot scope and safety rules`, `decision 31: Warp choices within the time-warp rules`, `decision 19: Time-warp rules`, `decision 20: Trajectory prediction on the frame thread`, `decision 16: Integrator and simulation clock`, `decision 17: Gravity model`, `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`, `decision 34: How death works`, `decision 35: Saving and audio` (plans are not saved), `decision 56: Flight-script actions, start states and the quest play-through` (burn labels), `decision 62: Scope: must rows for each milestone''s Outcome`, `decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer`, `decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms`, `decision 87: Flight scripts in milestone 2: additions, apsis conditions, live fly and scripts/fly`, `decision 112: Grapple, stack and berth in the sim: state, notices to the clock, the latest checkpoint`, `decision 114: Targets and target holds in the sim`, `decision 115: Planned burns as scheduled controls in the sim`, `decision 116: Prediction in milestone 3: horizon, target nodes, closest approach, relative nodes, budget`; and this plan''s own `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims` and `decision 118: Autopilot preset menu and input in milestone 3`.

## Scope and limits
- In: burn construction (centring, throttle rule, RCS rule, attitude, lead time), the first guesses and the shooting for circularise, set apoapsis, set periapsis, change orbit (Hohmann, with a merged plane change), change plane (inclination or the target''s plane); planning jobs on snapshots, the barrier and the shared budget; planning refusals; execution checks in the step (unsafe burn, propellant, attitude error, contact and latch), measurement, replans and trims, completion and its checkpoint request; the burn''s lead-time drop-out and the RCS burn''s ×4 cap; the preset menu model, its keys, input gating while engaged, disengage and abort; the plan''s summary for instruments.
- Out, to later parts: rendezvous, the Lambert solver, phasing, aim points, the clear-path check, the terminal phase and station-keeping (`task 161`, which adds its rows and its search to this part''s job); `:autopilot`, `:burn`, `:dv-below` and the other script vocabulary (`task 162`, through this part''s functions); burn markers, the dashed path and the goal orbit on the map (`task 164`); the AUTOPILOT screen, its clicks, the AUTO, PROP and MSTR lamps (`task 166`); the overlay''s autopilot panel (`task 167`).
- Out, to `milestone 4`: TLI, captures, TEI, mid-course corrections, plans across spheres, the Sun''s 0.551 AU and the consumables rules of `decision 32` (no life support or heat before it); the code leaves room for them (the job''s stages, the refusal list), not stubs.

## Files, in load order
- `src/controls.lisp`: `burn-plan` gains its preset, goal, goal orbit (an `orbit` for the map), reserve (m/s and kg), per burn the shot''s post-cut state (t, r, v) and Isp; still read-only, shared by copies.
- `src/clock.lisp`: the cursor''s added fields (`sim-plan-retries`, `sim-plan-replans`, the `:replan` phase and its cut time); the execution checks beside `plan-step-controls!`; `autopilot-engage!`, `autopilot-disengage!` and the abort, between steps or in the step; the RCS burn''s warp cap and the lead-time drop-out in `clock-check-level!`; `clock-autopilot` (the model''s slot; the struct is `autopilot.lisp`''s, called at run time as the clock calls `prediction.lisp`); the barrier in `clock-step!`; the job''s share of the frame in `clock-frame!`.
- `src/prediction.lisp`: a time horizon for shots (`:until`), the `:burn` drop-out event at the next hold-at from `sim-plan`, the budget split while a job runs.
- `src/autopilot.lisp` (new, after `prediction.lisp`, before `flights.lisp`): burn construction, first guesses, the job and its shooting, goal measures, refusals, the menu model, `autopilot-plan-summary`; `luv-in-space.asd` lists it and `tests/autopilot.lisp`.
- `src/overlay.lisp`: the readout''s MODE "AUTOPILOT" prefix while engaged (`decision 85` extended); the abort and refusal texts in the glyph table (`…` exists; check `:` and digits).
- `src/input.lisp`: O, Up, Down, Left, Right, Return, Backspace in `*key-map*` (Return keeps `:restart` while lost), the held-value repeat, the gating while engaged, the window title.
- Tests: `tests/autopilot.lisp` (new, after `tests/prediction.lisp`), `tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp`, `tests/input.lisp`, `tests/overlay.lisp`.

## Burns (`autopilot.lisp`, `decision 117`)
- `(finite-burn node-t dv-vec mass &key isp thrust)`: duration by `docs/design.md` "Mass budget and Δv", t = m₀ (1 − e^(−Δv / v_e)) / ṁ; full throttle unless under 10 s at full, then the throttle that makes 10 s, floor 0.1; under 0.5 m/s the RCS along ±x (1,780 N, 360 s; `rcs-translation-capability`), the sign keeping the nose within 90° of the coast hold''s direction; start = node − t_burn / 2, on the grid.
- Attitude: nose along Δv (or against it for an RCS −1 burn), cab (−z) radial out at the node, towards the normal when Δv lies within 10° of radial; a body → inertial quaternion.
- Slew estimate: the bang-bang time for the angle from the previous attitude (the last burn''s, or the coast hold''s at hold-at) at 80 % of the stack''s couple about the rotation axis and at most 5°/s (`docs/design.md` "Control modes", `decision 70`); hold-at = start − max(60 s, slew + 10 s), the lead time of `decision 31`.
- Propellant per burn by the rocket equation at the mass after the earlier burns (engine 449.7 s, RCS 360 s); the plan''s reserve max(2 % of its Δv, 20 m/s) in kg at the plan''s end mass.

## First guesses (`autopilot.lisp`)
From the snapshot''s osculating elements (`state->orbit`, μ⊕), the apsis and node times from the snapshot''s own coast shot (the prediction''s events), each node ≥ snapshot t + 120 s plus the burn''s half duration and lead (else the next one):
- Circularise at the next apoapsis or periapsis (row value): one `:circularise` burn of the vis-viva difference, tangential.
- Set apoapsis / set periapsis: one `:apsis` burn at the opposite apsis (a circular orbit: the first point 120 s plus lead ahead).
- Change orbit: a Hohmann to a circular altitude, `:departure` at the next apsis nearest the goal side (periapsis to raise, apoapsis to lower; a circular orbit: 120 s plus lead ahead), `:circularise` half a transfer period later; a plane change asked with it merges into the burn at the larger radius.
- Change plane: 2 v sin(Δi / 2) normal-wise at the cheaper node (`decision 117`): the equatorial nodes for an inclination (Ω kept), `plan 25`''s `:relative-ascending` / `:relative-descending` for the target''s plane; "NO TARGET" without one.

## Shooting and goal measures (`autopilot.lisp`, `prediction.lisp`, `decision 117`)
- A shot: `sim-assign!` of a preallocated copy from the snapshot, `sim-plan` set to the candidate, run by the job''s own `prediction` with `:until` the last cut + one osculating period, at `*prediction-level*` (×4 during an RCS burn, `decision 115`); the same step function as the flight, so a plan flown at ×1,000 is its shot bit for bit.
- Parameters: each burn''s Δv in its node''s LVLH axes (T, N, R); Newton with a finite-difference Jacobian (one shot per parameter), the minimum-norm step (residuals may be fewer than parameters), times re-centred after each iteration; at most 8 iterations, then "NOT CONVERGED".
- Residuals and tolerances on the shot after the last cut: apoapsis and periapsis the largest and smallest |r| over the period, within max(0.1 % of the goal radius, 1 km) (circularise: both at the burn apsis''s radius measured on the coast shot; set Ap / Pe: the asked one, the other kept within the tolerance of its coast value; Hohmann: both at the goal); inclination the mean osculating value over the period, within 0.01°; the target''s plane the angle between the period''s mean unit h and the target''s h at its middle, within 0.01°.
- The job (`autopilot-job`): snapshot, preset, goal, stage (`:coast`, `:guess`, `:iterate`, `:check`, `:done`, `:refused`), iteration, Jacobian column, the best plan; `(autopilot-job-work! job budget)` does at most `budget` work units (the prediction''s units, `decision 116`) and returns the stage; `(autopilot-plan-now sim preset goal)` runs one to the end (headless, tests, `task 162`''s scripts). Preallocated in the clock''s model; a plan conses only its result.
- Refusals at `:check` (the reason shown, `decision 117`): any node of the final shot below R⊕ + 150 km ("BELOW 150 KM") or within R☾ + 10 km ("TOO NEAR THE MOON"); plan propellant + reserve over m_p ("NEEDS <n> KG"); dominant body not Earth or a goal altitude outside 150–300,000 km ("NOT IN EARTH ORBIT", "GOAL OUT OF RANGE").

## Jobs, the barrier and the budget (`clock.lisp`, `prediction.lisp`)
- A running job caps the sim at its snapshot t + 60 s (`*plan-barrier*`): `clock-step!` lands there and takes no step beyond while the job runs; the frame''s accumulator is clamped as at the step cap; warp is not changed.
- `clock-frame!`: `prediction-update!` with at most half of `*prediction-work-per-frame*` while a job runs, the job with the rest, then the steps.
- Staleness at engagement: the flown t past the first hold-at − 10 s, or the flown r more than 1 m from the job''s final shot at the flown t → "PLAN STALE: REPLANNING", a new job from now, engaged when shown.

## Execution in the step (`clock.lisp`, `decision 117`)
Run in `sim-step-ticks!` right after `plan-step-controls!`, and after the contact responses for the notices; nothing here runs once per frame.
- Unsafe burn: while burning, the osculating periapsis after cutting now ≥ R_crash + 25 km but after the remaining Δv applied impulsively along the thrust axis < it → abort "UNSAFE ORBIT".
- Propellant: m_p below the remaining burns'' propellant + half the reserve → abort "PROPELLANT LOW".
- Attitude: the thrust axis more than 5° off the burn''s direction (fine steps only; kinematic steps cannot) → cut, `:holding` again, resume with the remaining Δv (cut-off re-armed at odometer + remaining) once the hold is settled; a second time → abort "ATTITUDE ERROR".
- Contact: a capture, bounce, latch or berth notice of `plan 24` in the step → abort "CONTACT", "LATCHED", "BERTHED".
- Abort and disengage: throttle 0, translation keys released, rate damping, `sim-plan` nil; an abort writes the notice "AUTOPILOT ABORT: <reason>" (the SHIP log, the AUTO lamp of `task 166`); `autopilot-disengage!` (Backspace, pilot input) writes "AUTOPILOT OFF" / "AUTOPILOT OFF: PILOT INPUT" through `clock-message!`. The clock''s model keeps the plan for the map in grey.
- Engage (`autopilot-engage!`): `sim-plan` the plan, cursor at burn 0 `:pending`, the coast hold (prograde) at once, retries and replans 0.
- Measurement at each cut: |v − v_shot(t_cut)| (the shot''s post-cut state by Kepler to the actual cut time) over max(0.2 m/s, 1 % of the burn''s Δv) → phase `:replan` with the cut time; the clock starts a job from that step''s sim re-shooting the remaining burns (after the last leg one `:trim` burn, only when the goal measure misses), its result installed at exactly the cut + 60 s in every mode; at most 2 replans, then "AUTOPILOT: GOAL MISSED" and disengaged.
- Completion: after the last cut (no replan) `:done`, the coast hold, the notice "AUTOPILOT: PLAN COMPLETE", the sim''s `checkpoint-request` (`decision 112`), disengaged.
- Warp: a running RCS burn caps warp at ×4 ("WARP ×4: RCS BURN"; warp up refused "WARP REFUSED: RCS BURN, LIMIT ×4"); engine burns keep `*cutoff-warp-limit*` ×100; the next burn''s hold-at is a drop-out event (`prediction-dropout-event` kind `:burn`, from `sim-plan` directly), "WARP ×L: BURN IN <duration>", ×1 at hold-at. The autopilot itself never changes warp.

## The menu and input (`autopilot.lisp`, `input.lisp`, `decision 118`)
- `autopilot-model` in `clock-autopilot`: open flag, rows (a list of row definitions so `task 161` appends "RENDEZVOUS <PLACE>"), selection, values, the job, the shown plan, the state (`:closed`, `:menu`, `:planning`, `:shown`, `:refused`, `:engaged`, `:off`) and its text; commands `autopilot-key!` with `:open`, `:up`, `:down`, `:left`, `:right`, `:return`, `:backspace` and the held-value repeat `autopilot-held!` (real elapsed time: one step at the press, 8 per second held, ×10 steps after 1 s).
- `(autopilot-menu-lines model sim)`: the rows as text, the selection marked, for `task 166` and `task 167`; `(autopilot-plan-summary plan sim)`: burns, current burn index, total Δv, propellant needed and left after, time to the next burn, its Δv and duration, the arrival (last cut) time; pure, consing only its result.
- `input.lisp`: the seven keys per `decision 118`''s gating; while engaged `input-frame!` writes no held keys and no ramp; a new flight-key press disengages ("AUTOPILOT OFF: PILOT INPUT") and acts from that frame; the title gains "O autopilot".

## Pieces, in order
Each piece is one task: code, its tests, its docs; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass. This part''s tests together stay under ~1.5 s (`docs/architecture.md` "Rules for tests"): shots at `:point` or `:j2` unless the test is about `:full`; at most one `:full` plan per piece.

1. **Burns and first guesses** (`autopilot.lisp` new, `controls.lisp`''s `burn-plan` fields, `luv-in-space.asd`; `tests/autopilot.lisp` new): `finite-burn`, the attitude, the slew estimate and lead time, propellant and reserve, the five first guesses. Tests: Hohmann 400 → 800 km Δv equal to the vis-viva closed form within 1e-9 relative; burn durations of "Mass budget and Δv" (56 m/s wet: 20 s; 100 m/s with 50 t: 83 s) within 0.5 s; a 2 m/s burn at the throttle that makes 10 s, a 0.3 m/s burn on the RCS with the sign that needs no slew for a retrograde Δv; start + duration / 2 = node within one grid tick; the attitude''s nose along Δv within 1e-12 and the cab radial out; slew estimates 180° wet ~40 s and with 100 t ~59 s (`decision 31`) within 2 s, lead max(60 s, slew + 10 s); plane change 2 v sin(Δi/2) and the cheaper node at the larger radius on an e = 0.1 orbit; the reserve floor 20 m/s below 1,000 m/s of plan. Done: tests pass; `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" lists `autopilot.lisp` as built; `AGENTS.md` "Layout" names it.
2. **The planning job and the orbit manoeuvres** (`autopilot.lisp`, `prediction.lisp`; `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp`): the shot with `:until`, Newton with the minimum-norm step, the goal measures, the job''s stages and work units, `autopilot-plan-now`, the refusals. Tests: from the start state (`:point`, `:j2` for the plane cases) circularise after a 50 m/s prograde kick, set Ap 1,000 km, set Pe 300 km from 400 × 1,000 km, Hohmann 400 → 800 km (also once at `:full`), Hohmann with INC 89.5°, plane 89° and the target''s plane (Tern Station''s turned 1° in Ω by a crafted object): the plan flown by `sim-step!` at ×1,000 and at ×100 meets its goal measure within the tolerances of `decision 117`, and its Δv lies within 3 % of the impulsive figure; the job split over 300-unit calls gives an `equalp` plan to `autopilot-plan-now`; work per call ≤ its budget; refused: a goal of 120 km passed to the job ("BELOW 150 KM"), 300 kg for 400 → 2,000 km ("NEEDS <n> KG"), plane TARGET without a target, 400,000 km ("GOAL OUT OF RANGE"). Measure the time per plan (outside `scripts/test`, a benchmark form in the test file''s comment) and record it in "Testing". Done: tests pass; `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" (goal measures, labels, refusals as built); `docs/architecture.md` "Trajectory prediction" (shots with `:until`).
