## Text (`text.lisp`, `decision 126`)
- Fonts through `font-path`; the zpb-ttf loader and HarfBuzz from base `luv` (`luv.slug`, no new system, `decision 3`); HarfBuzz is in luv''s slim shell, so `nix flake check` keeps working.
- `*text-repertoire*`: printable ASCII and `° × … ± ² ³ µ Δ ← → ↑ ↓ ○ ⊗ ▲ ▼ ■ □ ◆ ·` (what `docs/design.md` "Instruments and how each is drawn" and the labels use; part 10 may add). `text-atlas`: for each font the placements of the repertoire''s glyph ids (`slug-device-glyph-for`) packed by one `slug-glyph-atlas-for` call over both fonts, made once with the renderer; `text-glyph` (font, character) → a preallocated record (atlas location, outline box, band counts, advance), `?` for a character outside the repertoire; `text-missing-characters` lists them.
- Runs on a plane: origin, right and up unit vectors (single, the frame of the caller: body axes from the eye for the cockpit), cap height in metres (the em scale from the font''s cap height, `slug-font-cap-height`), colour (linear from sRGB integers), kind and factor:
  - `grid-run!` (monospace): character k of row j at its cell (cell 0.86 × cap wide, 1.6 × cap high, `docs/design.md` "Readability"), left, right or centred in a field; no shaping, consing nothing; for screens (part 10) and the plate.
  - `shaped-run!` (HarfBuzz, kerning), made once; for tape labels and engravings; an optional rotation in the plane.
- `text-batch`: a preallocated single-float instance array of `*text-max-glyphs*` 8,192 records (27 floats: Luvcraft''s 24 and kind, factor, spare), a fill count, regions that callers rewrite (static labels once, screens at 10 Hz in part 10); `text-batch-upload!` writes the used part.
- `:cab-text` live pipeline: Luvcraft''s vertex stage adapted: corners dilated per vertex in pixels as there, positions through the cab block''s clip rows (reversed-Z, `:greater`, no depth write), ink × factor ÷ exposure for kind 0 (emissive) and ink × `cab-irradiance` at the glyph''s origin for kind 1 (lit; until piece 3, a block constant); premultiplied alpha; one draw for all cockpit text. luv.slug''s knobs stay at their defaults.
- Size: ~350 lines in `text.lisp`, ~110 in `shaders.lisp`.

