INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (32, 3, 'Cockpit instruments, buttons, the grapple camera and messages', 400, 'Part 10 of `plan 3: masterplan`: what the cockpit shows and what the pilot touches. The six screens (ORBIT, ATTITUDE, TARGET, AUTOPILOT, SHIP, COMMS) get their lines, plots and modes; the dot-matrix strip, the lamps, the needle gauges and the throttle lever come alive; the 18 buttons, the MSTR lamp, the AUTOPILOT menu and the COMMS screen answer the mouse; the grapple camera renders the view from the cone onto the TARGET screen while armed; SHIP messages scroll on the strip and fill the COMMS log. When it is done the cockpit becomes the default view and the pilot can fly from it alone. It hangs on `plan 31: Text and the cockpit''s structure and view` (`*cockpit-panels*`, the text batch and its regions, `grid-run!`, `shaped-run!`, the cab block, `encode-cockpit`, the `:cab-*` pipelines, `cab-clip-rows!`, `*exposure-cockpit*`, `PLACEHOLDER(166)` on the faces) and reads the sim through the parts before it:
- `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling`: the grapple''s states, `grapple-range-into!` and `grapple-reading` with its tolerance flags, the berth, the transfer, `clock-log` and `clock-log-read`, Y''s `:acknowledge`.
- `plan 25: Predicted trajectories, targets and target holds`: `sim-target`, the render state''s target, `target-relative-into!` (range, closing speed, F R D, the target''s body direction), `prediction-closest-approach`, the holds 7–0.
- `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety`: `clock-autopilot`''s `autopilot-model` and its states, `autopilot-key!`, `autopilot-menu-lines`, `autopilot-plan-summary`, the abort and refusal texts.
- `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping`: the RENDEZVOUS rows, the cursor''s `:terminal` and `:station` phases.
- `plan 29: Meshes of the places, other ships and the grapple`: the objects in the render state and their draws, the floodlight, which the grapple camera sees.
- `plan 30: The map of milestone 3`: `orbit-ribbon-points!` and the trajectory''s points, which the AUTOPILOT orbit plot reuses on its own plane.

The specification: `docs/design.md` "The cockpit" ("Instruments and how each is drawn" with its table and "Lamps in detail", "Interaction", "Readability at 1280 × 800", "Messages and radio", "Ghostty" for COMMS''s terminal look), "Instruments" (the `milestone 3` rows), "Grappling and berthing" (the grapple camera, range and alignment), "The autopilot" ("Picking a preset", "Showing the plan"), "Controls" (B, Y, the mouse), "Scope" → "Feature list" (the rows "Cockpit screens …", "Dot-matrix strip, lamps, needle gauges, throttle lever", "18 cockpit buttons, mouse picking", "Grapple camera …", "Readability rules and colours", "Full instrument set", "SHIP messages on the strip and COMMS; Y acknowledges"); `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order", "Rendering precision", "Dev loop", "GPU tests", "Rules for tests"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "HUD and instruments", "Sun glare and brightness".

Decisions it builds on: `decision 36: Cockpit instruments: Slug screens, dot-matrix strip, gauges and lamps; Ghostty out`, `decision 37: Message channels the story may use`, `decision 7: Placeholder labels: dot-matrix overlay quads` (the 5×7 glyphs), `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`, `decision 4: Depth strategy`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 30: Views and cameras`, `decision 33: Grapple tolerances, contact and berthing`, `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms` (formats shared with the readout), `decision 87: Flight scripts in milestone 2: additions, apsis conditions, live fly and scripts/fly` (input ignored while a flight runs), `decision 94: Render targets in gpu.lisp: cached per name`, `decision 112: Grapple, stack and berth in the sim: state, notices to the clock, the latest checkpoint`, `decision 113: Grapple and contact details the design leaves open`, `decision 114: Targets and target holds in the sim`, `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`, `decision 118: Autopilot preset menu and input in milestone 3`, `decision 126: Cockpit structure and view in milestone 3: frames, draw order, Slug text, head look, exposure, cab light, portholes, bezels, tape labels`; and this plan''s own `decision 127: Cockpit screens'' contents in milestone 3: lines, modes, plots, colours and updates` and `decision 128: Cockpit devices, buttons, picking, the grapple camera and messages in milestone 3`, which hold every number below that the docs leave open.

## Scope and limits
- In: the screens'' lines and modes, the ATTITUDE plot, the AUTOPILOT orbit plot, the grapple camera; the strip, the lamps and their flashing, MSTR and its acknowledgement, the gauges, the throttle lever, the buttons'' lenses and lighting; picking, outlines, clicks, the wheel over COMMS; SHIP messages on the strip and in the COMMS log; the readability and contrast checks; `*default-view*` `:cockpit` and the end of every `PLACEHOLDER(166)`; `tests/cockpit.lisp`''s map of every instrument of "Flight" to a cockpit field.
- Out, to part 11 (`task 167`): the overlay''s message line and autopilot panel in the outside and map views (it calls this part''s `autopilot`-screen line functions only if they suit; the model''s functions are `plan 26`''s).
- Out, to part 13 (`task 169`): the cockpit screenshots in flights and the cockpit rendezvous and capture.
- Out, to `milestone 4` (`task 4: write the masterplan of milestone 4: The solar system: Moon, asteroid belt, planets, the deadly Sun`): SOI time, the Sun, hull temperature, life support; their places are fitted and dark, marked `PLACEHOLDER(4)` in code and shown as "--" or an unlit lamp. Out, to `milestone 5` (`task 5: write the masterplan of milestone 5: Story and quests: the playable prelude`): RADIO, JOB, the MSG lamp, the tape notes; `PLACEHOLDER(5)` in code, the job card reading "NONE".

## Files, in load order
- `src/clock.lisp`: `clock-message-stamp` (the real-time stamp of the last message of a key, kept after the message expires) for the WARP and GRPL lamps.
- `src/post.lisp`: `emissive-for-srgb` (the radiance whose tone map at an exposure gives an sRGB byte triple; inverse of `tone-map-srgb`, clamped below its asymptote) and `inverse-tone-map`, a shader function with this CPU twin (`decision 127`).
- `src/overlay.lisp`: the glyph table gains what the strip and SHIP messages use and lacks (checked against every message text of `plan 24`, `plan 25`, `plan 26`, `plan 27` by `glyph-missing`); `format-duration`, `format-utc` and the readout''s formats shared, not copied.
- `src/text.lisp`: the repertoire''s additions (`²` exists; `⊗ ○ ▲ ▼ ■ □ ◆ …` exist; check `·`, `−`), marker runs centred on a point (`marker-run!`), a region API for rewriting a screen''s runs in place if `plan 31`''s does not already give one.
- `src/cockpit.lisp` (contents, after `plan 31`''s structure; ~1,100 lines more, split into `cockpit-screens.lisp` after `cockpit.lisp` if it passes ~1,500, recorded in "Files in load order"):
  - `screen-lines` per screen (pure, from the render state, the clock, its prediction, the autopilot model and the real time; `decision 127`''s lines), the screens'' text regions, the 10 Hz rebuild and the mode signature;
  - the ATTITUDE plot''s block and markers, the rate bars; the AUTOPILOT orbit plot; the TARGET screen''s two modes;
  - the strip (`strip-lines`, the marquee queue, `strip-dots!`), the COMMS log view (typing, wrapping, scroll);
  - `lamp-states`, flashing, MSTR''s onsets and acknowledgement; the gauges'' lagged values; the throttle lever''s angle; the buttons'' table, lighting and press flashes; the moving instances (needles, lever) uploaded per frame;
  - picking: `cockpit-pick` (pointer → the nearest clickable), `*cockpit-clickables*`, the hover state, outlines;
  - `*cockpit-instruments*`: every instrument of "Flight", "Instruments" → its panel and line or device;
  - the grapple camera''s camera (`grapple-camera-update!`) and the image''s pin projection.
- `src/shaders.lisp`: `:cab-lines` (instanced segments on a plane, width in metres, emissive ÷ exposure; plots, rate bars, crosshair, outlines, dial scales), `:cab-dots` (the strip''s round LEDs), `:cab-attitude` (the sky plot per pixel), `:cab-screen-image` (the grapple image on the TARGET face), `:grapple-post` (grey, noise); the screen faces'' backlight in `plan 31`''s face shader.
- `src/render.lisp`: the grapple camera''s pass before the frame''s own (targets `:grapple-hdr`, `:grapple-depth`, `:grapple-image`, cached per name, `decision 94`), `encode-frame` drawing the new cockpit draws in `decision 126`''s order (devices with the opaque cab, then text, lines, dots, then glass); the frame slot gains their buffers.
- `src/input.lisp`: the pointer''s position kept per frame, left clicks to `cockpit-pick` and the command of the hit through the key path''s gating, the wheel over COMMS, Y''s `:acknowledge` also acknowledging MSTR; button presses from keys flash their lenses.
- `src/main.lisp`: `*default-view*` `:cockpit`; the cockpit''s per-frame state (`cockpit-state`: regions'' last rebuild, lags, MSTR, marquee, log cursor, hover, scroll) in the `game`, not the sim, kept across a restart except MSTR, the marquee and the log cursor.
- `src/capture.lisp`: captures snap the lags, type out the log fully and show the strip''s latest message static; `:pointer x y` to pose a hover for tests.
- Tests: `tests/cockpit.lisp` (most), `tests/post.lisp`, `tests/overlay.lisp`, `tests/text.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/input.lisp`, `tests/render.lisp` (GPU), `tests/capture.lisp`.

## Rules for every piece
- The values the screens show are pure functions; drawing writes preallocated regions. Per frame (plot markers, strip, lamps, gauges, lever, hover) conses nothing after the first frame; a 10 Hz rebuild of every screen conses at most 16 KB and takes ≤ 0.5 ms; the per-frame cockpit work ≤ 0.2 ms beyond `plan 31`''s 0.3 ms, measured and written in "Files in load order".
- Every colour through `emissive-for-srgb` at `*exposure-cockpit*`, so the image shows `decision 127`''s hex; never colour alone ("!" for caution, inverted and flashing for danger, a label on every lamp, a shape on every marker).
- Texts at cap ≥ 0.0175 d (d the face''s distance from the eye) on `plan 31`''s grids; nothing shrinks to fit, a long value is cut with "…".
- CPU tests of this part together ≤ ~0.6 s; GPU checks join `render-frames`'' canvas at 320 × 200 except the readability pair at 1280 × 800 in piece 8; ≤ ~2 s more in all, so `scripts/test` stays near its ~15 s.
- Shaders are live pipelines; `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0 after the frames.

## Pieces, in order
Each piece is one task: code, its tests, its docs; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.

