- `scripts/screenshot /tmp/c.png --view cockpit` shows every screen filled with the start state''s values in their colours, the strip with date and warp, the lamps and gauges; in `nix run` the game opens in the cockpit, the pilot can target Tern Station with ], plan and engage a preset from the AUTOPILOT screen by keys and by clicks, arm the grapple and see the camera on the TARGET screen, read SHIP messages on the strip and in COMMS, and acknowledge MSTR with Y or a click; the game window is closed afterwards.
- `tests/cockpit.lisp` maps every `milestone 3` instrument of "Flight" to a cockpit field; no `PLACEHOLDER(166)` remains.', '2026-10-15T07:23:11Z', 166);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (33, 3, 'The outside and map views'' overlay of milestone 3', 390, 'Part 11 of `plan 3: masterplan`: the overlay of the outside and map views in `milestone 3`. It adds two things there: the latest message line (the newest SHIP log entry) and the autopilot panel (the preset menu, the plan''s burns and the engaged state). The minimal readout stays as `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms` has it, apart from one change: it no longer repeats the message that the message line shows. Everything is a pure function in the readout''s line format, drawn by `readout-vertices!` in the overlay pass after the tone map. The cockpit view draws neither; it has its own strip, COMMS and AUTOPILOT screens.

## Builds on
- `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling`, piece 2: `clock-log` (the last 200 entries, each with its game t, text and notice key), `clock-log-read` (the read mark Y sets), `clock-messages`, `clock-message!`.
- `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety`, pieces 1–4: `clock-autopilot`''s `autopilot-model` and its states (`:closed`, `:menu`, `:planning`, `:shown`, `:refused`, `:engaged`, `:off`), `autopilot-menu-lines`, `autopilot-plan-summary`, the burn labels, the refusal and abort texts; the readout''s MODE "AUTOPILOT" prefix is that plan''s.
- `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping`: the rendezvous rows of the menu, the `:terminal` and `:station` phases.
- `plan 32: Cockpit instruments, buttons, the grapple camera and messages`: the AUTOPILOT screen''s plan lines (`decision 127: Cockpit screens'' contents in milestone 3: lines, modes, plots, colours and updates`). This part moves them into one shared function, `autopilot-plan-lines` in `overlay.lisp`. It also uses the glyph table, which that plan has already checked against every message text.
- `plan 30: The map of milestone 3`: the markers'' capacity (48) and the burn markers'' Δv format (`decision 125: Map in milestone 3: the trajectory line, line styles, plan display, markers, labels, click and focus`).

## Specification
- `docs/design.md`:
  - "Interaction" ("What the outside view adds": the latest message line and the autopilot panel in the overlay).
  - "The autopilot" ("Picking a preset": in the outside and map views a panel of the overlay; "Showing the plan"; "Interrupting").
  - "Instruments" (the readout as built; Burn; More alarms).
  - "Messages and radio" (SHIP; RADIO''s first line and JOB''s one-line form in the overlay come in `milestone 5`).
  - "Readability at 1280 × 800" (colours and "never colour alone").
  - The feature row "Overlay in the outside and map views: the latest message line, the autopilot panel" (must, 3).
- Decisions:
  - `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms`
  - `decision 105: Readout box: placement, padding and the overlay''s capacity`
  - `decision 102: Overlay colours: sRGB integers, linear vertices, encoded in the overlay fragment`
  - `decision 86: Death view, LOST panel and restart in milestone 2`
  - `decision 37: Message channels the story may use`
  - `decision 112: Grapple, stack and berth in the sim: state, notices to the clock, the latest checkpoint`
  - `decision 113: Grapple and contact details the design leaves open` (message texts)
  - `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`
  - `decision 118: Autopilot preset menu and input in milestone 3`
  - `decision 122: Flight scripts in milestone 3: autopilot steps, the record, close work, start states` (log entries keep their notice key)
  - `decision 125: Map in milestone 3: the trajectory line, line styles, plan display, markers, labels, click and focus`
  - `decision 127: Cockpit screens'' contents in milestone 3: lines, modes, plots, colours and updates`
  - `decision 128: Cockpit devices, buttons, picking, the grapple camera and messages in milestone 3` (Y and `clock-log-read`)
  - this plan''s own `decision 129: Overlay of the outside and map views in milestone 3: the message line and the autopilot panel`, which holds every number below.

## Scope and limits
- In this part:
  - the message line: its lines, the severity table, the arrival tracking, the duplicate rule in the readout;
  - the autopilot panel''s lines for every model state, and `autopilot-plan-lines` shared with the cockpit;
  - placement, draw order and the overlay''s capacity;
  - the captures'' switches;
  - CPU tests, GPU image checks and docs.
- Out of this part:
  - the menu model and its keys (`plan 26`);
  - the map''s burn markers and dashed path (`plan 30`);
  - the cockpit''s screens, strip and lamps (`plan 32`);
  - RADIO and JOB in the overlay (`milestone 5`; neither is a visible part of `milestone 3`, so no placeholder);
  - flight screenshots that show the panel (part 13, `task 169`).
- Panel clicks: none. The overlay is not clickable; the cockpit''s AUTOPILOT screen is (`decision 128`).

## Files, in load order (`docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order")
- `src/overlay.lisp`:
  - `*message-severity*`, `message-line-lines`, the `message-line` struct with `message-line-update!` and `message-line-reset!`;
  - `autopilot-plan-lines` and `autopilot-panel-lines`;
  - the readout''s duplicate rule in `readout-lines`;
  - `readout-box-size` and `readout-vertices!` take an optional minimum and maximum width in cells;
  - `message-line-origin` and `autopilot-panel-origin`;
  - `*overlay-max-vertices*` by the rule of `decision 129`;
  - the new defparameters `*message-line-chars*` 60, `*message-line-fresh*` 30 and `*autopilot-panel-chars*` 30.
- `src/cockpit.lisp`: the AUTOPILOT screen''s four plan lines call `autopilot-plan-lines` instead of its own copy. The text stays the same and `plan 32`''s tests stay green.
- `src/render.lisp`: `encode-overlay` (and `encode-frame`) takes the panel''s and the message line''s lines. Draw order: markers, readout, autopilot panel, message line, LOST panel. Nothing in `:cockpit`.
- `src/main.lisp`:
  - `draw` builds the lines in `:outside` and `:map` and calls `message-line-update!` once per frame with the game''s summed real time;
  - `game-restart!` calls `message-line-reset!`;
  - the game holds the `message-line` struct.
- `src/capture.lisp`:
  - captures draw the panel and the message line when `:readout` is true;
  - `:message-age` (default 0, real seconds since arrival) for the newest entry.
- Tests: `tests/overlay.lisp`, `tests/cockpit.lisp` (the screen still equals the shared lines), `tests/render.lisp` (GPU), `tests/capture.lisp`. No new file.

## The message line (`decision 129`)
- `(message-line-lines clock message-line real-time)` returns nil (no log entry) or one line.
- The line''s text: "HH:MM:SS " in game UTC, grey, then the entry''s text, cut at 60 characters with "…".
- Severity: the entry''s notice key through `*message-severity*` (an alist, default `:info`):
  - `:info`: paper white #E8E4D8.
  - `:caution`: amber #FFB000 with "! " before the text. The caution keys: warp refusals and drop-outs, NO CAPTURE and over-rating, release refusals, ENGINE LOCKED, PLAN STALE, NO TARGET, the planner''s refusals.
  - `:danger`: red #FF3030, inverted, flashing at 2 Hz until acknowledged (entry not yet below `clock-log-read`), then steady. The danger keys: autopilot aborts and AUTOPILOT: GOAL MISSED.
  - The worker lists every key that `plan 24`, `plan 25`, `plan 26` and `plan 27` write. A test asserts that every key found in those files'' `clock-message!` and notice calls has an entry or is meant to default to `:info`.
- Ageing: after 30 s of real time from arrival, an `:info` or `:caution` entry turns grey. It stays until a newer entry arrives.
- The `message-line` struct (render side, preallocated):
  - holds the newest entry seen (compared with `eq`) and the real time it was first seen;
  - `message-line-update!` conses nothing.
- Duplicates: `readout-lines` leaves out the newest `clock-messages` entry while that same entry is the message line''s (same text and t). The other live rows, their 3 s, the count of 3 and the 40-character cut stay.
- Placement: the box is centred horizontally, with its bottom 16 px above the frame''s bottom edge. At 1280 × 800 it stays clear of the LOST panel, whose top is at 60 % of the height.

## The autopilot panel (`decision 129`)
- `(autopilot-panel-lines model sim render-state clock real-time)` returns nil while the model''s state is `:closed`, else the panel''s lines.
- Line 1: "AUTOPILOT" in grey, then the state word: MENU, PLANNING…, PLAN, REFUSED, ENGAGED (green) or OFF.
- `:menu` and `:refused`:
  - a window of at most 8 rows of `autopilot-menu-lines` that keeps the selection visible, the selected row paper white inverted;
  - the last line "PLAN [RET]  CLOSE [O]" in grey, or the refusal in amber, "! <REASON>".
- `:planning`: "PLANNING…".
- `:shown` and `:engaged`:
  - the four lines from `autopilot-plan-lines` (`decision 127`''s formats, from `autopilot-plan-summary`);
  - up to 6 burn rows, "<n> <LABEL> <dv> M/S <duration>", with Δv as the map''s burn markers show it: done burns grey, the current one with ">" in paper white, later ones paper white;
  - the rendezvous phase in green while the plan is `:terminal` or `:station`;
  - the last line "ENGAGE [RET]  DROP [BKSP]" in grey, or "ENGAGED  OFF [BKSP]" in green.
- `:off`:
  - the kept plan''s burn rows in grey;
  - an abort shows as "ABORT: <REASON>", red, inverted, flashing until acknowledged; otherwise "OFF  RE-PLAN [RET]  CLOSE [O]" in grey.
- Width:
  - the box is 30 cells wide, fixed: it doesn''t jump as lines change;
  - longer lines are cut with "…";
  - it sits top right, 16 px from the top and right edges;
  - at 1280 × 800 it stays clear of the readout''s widest line (~40 cells).
- The function is pure and conses only its result. It is called once per frame only in `:outside` and `:map`; the readout''s own 10 Hz rule does not apply, since the readout itself is rebuilt each frame.

## Capacity
- `*overlay-max-vertices*` = 2 × (fullest readout + fullest panel + fullest message line) + the map markers'' vertices at `plan 30`''s capacity, rounded up to a multiple of 6.
- Each piece that adds text recomputes it the way `decision 105` did: the fullest strings × dots per glyph × 6.
- The existing `overlay-capacity` test checks the sum.

## Pieces, in order
Each piece is one task: its code, its tests and its docs. `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass after each. This part adds under 0.3 s to `scripts/test`: CPU tests that build lines from crafted states, and two 1280 × 800 captures in `render-frames`'' canvas.

1. **The message line** (`overlay.lisp`, `render.lisp`, `main.lisp`, `capture.lisp`; `tests/overlay.lisp`, `tests/render.lisp`, `tests/capture.lisp`; needs `plan 24` piece 2)
   - Code: `*message-severity*`, `message-line-lines`, the `message-line` struct with its update and reset, the duplicate rule, the bottom-centre origin, `encode-overlay`''s new argument and draw order, `:message-age`, the capacity.
   - CPU tests:
     - no log entry gives no line;
     - an `:info` entry ("LATCHED TERN STATION" at a known t) gives "HH:MM:SS LATCHED TERN STATION" with the time grey and the text paper white;
     - a warp refusal is amber with "! ";
     - "AUTOPILOT ABORT: PROPELLANT LOW" is red, inverted, with an `:on`/`:off` flash by real time while unread; after `clock-log-read` passes it, steady;
     - at an age of 30.1 s the `:info` text is grey;
     - a 75-character text is cut to 60 with "…";
     - the readout leaves out the newest live message that the message line shows, and keeps the two before it;
     - `message-line-update!` conses nothing over 1,000 frames;
     - `game-restart!` resets it;
     - every key that the earlier parts write resolves (see "The message line").
   - GPU test (`tests/render.lisp`, `readout-checks`'' style), at 1280 × 800 with one `:info` and one `:danger` log entry:
     - inside the message line''s computed box, only the exact colours #0A0C0C, #8A8A80, #E8E4D8, and #FF3030 in the flash''s on phase;
     - each of those colours present;
     - with `:readout nil` the box''s region holds other pixels.
   - Done:
     - tests pass;
     - `docs/design.md` "Instruments" gains "The message line as built" under the readout, with `decision 129`, and states the duplicate rule;
     - `docs/design.md` "Messages and radio" names the overlay''s SHIP line;
     - `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`overlay.lisp`, `render.lisp`, `main.lisp`, `capture.lisp`), "Frame passes" item 3 (the draw order), "GPU tests" (the check and its colours).
2. **The autopilot panel''s lines** (`overlay.lisp`, `cockpit.lisp`; `tests/overlay.lisp`, `tests/cockpit.lisp`; needs `plan 26` pieces 1–4, `plan 27`''s phases, `plan 32`''s AUTOPILOT screen)
   - Code: `autopilot-plan-lines` (moved from `cockpit.lisp` if `plan 32` wrote it there; the AUTOPILOT screen then calls it), `autopilot-panel-lines` for every state, the cut at 30 cells.
   - Tests, with a model driven by `autopilot-key!` from the start state (plans by `autopilot-plan-now` at `:point`, at most one plan per test):
     - `:closed` gives nil;
     - O gives MENU with the selection inverted, and the window keeps it visible when Down moves past row 8;
     - a refusal ("SET PE 120 KM" passed to the job) gives "! BELOW 150 KM" in amber;
     - `:planning` gives "PLANNING…";
     - the Hohmann 400 → 800 km plan shown gives the four lines, equal to `autopilot-plan-summary`''s figures in their formats, then the rows "1 DEPARTURE …" and "2 CIRCULARISE …" and "ENGAGE [RET]  DROP [BKSP]";
     - engaged and past the first cut, row 1 is grey and row 2 has ">";
     - a crafted `:station` plan gives "ON STATION 100 M" in green;
     - Backspace gives OFF with the burn rows grey;
     - an abort gives the red inverted flashing text until Y, then "OFF  RE-PLAN [RET]  CLOSE [O]";
     - no line is wider than 30 cells;
     - every character is in the glyph table (`glyph-missing` nil);
     - `tests/cockpit.lisp`: the AUTOPILOT screen''s rows 1–4 equal `autopilot-plan-lines` for the same plan.
   - Done:
     - tests pass;
     - `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" ("Picking a preset", "Showing the plan") states the panel as built, with `decision 129`;
     - `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`overlay.lisp`, `cockpit.lisp`).
3. **The panel drawn in the outside and map views** (`overlay.lisp`, `render.lisp`, `main.lisp`, `capture.lisp`; `tests/overlay.lisp`, `tests/render.lisp`)
   - Code: `readout-vertices!`''s width bounds, the top-right origin, `encode-overlay`''s panel argument in the draw order, `draw` building it in `:outside` and `:map` only, captures, the final capacity.
   - CPU tests:
     - at 1280 × 800 the panel''s box (30 cells) lies within the frame and does not intersect the box of the fullest readout or of the message line;
     - the vertex count of the fullest panel, readout and message line together with 48 markers stays within `*overlay-max-vertices*`;
     - nothing is drawn for the panel in `:cockpit`.
   - GPU tests (`render-frames`'' canvas at 1280 × 800, the Hohmann plan shown):
     - inside the panel''s computed box, only exact #0A0C0C, #8A8A80, #E8E4D8 and #40D040 (none green while shown, green present once engaged);
     - the selected menu row''s block, in a second capture with the menu open, is paper white with dark text pixels in it;
     - the same in `:map` (the panel drawn over the markers);
     - `report-failed-live-artifacts` returns 0.
   - Done:
     - tests pass;
     - in the running game (`./sly play` or `nix run`), O shows the panel top right in the outside and map views, and Return, a second Return, a warp to the burn and Backspace show each state;
     - a `./sly screenshot` of it has been looked at, not committed;
     - `docs/design.md` "Interaction" ("What the outside view adds", as built);
     - `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order", "Frame passes", "GPU tests" and "Testing" (the new checks and their measured time);
     - `AGENTS.md` "Layout": `overlay.lisp`''s list gains the message line and the autopilot panel; "Commands" → "Run": O shows the autopilot panel in the outside and map views.

## Docs and `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/design.md`:
  - "Instruments": the message line as built and the readout''s duplicate rule;
  - "The autopilot": the panel as built;
