- `AGENTS.md`: "Layout" (`overlay.lisp`), "Commands" ("Run": the panel).

## Done when
- The three pieces are done; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass, and `scripts/test` stays near its ~15 s.
- In the outside and map views, the newest SHIP message shows at the bottom in its severity''s colour and stays after the readout''s 3 s.
- The autopilot panel shows the menu, the plan with its burns, the engaged state and aborts, the same as the cockpit''s AUTOPILOT screen.
- The readout is unchanged except for the duplicate rule.', '2026-10-15T07:27:15Z', 167);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (34, 3, 'Earth''s night lights and clouds', 300, 'Part 12 of `plan 3: masterplan`: Earth''s night lights and clouds, both "should" (`docs/design.md` "Scope" → "Feature list": "Earth''s night lights (Black Marble 2016)" and "Earth''s static cloud layer", milestone 3). The specification is `docs/design.md` "Earth" (the night side and clouds bullets) and "Sources", `decision 40: Earth''s look and drag` (its consequence gives the files and sizes) and `decision 13: Asset storage and attribution` (≤ 5 MB a file, `assets/` ≤ 25 MB, `SOURCE.md`, `CREDITS.md`). The numbers the docs left open are `decision 130: Earth''s night lights and clouds in numbers: conversion, packing, radiance, fade, cloud albedo and shadow`. Nothing here depends on another part of this milestone; it touches only the assets, `assets.lisp`, `impostors.lisp`, `shaders.lisp` and `render.lisp`''s texture loading.

## Files, in load order
- `scripts/convert-earth` (new, with ImageMagick from the flake''s pinned nixpkgs in the dev shell, `flake.nix`): as `decision 130`: downloads `BlackMarble_2016_3km.jpg` and `cloud_combined_8192.tif` (URLs in `docs/design.md` "Sources") into a `mktemp -d` directory, checks pinned SHA-256s, writes `assets/earth/black-marble-5400.jpg` and `assets/earth/clouds-5400.jpg` (or into `[out-dir]`); the background floor F of the night map fixed in the script; deletes its temporary directory; two runs identical.
- `assets/earth/SOURCE.md`, `CREDITS.md`: the two files with URL, fetch date, byte size, SHA-256 of source and result, layout, the derivation (the command, F, filters, quality), credits "NASA Earth Observatory images by Joshua Stevens, using Suomi NPP VIIRS data from Miguel Román, NASA GSFC" and "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center Image by Reto Stöckli", NASA''s guidelines as for the day map.
- `assets.lisp`: `merge-alpha-pixels` (night pixels'' RGB, the cloud image''s R byte as A; consing one array), reused by the render''s load; `downsample-pixels` already averages A.
- `shaders.lisp` (`earth-fragment`): night lights and clouds per `decision 130`: the night texture and its 1/8 copy mixed by the same footprint as the day map; lights × `*night-lights-radiance*` × smoothstep(+0.05 → −0.10 in n·s) × (1 − 0.6 α); clouds white × `*cloud-albedo*` mixed by α, lit as the ground; the ground''s shadow (1 − `*cloud-shadow*` α′) at the point moved toward the Sun by h·tan z (5 km, capped 40 km); the rim and the halo unchanged. Two more bindings (night view and its 1/8 view; the day map''s sampler serves).
- `impostors.lisp`: the tunables `*night-lights-radiance*`, `*cloud-albedo*`, `*cloud-shadow*`, `*cloud-height*`, `*cloud-shadow-cap*` into the frame uniforms (a vec4 beside `earth-shade`, or its free component and one more; the worker picks, the shader comment names it); live-redefinable like `*rim-strength*`.
- `render.lisp`: `*earth-night-texture*`, `*earth-clouds-texture*`; at renderer start decode both, merge, upload with its 1/8 copy beside the day map (`texture-from-pixels`, `:rgba8-unorm-srgb`: RGB decoded, A linear); the bind group gains the two views. GPU memory grows by one 58 MB texture, not two.

## Pieces, in order
1. **Convert and commit the two textures** (`--web`: downloads; afterwards `scripts/convert-earth` reruns them). `scripts/convert-earth`, ImageMagick in the dev shell, the two JPEGs, `SOURCE.md`, `CREDITS.md`; F measured once from the 3 km image (unlit Sahara around 23° N 10° E and the open Pacific around 0° 150° W read 0 after it), fixed in the script.
   - Tests (`tests/assets.lisp`, one shared decode of each, as the Blue Marble''s): each file exists, ≤ 5 MB, decodes to 2700 × 5400; `assets/` ≤ 25 MB; night: the Nile delta (30.0° N, 31.2° E) and the Po valley bright (R+G+B above 200 at the texel or its 3 × 3 block''s maximum), the Sahara and the open Pacific texels 0 per byte within 2; clouds: the 1/8 copy''s mean over the Southern Ocean (50–60° S) above the Sahara''s (15–30° N, 0–30° E) by 50 of 255; `merge-alpha-pixels` keeps RGB and puts the cloud byte in A.
   - Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Assets" (the files, sizes, the script), "Files in load order" (`assets.lisp`), `AGENTS.md` "Commands" (`scripts/convert-earth [out-dir]`, needs network, its time) and "Layout" (`assets/earth/`, `scripts/`).
   - Done when: a second run of `scripts/convert-earth /tmp/x` gives the same SHA-256s as the committed files; `nix build` installs both under `result/share/luv-in-space/assets/earth/`; `scripts/test` passes.
2. **Night lights in the Earth shader.** The night texture loaded (A 255 until piece 3), its 1/8 copy, the lights and the terminator fade of `decision 130`.
   - Tests (`tests/render.lisp`, in `render-frames`'' canvas, one frame each): a nadir camera at night over Europe or the Nile (the start epoch, 2040-01-01 00:00 UTC, is night there; set by state, not flown) reads a bright pixel count above zero and its mean above the same frame with `*night-lights-radiance*` 0 by at least 5; the existing "night side at the nadir < 8" stays, moved to a point over open ocean if its nadir now shows lights (say so in its comment); a sunlit nadir frame differs from the same with lights off by at most 1 per pixel (no lights by day).
   - Docs: `docs/design.md` "Earth" night bullet gains "As built" with the numbers; `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`impostors.lisp`, `render.lisp`, the tunables), "GPU tests".
