3. **Clouds and their shadow.** Cloud cover into A (`merge-alpha-pixels` at load), white clouds lit as the ground, lights dimmed beneath them, the offset shadow of `decision 130`.
   - Tests (`tests/render.lisp`): a sunlit nadir frame over a cloudy region (the Southern Ocean or the ITCZ, chosen from the texture) reads its mean at least 10 above the same frame with `*cloud-albedo*` 0 and `*cloud-shadow*` 0; Earth from 40,000 km still round within 2 px and lit; the shadow offset as a pure CPU function (`cloud-shadow-offset` in `impostors.lisp`, its shader twin in step) against closed form: 0 at the subsolar point, h·tan z below the cap, the cap at grazing light.
   - Docs: `docs/design.md` "Earth" clouds bullet "As built"; `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order", "GPU tests"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Spheres and planet surfaces" or its clouds line: from "assumed" to "ran", with the run.
   - Done when: a screenshot from the start state shows clouds over the day side and their shadows near the terminator; `scripts/test` passes within its budget.

## Rules
- Rendering files only; the sim is untouched (`decision 12: Module layout and package split`). Shaders stay live: `define-frame-shader earth-fragment` re-evaluated shows on the next frame (`decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`).
- Image checks, never pixel-exact (`docs/architecture.md` "GPU tests"); comparisons against the same frame with a tunable at 0 keep them robust on lavapipe.
- Dropping either layer ("should") needs a recorded reason (`pm decision record`), and the `docs/design.md` "Feature list" row marks it cut.', '2026-10-15T07:30:09Z', 168);
