Decisions: `decision 87: Flight scripts in milestone 2: additions, apsis conditions, live fly and scripts/fly` (screenshots not committed), `decision 109: Live fly: the restart at once, Return and N ignored, the record in ./sly log`, `decision 106: Captures freeze the game, not the clock''s pause`, `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 21: Physics test bounds and flight scripts`, `decision 2: Screenshots and GPU test: offscreen capture on a hidden canvas, headless on lavapipe`, `decision 10: Test and screenshot commands`, `decision 64: Scripts always re-enter the dev shell`, `decision 122: Flight scripts in milestone 3: autopilot steps, the record, close work, start states`, `decision 123: Milestone 3''s flight scripts run in scripts/test-slow, not scripts/test`, `decision 126: Cockpit structure and view in milestone 3: frames, draw order, Slug text, head look, exposure, cab light, portholes, bezels, tape labels`, `decision 128: Cockpit devices, buttons, picking, the grapple camera and messages in milestone 3`, `decision 129: Overlay of the outside and map views in milestone 3: the message line and the autopilot panel`, `decision 125: Map in milestone 3: the trajectory line, line styles, plan display, markers, labels, click and focus`, `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims` (burn labels), `decision 119: Rendezvous planning in milestone 3: Lambert, search, aim and stop points, checks, shooting, burns`, `decision 32: Autopilot scope and safety rules`, `decision 42: Scope: what each milestone builds`, `decision 62: Scope: must rows for each milestone''s Outcome`. This plan''s own: `decision 131: Flight screenshots and live runs in milestone 3: the screen state, screenshot waits, live shots, the cockpit capture script`.

## Scope and limits
- In: the screen state in screenshot entries and captures; the waits `:in-burn`, `:terminal`, `:range-below`; `:approach`''s `:screenshots`; `:screenshot` steps in every `milestone 3` script; `flights/cockpit-k-17.sexp`; live `fly` with `:shots`; the Done when from a clean checkout; `AGENTS.md` and `docs/` against what was built.
- Out: new game features. A picture that shows a fault of an earlier part (a wrong mesh, a missing panel row, a misplaced marker) is a follow-up task in that part''s plan, not fixed here.
- Out: committed PNGs (`decision 87`); `scripts/fly` regenerates them bit for bit.

## Files, in load order
- `src/clock.lisp`: `(clock-screen-snapshot clock)`, a fresh `clock-screen` struct: the nominal warp level, the live messages, the SHIP log (`clock-log`) and its read mark (`clock-log-read`), a copy of the autopilot model; nothing shared with the clock. `(clock-screen-load! clock screen)` writes a copy back. Pure, no HAL.
- `src/flights.lisp`:
  - the `:screenshot` entry gains `screen` (`clock-screen-snapshot` at the step);
  - the waits `(:wait :in-burn <label>)`, `(:wait :terminal)`, `(:wait :range-below <m>)` and their expectations;
  - `(:approach … :screenshots (<view> …))`;
  - live `(fly name &key game shots)` (the pending shot, the pause, the shooter thread);
  - `(flight-status)` gains the PNG paths written so far.
- `src/input.lisp`: P ignored while a shot is pending.
- `src/main.lisp`: the game''s clock takes a screen in `game-load-state!`; the shooter''s pause leaves the render state at the sim''s state.
- `src/capture.lisp`: `capture-game-state :screen`; `fly-screenshots` passes each entry''s screen; `fly-live-shot!` (the window PNG of one pending shot: the view set, 10 frames, `screenshot`).
- `flights/`: `:screenshot` steps in the ten scripts of `plan 28`; `cockpit-k-17.sexp` (new).
- Tests: `tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/flights.lisp`, `tests/input.lisp`, `tests/capture.lisp` (in `scripts/test`); `tests/slow-flights.lisp` (in `scripts/test-slow`).

## Screen state in screenshots (`clock.lisp`, `flights.lisp`, `capture.lisp`; `decision 131`)
- Why: the panel, the message line, the strip, COMMS, the lamps and the warp in the readout read the clock, and a screenshot entry held only a sim.
- `clock-screen-snapshot` copies; changes to the clock after the step leave the entry unchanged (`equalp` to itself before and after).
- `capture-game-state game path :sim s :screen sc`: `game-load-state!` restarts the frozen game''s clock on the sim, then `clock-screen-load!`. Without `:screen`, captures stay as `decision 106` has them (WARP ×1, no messages).
- With a screen the readout shows the snapshot''s nominal warp (`WARP ×100000`), no ACT caution (the rate meter stays empty), the newest message fresh (`:message-age` 0, `plan 33`), the lamps and strip as `plan 32`''s captures snap them.
- `fly-screenshots`: per entry its sim, view and screen; the outside view at its default pose, the cockpit head at Home (`plan 31`), the map framed on opening with the prediction run to completion (`plan 30`).

## Waits for screenshots (`flights.lisp`; `decision 131`)
- Conditions checked after each step, as every condition wait; none passes an `until` to the step, so none adds a step boundary:
  - `(:wait :in-burn <label>)`: the engaged plan''s cursor is inside that labelled burn (from its first step with the burn''s controls to its cut); labels as the record''s (`:phasing`, `:departure`, `:arrival`, `:circularise`, `:apsis`, `:plane`, `:trim`; `decision 117`, `decision 119`).
  - `(:wait :terminal)`: the cursor''s phase is `:terminal`.
  - `(:wait :range-below <m>)`: the target''s CoM within m of the stack''s CoM; without a target the wait fails "NO TARGET".
  - All take `:within` (default 30 days); also as expectations.
- `(:approach <fixture> … :screenshots (<view> …))`: at the step where the 20 m hold goes on (stopped, the offset, angle and lateral speed inside the hold''s limits), one `:screenshot` entry per view, labelled `approach-20m-<view>`; views `:outside`, `:map`, `:cockpit`. A copy, as every screenshot: the approach''s states unchanged.
- Script rule: `:screenshot` steps sit after condition waits or other steps only, never after `:after`, `:at` or event waits added for them. So a script and its copy without the screenshot steps and their waits fly the same states bit for bit (tested in pieces 1–3).

