INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (61, 12, 'Check figures, dates and names across the documents', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/story.md, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. Checked: ship figures (28 t, v_e 4,410, 6,650/1,738/1,017 m/s, 180 person-days, 10 kg/s) in all docs; every quest''s Δv and propellant recomputed by the rocket equation (dry 7,961 kg) against design ''Δv for the standard legs'', ''Earth-orbit points of interest'', ''The Moon'', ''Δv checked against the ship'', ''Rendezvous'' and decision 55, plus story ''Running checks'' and the flight scripts'' :dv-below and :propellant-above; dates (start, TLI 01-20 06:01, Moon 01-26 02:36, BQ7 found 01-19, meeting 03-10 ~23:00, perigee 03-12 12:00, TANKER 3 schedule) against decisions 50, 55, 58; names, call signs and ids of story ''Names and terms'' in design and architecture; units, frames, epoch and constants of decision 14. Quest 7''s ''1,378 + 1,353'' was right (25 to POD 14 + 1,353 out, then 1,353 back; 12,821 kg out = 203 + 12,618) but unclear. Changed: story quest table row 7 Δv and stores cells (≤ 12 days away out, as its Propellant line and Running checks say, not ≤ 7 per leg); story quest 4 gain on Fulmar 7.8°/orbit, 2.96 days (as design); story Running checks TLI at 2040-01-20 06:01 (decision 55); architecture quest-3 :propellant-above 22310 (Running checks'' 22,870 less 560; was 22,333, stale); design Highport TLI 376 m/s from the 2040-01-20 06:01 perigee (was 370 and ''near 01-21'', decision 55); design TANKER 3 Fulmar slot r = 6,878.1366 km (R⊕ of decision 14); design BQ7 check ''stack (58 t dry, 72.6 t wet)''; design rigid-body rows named GRINDSTONE and 2040 BQ7.', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

## What to check
- The ship''s figures in every document match `docs/design.md` "Parts", "Mass budget and Δv": 28 t of LH2/LOX, v_e 4,410 m/s, 6,650 m/s empty, 1,738 m/s with 50 t, 1,017 m/s with 100 t, 180 person-days, 10 kg/s transfer.
- Δv per leg in `docs/story.md` (quest table, per-quest "Propellant" lines, "Running checks") against `docs/design.md` "Δv for the standard legs", "Earth-orbit points of interest", "The Moon", "Δv checked against the ship", "Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach" and `decision 55: Meeting 2040 BQ7 and the lunar arrival from the polar plane`.
  - Known suspect: quest 7''s "1,378 + 1,353" in the quest table, while `docs/design.md` gives 1,273 m/s for Highport → Peary Depot (1,353 with margin). Recompute or correct it, and the "Running checks" propellant and the flight scripts'' `:dv-below` and `:propellant-above` in `docs/architecture.md` that follow from it.
- Dates and times: start 2040-01-01 00:00 UTC, TLI 2040-01-20 06:01, Moon at Highport''s apogee 2040-01-26 02:36, BQ7 found 2040-01-19, meeting ~2040-03-10 23:00, perigee 2040-03-12 12:00, TANKER 3 leaving Fulmar 2040-03-06 06:00. The same in story, design, the architecture''s flight scripts and `decision 50`, `decision 55`, `decision 58` (`pm show d50` etc. for their subjects).
- Names and ids: place names, call signs, ship names and the ids of `docs/story.md` "Names and terms" ("Proposed ids") used identically in `docs/design.md` (places, fixtures, rigid bodies) and `docs/architecture.md` (flight scripts, start states, removal causes `:burned-up`, `:delivered`).
- Units, frames and epoch: SI and `double-float` world positions, frames (heliocentric, planet-centred, ship-local FRD), the epoch and constants of `decision 14: Units and time epoch`; the same wherever the documents give formulas or figures.

## Done when
- Every mismatch found is fixed in the documents (or is a follow-up task), and the done note lists what was checked and changed.', '2026-10-14T21:19:46Z', '2026-10-14T21:22:29Z', 60, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (62, 12, 'Check the documents against the decision log', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md, docs/story.md, AGENTS.md. Checked: all answered decisions 1-59 against the docs (figures and rules spot-checked: cockpit, views, warp, autopilot, death, grapple, integrator, prediction, ephemerides, drift bounds, pin, assets, rails, rendezvous, story ships, texts); every ''decision N: subject'' citation against current subjects (all matched except AGENTS.md''s example); superseded text of decisions 19, 23, 39, 50 (none left beyond the marked history notes); lasting choices listed by the task (units, frames, integrator, depth, propulsion, death, planets, names, premise) all recorded (14, 15, 16, 4, 22, 34, 39, 49, 48). Changed: luv-capabilities ''HUD and instruments'' and ''What this means'' no longer describe screen textures or leave Ghostty open (decision 36); design ''The Moon'' landing cut cites decision 39, not 34; design ''Pillars'' cites new decision 60: Design pillars (recorded: the pillars were lasting and unrecorded); architecture ''Removal of objects'' and ''Checkpoints'' cite decision 53; story ''Start date'' cites decision 52 instead of task 52, drops ''stays the default''; AGENTS.md citation example now decision 14: Units and time epoch. Supersede links added: decision 55 partly supersedes decision 52 (quest 9''s meeting point, 400,000 -> 325,000 km), decision 58 partly supersedes decision 57 (TANKER 3 leaves Fulmar 2040-03-06 06:00); the docs already followed both. Bare ''decision N'' citations without subject left where the same section cites the full subject.', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

## What to check
- `pm decision list --answered`: every answered decision is reflected in the document it concerns (`docs/luv-capabilities.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/story.md`, `docs/luv-wishlist.md`, `AGENTS.md`), and no document states the superseded part of a decision (e.g. `decision 50` partly superseded by `decision 55`; `decision 19` by `decision 43`; `pm show d<id>` shows the supersede links).
- Decisions are cited by id and current subject; a citation whose subject no longer matches is corrected (`grep -n ''decision [0-9]'' docs/*.md AGENTS.md`).
- Decisions recorded by tasks but missing from the documents, and choices in the documents that no decision records although they are lasting (unit of length, frames, integrator, depth strategy, propulsion, death, planets in scope, names, premise), are listed in the done note; missing records are added with `pm decision record` and cited where the document states the choice.

## Done when
- Every answered decision is in its document, no superseded text remains, every citation''s subject is current, and every lasting choice has a record.', '2026-10-14T21:19:46Z', '2026-10-14T21:25:00Z', 60, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (63, 12, 'Check luv capabilities, wishlist and architecture against each other', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md. Checked: each of the 12 gaps in luv-capabilities ''Gaps and workarounds'' plus ''Other findings'' against architecture ''Written here'' and ''Files in load order'' (all had a workaround, none named its file) and against the wishlist (every reusable gap has a line; starfield and instancing are game-specific); every wishlist line against a finding (two rested on none: the recipe deleting all but fonts/ at ../luv/flake.nix:720, and the Objective-C bridge writing ../build/*.dylib; both verified in ../luv and added); the architecture''s luv reliances: reversed-Z, camera-relative single floats, sdl3-image (ran, runs 29-33), dot-matrix overlay and report-failed-live-artifacts (built here, src/scene.lisp, src/main.lisp), Slug text and render-to-texture-then-sample (ran via Luvcraft''s smoke test, run 28), audio-sink (only read: now ran, run 35 on SDL''s dummy driver; a failing driver signals an error), no Ghostty per decision 36 everywhere; budgets: clock 4 ms / 4,096 steps, prediction 1 ms, rest 6 ms, x100,000 ~830 steps, x1,000,000 ~x490,000, play-through ~15 s, test budgets: arithmetic consistent with ~180 ns per step. Changed: luv-capabilities adds the CPU, run 28''s render-to-texture finding, the two packaging/platform findings, ''luv''s developer'' for the M2 Pro line, the integrator measurement and the budgets resting on it in ''Performance'' (GPU side not measured, iGPU target), audio sink ran with run 35; wishlist cites Platforms for the bridge and says the terminal-wall line has no workaround here (cut by decision 36); architecture ''Written here'' names each workaround''s file and adds the ''Other findings'' items, audio-sink cites run 35; design ''Performance target'' names the GPU and the measured step cost; decision 61: Performance target GPU: the default Vulkan device, the Intel iGPU. Follow-up task 68: scripts/test fails when started from an inherited luv dev-shell environment. scripts/test passes (23/0, with LUV_DEV_SHELL unset).', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

## What to check
- Every gap in `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Gaps and workarounds" has its workaround named in `docs/architecture.md` (with the file that holds it in "Files in load order") and, where it would serve other luv programs, a line in `docs/luv-wishlist.md`; every wishlist line rests on a finding in `docs/luv-capabilities.md`.
- The luv systems, rendering paths and choices the architecture relies on (reversed-Z infinite far projection, camera-relative `single-float` rendering, Slug text, the overlay''s dot-matrix labels, render targets for the grapple camera, `sdl3-image`, the audio sink, no Ghostty per `decision 36`) are ones `docs/luv-capabilities.md` found working, or are marked as built in this repo. Where a claim is doubtful, check it in `../luv` (read-only) or by running a luv program, not only by reading.
- The performance budgets in `docs/design.md` "Performance target" and `docs/architecture.md` ("Integrator", "Trajectory prediction", the play-through''s run time) agree with the measurements in `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Performance".

## Done when
- Gaps, workarounds, wishlist and architecture point at each other without holes, and the budgets agree with the measurements; the done note lists what was checked and changed.', '2026-10-14T21:19:46Z', '2026-10-14T21:28:46Z', 60, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (64, 12, 'Check that every feature is assigned and the milestones agree with the scope', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. Checked: every feature named in design.md''s Ship, Flight, Cockpit and Places sections against ''Feature list''; architecture ''Files in load order'' milestones per file against the rows; ''Scripts by milestone'' against the Done when rows; pm milestone show 2-6 Outcome and Done when against the must rows. Changed: decision 62: Scope: must rows for each milestone''s Outcome (partly supersedes decision 42 and decision 32): scenery ships must in 3 (milestone 5''s ''other ships at their work''), real asteroids on the map must in 4 (milestone 4''s belt), the autopilot''s transfers to asteroids and planets cut (no such destination; mid-course corrections kept); new design section ''Title screen and menus'' for the milestone 6 rows that had none; rows added or extended: overlay message line and autopilot panel (3), Moon crash (2), planets'' crash spheres (4), the Moon''s orbit and map focus (4), in-game runs with screenshots per milestone 3/4/5 Done when, name plate with the cockpit (3) and registration on the hull (2); the stale row ''story''s start date, ship name and place names'' (5) removed (they arrive in 2 and 3); ''Each milestone against…'' updated. architecture.md: file milestones for autopilot, places, impostors, meshes (3: places and ships), ribbons, overlay, cockpit, camera, input (gamepad 6 could), audio (6 should). Follow-up: task 69: Architecture: the Sun-death flight script of milestone 4 (the must row has no script in ''Scripts by milestone''). No human decision needed.', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

