INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (92, 13, 'math.lisp: vectors, quaternions, the single-float boundary', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/math.lisp, tests/math.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md. vec3/quat/mat3 per decision 65: Vectors and quaternions in math.lisp, with in-place ! twins, quat-from-mat3 (Shepperd) behind quat-from-basis, relative-single with out and index. The round-trip bound is loosened from 1e-15 to 2e-15: the measured worst case is 1.2e-15 per component (~5 ulp over two rotations); the reason is in the test''s comment and in docs/architecture.md ''Frame transforms''. The ./sly eval check gives #(0.995 0 -0.0998).', 'Piece 1 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: write `src/math.lisp` and `tests/math.lisp` as the plan''s section "1. `math.lisp`" lists them (`decision 65: Vectors and quaternions in math.lisp`).

- Files: `src/math.lisp`, `tests/math.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `math` right after `package`, before `shaders`; the test after `tests/package.lisp`); `docs/architecture.md` "Frame transforms" (quaternion tests now in `tests/math.lisp`) and "Files in load order" (`math.lisp` names `decision 65`''s layout); `AGENTS.md` "Layout": the `src/` bullet becomes the skeleton plus the simulation files built so far, citing "Files in load order".
- Contents: vec3 and quaternion `(simple-array double-float …)` with constructors, the vec3 operations and their in-place `!` twins, mat3 row-major operations including the symmetric inverse and `mat3-from-quat`, quaternion product, conjugate, normalise, `quat-rotate`, `quat-from-axis-angle`, `quat-slerp`, `quat-derivative` (ω in body axes), `quat-from-basis`; `relative-single`.
- Tests: the plan''s list (round trip within 1e-15 from a fixed seed list, FRD signs for pitch/yaw/roll, slerp at 0, ½, 1, `relative-single` 1.25 exactly, symmetric inverse within 1e-15).

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(quat-rotate (quat-from-axis-angle (vec3 0 1 0) 0.1d0) (vec3 1 0 0))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` gives a vector with negative z.', '2026-10-14T22:55:05Z', '2026-10-14T23:09:48Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (93, 13, 'units.lisp: constants, calendar, display conversions', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/units.lisp, tests/units.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md (''Time'', ''Files in load order'', ''Rails, orbits and frames'' Units line), AGENTS.md Layout. Deviation from the plan: J2000.0 is 11:58:50.816 in the game''s UTC, not 11:58:55.816, since decision 14 fixes TT - UTC at 69.184 s for every date (recorded as a consequence of decision 14). The mu digits are taken from docs/architecture.md; task 95 checks them against DE440.', 'Piece 2 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: write `src/units.lisp` and `tests/units.lisp` as the plan''s section "2. `units.lisp`" lists them (`decision 14: Units and time epoch`, `decision 66: Calendar dates on the 1/64 s grid`).

- Files: `src/units.lisp`, `tests/units.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems, after `math`); `docs/architecture.md` "Time" (grid rounding and `(start-t)`); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" `src/` bullet kept true.
- Contents: every constant of the plan''s list with its source in a comment beside it (μ of Sun, Earth, Moon from DE440; IAU radii; J2; g₀; ε; AU; TT − UTC; day, Julian century; `+fine-step+` = 1/64 s); calendar `utc->t` (Fliegel–Van Flandern, integer days and seconds apart), `utc->grid-t`, `t->utc`, `*start-date*` (2040 1 1 0 0 0), `start-t`, `t->ut1-days`, `t->julian-centuries`; display conversions (km, km/s, degrees, duration fields, `format-utc`).
- Tests: the plan''s list (J2000.0 within 1e-9 s of 0, round trips, `(start-t)` on the grid and within 1/128 s, `format-utc` of the start and a day later, start inside 1800–2050, degree/radian round trip).
- Piece 4 (`bodies.lisp` ephemerides) checks the μ digits against Park et al. 2021 with web access; write them here from `docs/architecture.md` "Units".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; every constant in `units.lisp` cites a source.', '2026-10-14T22:55:05Z', '2026-10-14T23:11:39Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (94, 13, 'bodies.lisp part one: bodies, rotations, body-fixed frames', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/bodies.lisp, tests/bodies.lisp (new), luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md (Files in load order), AGENTS.md (Layout). Body list with Laplace spheres (Earth 9.246e8 m from the EMB a = 1.00000261 AU of Standish Table 1, Moon 6.618e7 m from a = 384,399 km); Earth Rotation Angle with whole UT1 days dropped before the multiply; Moon and Sun IAU WGCCRE 2015 leading terms; body-fixed-matrix takes a key or a body. scripts/test passes (557).', 'Piece 3 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: start `src/bodies.lisp` and `tests/bodies.lisp` as the plan''s section "3. `bodies.lisp`, part one" lists them. Needs pieces 1 and 2 (`math.lisp`, `units.lisp`).

- Files: `src/bodies.lisp`, `tests/bodies.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems, after `units`); `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" kept true; `AGENTS.md` "Layout" `src/` bullet kept true.
- Contents: the `body` struct and a fixed list `:sun`, `:earth`, `:moon` (μ, radius, crash radius per `decision 34: How death works`, parent, parent orbit''s mean semi-major axis, Laplace sphere, Earth''s J2), `(body key)`; Earth Rotation Angle with the integer part of D_U kept apart; the Moon''s IAU WGCCRE 2015 leading-term rotation (no periodic terms); `body-fixed-matrix`, `latitude-longitude`, `body-texture-uv` ("Frames").
- Tests ("Frame transforms"): θ at J2000.0 and its rate within 1e-12 rev; texture (u, v) of body-fixed x and the north pole; longitude 90.246° W after 6 UT1 hours within 1e-9°; Laplace spheres within 1 % of ~9.25×10^8 m and ~6.6×10^7 m. The Moon''s synchronous rotation test is piece 4''s.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes.', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:13:44Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (95, 13, 'bodies.lisp part two: ephemerides and the Hermite cache', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/bodies.lisp, tests/bodies.lisp, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md. μ and radii checked against gm_de440.tpc (Park et al. 2021) and IAU 2015: units.lisp unchanged. Cached body-state-into ~48 ns (Sun from Earth), ~31 ns (Moon). Deviations recorded in decision 89: Ephemeris test bounds and the start Sun''s RA (Moon Hermite bound 3 cm, 2.5 cm measured; Earth/EMB identity 1e-4 m; start Sun RA 280.5° ICRF, design.md fixed).', 'Piece 4 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: the ephemerides and their cache in `src/bodies.lisp`, as the plan''s section "4. `bodies.lisp`, part two" lists them (`decision 18: Ephemerides`, `decision 67: Ephemeris cache and the Moon''s series frame`). Needs piece 3 (the `body` list and rotations). Web access: for the JPL Horizons vectors and the DE440 digits.

- Files: `src/bodies.lisp`, `tests/bodies.lisp`; `src/units.lisp` if a constant differs from its source; `docs/architecture.md` "Ephemerides" (the two cached quantities, the global cache and the precession of `decision 67`, replacing "kept in a small table in the `game` object"; the measured cost of a cached `body-state-into`) and "Ephemeris spot checks" (Mars and Jupiter wait for milestone 4).
- Models: Sun at the origin; the EMB from Standish Table 1 (EMB row), Kepler by Newton to 1e-14 rad, analytic velocity, ecliptic → ICRF by ε; the Moon from Meeus ch. 47 (tables 47.A and 47.B in full, no nutation), precessed by Meeus eq. 21.5, velocity by ±60 s central difference; Earth = EMB − μ_Moon/(μ_Earth + μ_Moon) × Moon.
- Cache: nodes every 4,096 s for the EMB and the geocentric Moon, each a pure function of its index; cubic Hermite; direct-mapped, 64 slots per quantity.
- API: `body-state` → `(values r v)`, `body-state-into`, origins `:sun`, `:earth`, `:moon`; `body-state-series` bypasses the cache.
- Tests ("Ephemeris spot checks"): Horizons vectors committed as constants with their query in a comment (EMB from the Sun, target 3 centre 500@10; Moon from Earth, target 301 centre 500@399; 2026-01-01, 2040-01-01, 2049-06-01 00:00 TDB; bounds as in the plan); the Sun from Earth at the start near RA 281°, Dec −23° within 0.5°; Hermite vs series within 2 cm over 200 fixed times in 2040; node bit-identical computed first or after 100 others; the Earth/EMB/Moon identities within 1e-6 m and 1e-4 m; the Moon''s prime meridian within 10° of Earth at the three dates.
- Also: check μ of Sun, Earth, Moon digit by digit against Park et al. 2021 and the IAU radii; fix `units.lisp` and say so in the done note if one differs.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes, every Horizons query is reproducible from its comment, and the cost of a cached `body-state-into` (a few hundred ns at most) is measured and written in "Ephemerides".', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:21:10Z', 82, 1);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (96, 13, 'orbits.lisp: ellipses, Kepler, apsides, radius crossings', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/orbits.lisp, tests/orbits.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md (Rails, Kepler round trip, Files in load order), AGENTS.md. The semi-latus rectum is orbit-semi-latus (orbit-p is the struct predicate). Hyperbolic states signal a PLACEHOLDER(97) error. The part''s orbit tests take ~0.04 s.', 'Piece 5 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: write `src/orbits.lisp` and `tests/orbits.lisp` for ellipses as the plan''s section "5. `orbits.lisp`" lists them (`decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`). Needs pieces 1–4 (the lighting test needs the ephemerides).

- Files: `src/orbits.lisp`, `tests/orbits.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems, after `bodies`); `docs/architecture.md` "Rails" (names the `orbit` struct) and "Kepler round trip" (hyperbolic cases are piece 6''s); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" `src/` bullet kept true.
- Contents: the `orbit` struct; `state->orbit`, `orbit-state` (argument of latitude and true longitude where ω or Ω are conventional); elliptic Kepler by Newton from E₀ = M + e sin M (π for e > 0.8) to 1e-15 relative; a, p, n, period, apsis radii, `orbit-energy`, `orbit-next-apsis`, `orbit-radius-crossings` in closed form (nil outside [q, Q]); `orbit-j2-rates`.
- Tests ("Kepler round trip"): the plan''s list: round trips within 1e-9 for circular equatorial, the polar start orbit of `decision 38: Start orbit: polar`, i = 150°, e = 0.5, e = 0.9 at eight anomalies, and orbit → state → orbit; propagation there and back; Kepler residual below 1e-14 up to e = 0.99; start orbit period 92.6 min and 7,669 m/s; 800 × 90 km apsides; the K-17 crossing 2,603.07 s after apogee at −14.35° (within 0.01 s, 0.01°) and none for periapsis 1 m above; J2 Ω̇ ≈ −5.0°/day at 400 km 51.6° and |Ω̇| < 1e-15 rad/s at 90°; the start''s β −10° and the ship 25° from the Sun within 1°.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(orbit-period (state->orbit …))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` works on a hand-made state.', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:24:58Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (97, 13, 'orbits.lisp: hyperbolas and orbit-points', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/orbits.lisp (hyperbolas: state<->orbit, make-hyperbolic-orbit, hyperbolic Kepler, perifocal forms, radius crossings for r >= q, the |e-1| < 1e-6 display rule; orbit-points for both conics), tests/orbits.lisp (7 hyperbola/orbit-points tests), docs/architecture.md ''Hyperbolic rails'' and its tests. scripts/test passes (1177); the plan''s math/units/bodies/orbits tests take 0.185 s together. The Kepler residual test uses e = 1.5 and 3 only: at e = 1.0046 the plain form exceeds 1e-14 relative for small |M|, which milestone 4''s near-parabolic series fixes.', 'Piece 6 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: extend `src/orbits.lisp` to e > 1 and add `orbit-points`, as the plan''s section "6. `orbits.lisp`: hyperbolas" lists them (`decision 46: Rails across spheres, hyperbolas and re-entry`, `decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`). Needs piece 5.

