- Tests: round trips for e = 1.5 and 3 at H = 0, ±0.5, ±2 within 1e-9; propagation there and back; Kepler residual below 1e-14 for |M| from 1e-6 to 1e3; periapsis speed √(v∞² + 2μ/q) within 1e-12; ellipse `orbit-points` within 1e-6 m of the conic''s radius.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes and the whole plan''s tests (`tests/math`, `units`, `bodies`, `orbits`) run in under 0.5 s together.', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:27:32Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (98, 14, 'physics.lisp: ship state, gravity models, the step rule', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/physics.lisp, tests/physics.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md. ship-state (deep copy-ship-state, make-ship-state copies its inputs), gravity-into! (:none/:point/:j2/:full, optional central body, Earth only) with third-body-add!, coarse-step (inline; halves down from the 16,384 s clamp, so exact powers of two). Measured, compiled, warm cache: :point 2 ns, :j2 5 ns, :full 80 ns, coarse-step ~90 ns, all consing nothing (tested). Deviations from the plan''s test list, each explained in the test''s comment: at r = R the rule gives 2 s, not 1/64 s (the lower clamp needs d < ~185 km), so the clamp is tested at 100 km and at 0; the Moon''s tidal check uses 3 r/d (~5.5 %) since the next order is 1.5 r/d ~2.7 % at 7,000 km. ./sly eval of (coarse-step (vec3 6778136.6d0 0 0) 0d0 nil) gives 2.0d0; scripts/test passes (1227).', 'Piece 1 of `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer`: write `src/physics.lisp` and `tests/physics.lisp` as the plan''s section "1. `physics.lisp`: ship state, gravity, the step rule" lists them (`decision 69: Ship state, step rule and kinematic attitude in physics.lisp`, `decision 17: Gravity model`). Needs `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits` done (math, units, `body-state-into`).

- Files: `src/physics.lisp`, `tests/physics.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `physics` after `orbits`, before `shaders`; the test after `tests/orbits.lisp`); `docs/architecture.md` "Drift bounds" (the step rule is `physics.lisp`''s, called by the clock) and "Files in load order" (`physics.lisp` also holds the step rule); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" `src/` bullet kept true.
- Contents: `ship-state` struct (r, v, q body → inertial, w body rad/s, m-p, dv) with a deep `copy-ship-state`, `equalp` bit for bit, a constructor from (r, v, q, w, m-p); `(gravity-into! a r t model)` for `:none`, `:point`, `:j2` (closed form, pole along ICRF z), `:full` (`:j2` plus Sun and Moon with indirect terms from `body-state-into … :earth`), an `ecase` on the central body (Earth only); `(coarse-step r t thrusting)`: η = 1/256 × min √(d³/μ) over Earth, Moon, Sun, down to a power of two, clamped to [1/64 s, 16,384 s], ≤ 1 s when thrusting. Typed double-float, inline where hot, consing nothing; η and the clamps `defparameter`s citing "Integrator".
- Tests: the plan''s list: J2 radial at the equator and over the pole within 1e-14 relative, no tangential component, z → −z symmetry; Moon and Sun terms at three points against rationals within 1e-9, the tidal 2 μ r / d³ within 2 %; step rule 2 s at 400 km, 512 s at 2×10⁸ m, 1 s when thrusting, 1/64 s at r = R, 16,384 s at the upper clamp, all powers of two.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(coarse-step (vec3 6778136.6d0 0 0) 0d0 nil)'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` gives 2.0d0.', '2026-10-14T22:56:14Z', '2026-10-14T23:32:52Z', 83, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (99, 14, 'physics.lisp: the RK4 step, exhaustion, kinematic attitude and the drift tests', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/physics.lisp (rk4-step!: RK4 on r, v, q, ω, m_p, exhaustion scaling, odometer, kinematic attitude; coarse-step skips Moon/Sun reads that cannot set the step, results unchanged), tests/physics.lisp (drift table with fine rows shortened to 5 circular and 1 e=0.5 orbits, rotation, exhaustion, kinematic, zero consing, determinism; 1.9 s), docs/architecture.md (Integrator: exhaustion, odometer, kinematic step, measured cost; Drift bounds: measured values). decision 90 recorded; follow-up task 139.', 'Piece 2 of `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer`: add `rk4-step!` to `src/physics.lisp` and the drift tests to `tests/physics.lisp` as the plan''s section "2. `physics.lisp`: the RK4 step and the drift tests" lists them (`decision 69: Ship state, step rule and kinematic attitude in physics.lisp`, `decision 16: Integrator and simulation clock`, `decision 21: Physics test bounds and flight scripts`). Needs piece 1 (the previous task of this plan).

- Files: `src/physics.lisp`, `tests/physics.lisp`; `docs/architecture.md` "Integrator" (the exhaustion scaling of all thrusters, the odometer, the kinematic step; the cost line with measured ns per step for `:point`, `:full`, with and without attitude, replacing the stand-in measurement).
- Contents: `(rk4-step! state h t model force-body torque-body mdot inertia inertia-inverse &optional attitude-fn)` (the mass passed in or folded into the inputs, your choice, consing nothing): classical RK4 on r, v, q, ω, m_p; Euler''s equations with the full tensor; q renormalised after the step; odometer |F|/ṁ ln(m₀/m₁) or |F| h / m. Exhaustion: when ṁ h > m_p, force, torque and ṁ scaled by m_p / (ṁ h) so m_p ends at 0.0d0 exactly; at m_p = 0 all zero (no death, `decision 34: How death works`). Kinematic attitude: with `attitude-fn` (t, r, v → quat and ω_t inertial) q comes from it at each stage, torque ignored, q and ω (body) set from it at t + h.
- Tests ("Drift bounds"): the plan''s table (two-body, periapsis 6,778 km, i 51.6°, Ω 30°, ω 40°, attitude integrated alongside with I = diag(1, 2, 3)×10⁴): fine step circular 10 orbits and e = 0.5 2 orbits (< 1e-11, 0.05 m); coarse circular 1,000 orbits (1e-10, 5 m), e = 0.5 1,000 orbits (1e-9, 100 m), e = 0.9 200 orbits (ΔE/E 1e-8, ΔL/L 1e-9, 5 km), against `orbit-state` at whole periods. If they don''t fit in ~2 s, shorten the fine rows (5 circular, 1 at e = 0.5, bounds unchanged) and say so in the comment. Torque-free rotation (diagonal and rotated tensor, 1,000 s at 1/64 s: energy and |I ω| inertial within 1e-9, |q| within 1e-12); exhaustion (ṁ h = 2 m_p → 0.0d0 exactly, Δv by the rocket equation within 1e-12); kinematic hold of x along v within 1e-12 rad after 100 coarse steps; 10,000 `:full` steps cons < 1 KB; two identical runs `equalp`.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes inside the plan''s budget; the measured cost is in `docs/architecture.md` "Integrator".', '2026-10-14T22:56:14Z', '2026-10-14T23:40:46Z', 83, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (100, 14, 'ship.lisp: the Mule''s parts, mass properties, engine and RCS layout', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/ship.lisp, tests/ship.lisp (new); luv-in-space.asd, src/math.lisp (mat3-inverse-symmetric!), docs/design.md Parts (cabling 199 kg) and Inertia (shapes), docs/architecture.md Files in load order, AGENTS.md Layout. Figures from the code: wet CoM (10.341, 0, -0.218), dry I_xx 5.16e4 (4.2 % over the table, as decision 71 measured), trim 1.56/0.86/-2.94 deg, y/z translation 1266/1390.5 N, dv 6,649.8 m/s. The tanks empty at 28,000 / mdot = 1,212.98 s (plan 14''s 1,213.2 was a slip; the test uses the computed time). scripts/test passes.', 'Piece 3 of `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer`: write `src/ship.lisp` and `tests/ship.lisp` as the plan''s section "3. `ship.lisp`" lists them (`decision 71: The Mule''s mass model in ship.lisp`, `decision 22: The player''s ship and its propulsion`, `docs/design.md` "The ship(s)"). Needs pieces 1–2 (the thrust tests run `rk4-step!`).

- Files: `src/ship.lisp`, `tests/ship.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `ship` after `physics`; the test after `tests/physics.lisp`); `docs/design.md` "Parts" (cabling and plumbing 199 kg, the dry sum then 7,961 kg) and "Inertia" (one line naming the shapes `ship.lisp` uses); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" and `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" kept true.
- Contents: the "Parts" table as data with each row citing it (shapes and sizes of `decision 71`); precomputed dry mass, first and second moments about R; `(ship-mass-properties m-p &optional load)` into preallocated outputs: mass, CoM, full tensor about the CoM by the parallel-axis rule, its inverse; propellant as two solid cylinders per "Inertia" (MR 5.5); engine F 101,800 N, Isp 449.7 s, `ship-engine-force`, `ship-engine-mdot` (throttle 0 or 0.1–1.0), `(ship-trim-angle m-p)` with the gimbal at (0, 0, −0.5); the 24 RCS thrusters as data (eight blocks at x 0.5 and 14.5, y, z ±1.8; 445 N, Isp 360 s), `(rcs-matrix! b com)` (6×24), the couples and `(rcs-translation-capability axis com)` of `decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer`; `(ship-dv-remaining m-p)`. `load` stays nil in milestone 2 (no PLACEHOLDER needed).
- Tests: the plan''s list: dry 7,961 and wet 35,961 kg exactly; CoM rows Wet, Half, Dry of "Inertia" within 0.01 m, I diagonal within 5 %, I_xz within 10 %, principal tilt within 1°, tensor symmetric, positive definite, × inverse = 𝟙 within 1e-12; single box and two point masses in closed form; trim wet 1.6°, half 0.9°, dry −3.0° within 0.1°; couples 12,460 and 3,204 N m, opposed pairs summing to zero, translation ±x 1,780 N, ±y/±z 1,266 N wet and 1,391 N dry within 1 N; Δv at 28,000 kg 6,650 m/s within 1 m/s; a 100 s field-free burn (`:none`) matches the rocket equation within 1e-9 and the odometer within 1e-12; a 1,300 s burn empties the tanks to 0.0d0 exactly in the step containing 1,213.2 s and stays at 7,961 kg.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(ship-mass-properties 28000d0)'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` returns 35,961 kg and CoM (10.34, 0, −0.22).', '2026-10-14T22:56:14Z', '2026-10-14T23:47:55Z', 83, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (101, 14, 'controls.lisp: control state, the RCS mixer, direct mode, translation and flight-step!', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/controls.lisp, tests/controls.lisp, src/ship.lisp (make-mass-properties inline for the stack), luv-in-space.asd, AGENTS.md, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. scripts/test passes (controls tests ~0.3 s). Mixer 0.4-10 us per call, ≤23 of 96 solves. Done-when eval: 64 direct-pitch steps from the start give dω_y = 0.0275545 rad/s; vs 12,460/I_yy(start) 5e-6 relative (the 0.5 kg of RCS propellant burned moves I_yy), vs Σ 12,460 h / I_yy(each step) within 1e-6 (tested). Deviations from plan 14, in test comments and decision 70''s consequences: w = 1e5 not 1e6; 10 kN +y gives 1,592 N (exact closed form), not 1,266; at the wet CoM pure +x also fires a small pitch-trim couple; burned propellant checked within 1e-9 kg (m_p rounding), not 1e-12 relative; ''dry'' taps with 1 kg left.', 'Piece 4 of `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer`: write `src/controls.lisp` and `tests/controls.lisp` as the plan''s section "4. `controls.lisp`, part one" lists them (`decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer`, `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`, `docs/design.md` "Controls" and "Control modes"). Needs pieces 1–3.

- Files: `src/controls.lisp`, `tests/controls.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `controls` after `ship`, before `shaders`; the test after `tests/ship.lisp`); `docs/design.md` "RCS forces, torques and accelerations" (the mixer runs per fine step, not per frame); `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`controls.lisp` also holds the flight computer, the mixer and `flight-step!`) and "Integrator" (the mixer''s measured cost per call); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" kept true.
- Contents: the `controls` struct (throttle lever, rotation keys per pitch/yaw/roll, translation keys per body axis, fine flag, attitude mode, hold kind, inertial target quat, roll offset, settled flag, last duty cycles), deep `copy-controls`, `equalp` bit for bit, `(new-controls)` = rate damping with a prograde hold, throttle off (`decision 38: Start orbit: polar`); commands `controls-set-throttle` (below 0.1 is 0), `controls-throttle-full`, `controls-throttle-cut`, `controls-set-rotation-key`, `controls-set-translation-key`, `controls-toggle-fine`; `(rcs-mix! u b tau-c f-c)`: weighted Stark–Parker BVLS with Householder QR, fixed iteration limit and column order, duties in [0, 1], zero command → zeros, consing nothing; direct mode (full couple per held key, ×0.1 fine) and translation (`rcs-translation-capability`, ×0.1 fine) in one mix; `(flight-step! state controls h t model &optional attitude-fn)`: mass properties, flight computer (closed loops come in piece 5; until then rate damping and holds command zero torque, marked `PLACEHOLDER(102)`), mixer, engine plus RCS force, torque and ṁ, `rk4-step!`; with `attitude-fn` engine only.
- Tests: the plan''s list: 50 torques within 90 % of the couples at wet, half and dry CoM met within 1e-6 × couple, duties in [0, 1], zero → zeros; pure +x force uses only the four aft axial nozzles at 1,780 N with zero torque; 10 kN +y with zero torque gives ~1,266 N (2 %) wet; one fine step of direct pitch changes ω by I⁻¹ τ h within 1e-9 (0.027°/s wet, 0.060 dry per 1/60 s); one fine +x step 0.77 mm/s wet within 1 %; one second of all-RCS burns Σ u_i 445 / (360 g₀) within 1e-12, one shared pool. Measure the mixer per call; above a few tens of µs record the profile in "Integrator" and add a follow-up task.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; a `./sly eval` of 64 `flight-step!`s in direct mode with pitch held from the start state shows ω_y = 12,460 N m / I_yy × 1 s within 1e-6 relative (about 0.028 rad/s wet).', '2026-10-14T22:56:14Z', '2026-10-15T00:01:55Z', 83, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (102, 14, 'controls.lisp: rate damping, holds 1–6 and R, fine control, kinematic holds', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/controls.lisp (rate damping, hold-attitude, slew and settle law, controls-set-hold, controls-toggle-rate-damping, controls-inertial-hold, controls-attitude-fn; PLACEHOLDER(102) gone), src/math.lisp (non-consing quat-from-basis!, quat-from-mat3!), tests/controls.lisp (rate damping, holds, roll key, key rules, kinematic burn, determinism, allocation), docs/design.md ''Control modes'', docs/architecture.md ''Testing'' -> ''Controls'' and the Integrator cost line. scripts/test passes (2321). Measured: rate damping 95 % at 3.23 s wet, 1.89 s dry; holds settle ~25 s wet and dry, R after a 2 deg/s tumble 6.6 s; kinematic burn 6e-9 in dv, 3 mm in apoapsis. tests/physics.lisp, tests/ship.lisp and tests/controls.lisp together run in 2.68 s (controls'' new tests 0.34 s).', 'Piece 5 of `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer`: add the closed loops to `src/controls.lisp` and their tests to `tests/controls.lisp` as the plan''s section "5. `controls.lisp`, part two" lists them (`decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer`, `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`, `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering` for what part 3 expects of `controls-attitude-fn` and `controls-inertial-hold`). Needs piece 4.

- Files: `src/controls.lisp`, `tests/controls.lisp`; `docs/design.md` "Control modes" (one bullet: the slew law, the settle hysteresis, the roll rule of `decision 70`); `docs/architecture.md` "Testing" (a "Controls" bullet list for `tests/controls.lisp` with the bounds below, beside "Drift bounds").
- Contents: rate damping τ = I (ω_c − ω) / 0.5 s + ω × I ω, clamped per axis to the couple (×0.1 fine), ω_c 5°/s (0.5°/s fine) on held axes; `(hold-attitude kind r v roll-offset)` → target quat and frame rate for `:prograde` … `:radial-in` with the default roll (cab −z radial out; towards normal for the radial holds), `:inertial` from the stored quat; the slew law (√(2 × 0.8 α |φ|), 0.5/s linear tail, 5°/s cap, feed-forward of ω_t, 80 % couple) and the settled hysteresis (0.1°/0.02°/s in, 0.2°/0.05°/s out); commands `controls-set-hold` (same hold again → rate damping), `controls-toggle-rate-damping` (T), `controls-inertial-hold` (R); a pitch or yaw key releases a hold, a roll key turns the roll offset at the rate-damping rate; `(controls-attitude-fn controls)` for `rk4-step!`''s kinematic mode. Tunables `defparameter`s citing "Control modes".
- Tests: the plan''s list: rate damping to 95 % of 5°/s within 3.5 s wet and 2.0 s dry, released |ω| < 0.02°/s within 6 s wet, fine to 0.5°/s overshooting at most 1 %; from 90° off prograde in the 400 km polar orbit (`:full`) the prograde hold settles within 40 s wet and 35 s dry (measured times in the comment), then < 0.1° and < 0.02°/s for 120 s; retrograde, normal, anti-normal, radial out and in, and R after a 2°/s tumble settle within 40 s; default roll within 0.1°; a roll key held 2 s turns 10° within 0.5° and the hold keeps it; key rules (1 twice → rate damping, W releases, T releases or toggles direct); the 60 s kinematic prograde burn at the coarse step (1 s cap) matches the fine-step hold-flown burn within 1e-6 in Δv and 1 m in apoapsis radius; 120 s of a scripted key list run twice gives `equalp` states and controls.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; the plan''s tests together (`tests/physics.lisp`, `tests/ship.lisp`, `tests/controls.lisp`) run under 3 s, measured and stated in the done note.', '2026-10-14T22:56:14Z', '2026-10-15T00:09:58Z', 83, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (103, 15, 'clock.lisp: the sim state, the start state, sim-step! and checkpoints', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/clock.lisp, tests/clock.lisp (new; 7 tests, ~0.25 s together), luv-in-space.asd, src/physics.lisp (ship-state-assign!), src/controls.lisp (controls-assign!), docs/architecture.md (The clock, Checkpoints, Files in load order), AGENTS.md (Layout). sim-step! is an inline wrapper over sim-step-ticks!, which returns h in 1/64 s ticks so a full call boxes nothing; the kinematic attitude reads the controls through a special (*hold-controls*) instead of a controls-attitude-fn closure per step, which would cons. Crash test call site PLACEHOLDER(104), checkpoint-safe-p impact PLACEHOLDER(105). Done check: the ./sly eval gives (start-t) + 1. Follow-up task 140: a once-seen 32 KB flake in rk4-cons-nothing-and-deterministic.', 'Piece 1 of `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`: write `src/clock.lisp` (part one) and `tests/clock.lisp` as the plan''s section "1. `clock.lisp`, part one" lists them (`decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 38: Start orbit: polar`, `decision 66: Calendar dates on the 1/64 s grid`, `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering` for the inertial hold on entering a coarse step). Needs `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits` and `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer` done.

- Files: `src/clock.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `clock` after `controls`, before `shaders`; `tests/clock` after `tests/controls`); `docs/architecture.md` "Checkpoints" (milestone 2''s `sim` fields), "The clock" (`sim-step!` as the one step, landing on `until` and the cut-off rule), "Files in load order" (`clock.lisp` also holds the start state); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" (`src/` bullet) kept true.
- Contents: the `sim` struct (`t`, `body`, `ship`, `controls`, `model`, `cutoff`, `loss`, `steps`), deep `copy-sim`, `sim-assign!` consing nothing; `(new-game-sim)` (a = 6,778,136.6 m, e 0, i 90°, Ω 270°, u 0 at `(start-t)` through `orbit-state`; q, ω from `hold-attitude :prograde`; m_p 28,000 kg; `(new-controls)`); `(sim-step! sim level &key until)`: fine step at ×1/×4, `coarse-step` with `controls-attitude-fn` above (inertial hold engaged first when no hold), landing on `until` and on the Δv cut-off (fine: the step after crossing; coarse: the engine-only closed form rounded up to the grid), `flight-step!` with `(sim-model sim)`, `t += h`, `steps += 1`, returns h; nil for a sim with a `loss`. Leave a call site for piece 2''s crash test (`PLACEHOLDER(104)` until it lands). `take-checkpoint`, `restore-checkpoint!`, `checkpoint-safe-p` (throttle off, no loss; piece 3 adds the impact). Tunables as `defparameter`s citing their decisions; no wall clock, no HAL/SDL/`*game*`.
- Tests (the plan''s list): start state elements, attitude and |ω| = n; 1,000 mixed steps stay on the 1/64 s grid and land on every `until`; 25 m/s cut-off at ×1 and ×100 (on the grid, Δv in [25, 25 + one fine step''s Δv), cut times within 1/64 s); checkpoint restore + 2,000 mixed steps `equalp`; the polar node with `:j2` over 7 days at ×1,000 (Ω within 1e-6° of 270°, |Ω̇| < 1e-15 rad/s); 10,000 `sim-step!`s cons < 1 KB.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(let ((s (new-game-sim))) (dotimes (i 64) (sim-step! s 1)) (sim-t s))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` gives `(start-t)` + 1.', '2026-10-14T22:56:45Z', '2026-10-15T00:19:56Z', 84, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (104, 15, 'hazards.lisp: the swept crash test against Earth and the Moon, and death', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/hazards.lisp, tests/hazards.lisp, src/clock.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md. crash-test! takes (sim r0 v0 q0 ticks) (q0 for the slerp; h as fixnum ticks and t0 from sim-t so nothing is boxed); the loss slot is loss-time. Measured: crash-test! ~33 ns per step in LEO (fine and coarse); hazards tests together ~0.13 s. The grazing fine run takes the fine step within 300 s of each periapsis, coarse between (full fine orbits ~1 s). Moon 1 km graze shot in the test: Earth''s tide moves the two-body aim 1.1 km (the first shot crosses and is caught).', 'Piece 2 of `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`: write `src/hazards.lisp` and `tests/hazards.lisp` as the plan''s section "2. `hazards.lisp`" lists them (`decision 74: Crash test on the step''s Hermite and the death state`, `decision 34: How death works`, `docs/architecture.md` "Collisions and the Sun", `docs/design.md` "Dying and what follows"). Needs `task 103: clock.lisp: the sim state, the start state, sim-step! and checkpoints`.

- Files: `src/hazards.lisp`, `tests/hazards.lisp` (new); `src/clock.lisp` (`sim-step!` keeps the step''s start r, v, t in a preallocated buffer and calls `crash-test!` after `flight-step!`, replacing `PLACEHOLDER(104)`); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `hazards` after `clock`; `tests/hazards` after `tests/clock`); `docs/architecture.md` "Collisions and the Sun" (the exact sag bound, the death state), "Testing" → "Crash detection" (the Moon case as built), "Integrator" (the crash test''s measured cost per step); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" kept true.
- Contents: `(crash-test! sim r0 v0 t0)` against Earth (R + 100 km) and the Moon (R, geocentric state from `body-state` at both ends): relative cubic Hermite p(s), chord closest approach minus max(|p''''(0)|, |p''''(1)|)/8 against R_c; only then Newton on d|p|²/ds, first crossing by bracketed Newton to 1e-9 in s; the earliest crossing over both bodies wins. Death: a `loss` struct (cause `:crash`, body, `t`, speed relative to the body, latitude, longitude via `latitude-longitude`), the ship at the crossing''s Hermite state (attitude slerped, ω and m_p of the step''s end), `t` the impact time; `(sim-lost-p sim)`. Conses nothing.
- Tests (the plan''s list): radial free fall from 1,000 km at ×1 and ×1,000 within 1e-3 s of the closed form; periapsis 50 km below R_c at the coarse step (time within 1e-2 s of `orbit-radius-crossings`, point within 0.01°, speed within 1e-3 m/s of vis-viva); grazing 1 m above, two orbits fine and coarse: no impact; the Moon at 3 km/s with impact parameter 0.9 R_☾ caught (|p| = R_☾ within 1e-3 m), a hyperbola 1 km above R_☾ not; after death `sim-step!` returns nil and the sim is unchanged, a restored checkpoint flies to the same impact bit for bit.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; the cost per step when nothing is near is measured (a few tens of ns) and in "Integrator".', '2026-10-14T22:57:02Z', '2026-10-15T00:27:53Z', 84, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (105, 15, 'prediction.lisp: the milestone-2 events by sim-step! on a copy', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/prediction.lisp, tests/prediction.lisp, src/clock.lisp (checkpoint-safe-p: no impact predicted, optional clock prediction), luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md (''Trajectory prediction'' milestone-2 form, ''Steps'' event waits, load order, Checkpoints), AGENTS.md Layout. scripts/test passes; the prediction tests take ~0.39 s together. Done-when check: ./sly eval of prediction-run! after an instantaneous 100 m/s retrograde burn from the start state predicts an impact and no apsides. That is correct: the osculating periapsis is 57.6 km, below the 100 km crash radius (decision 87''s deorbit uses 102.3 m/s for 50 km). With 50 m/s it lists the apoapsis and the periapsis and no impact.', 'Piece 3 of `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`: write `src/prediction.lisp` and `tests/prediction.lisp` as the plan''s section "3. `prediction.lisp`" lists them (`decision 75: Prediction in milestone 2: the step function on a copy`, `decision 20: Trajectory prediction on the frame thread`, `decision 21: Physics test bounds and flight scripts`). Needs `task 104: hazards.lisp: the swept crash test against Earth and the Moon, and death`.

- Files: `src/prediction.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp` (new); `src/clock.lisp` (`checkpoint-safe-p` adds "no impact predicted"); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems: `prediction` after `hazards`; `tests/prediction` after `tests/hazards`); `docs/architecture.md` "Trajectory prediction" (milestone 2''s form, the step budget), "Scripted runs" → "Steps" (an event wait ends at the first grid point at or after the event); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" kept true.
- Contents: the `prediction` struct (own `sim` copy, a preallocated 20,000-step buffer of t, r, v, the horizon of one osculating period or two on request, events, validity, the controls'' signature); `(prediction-update! pred sim)` with the plan''s restart rules (signature change, throttle on, > 1 m off the buffer''s Hermite, t past the buffer''s end, restore or death) else extending the tail, at most `*prediction-steps-per-frame*` (4,096) `sim-step!`s at ×1,000 per call; `(prediction-run! pred sim)`; `(prediction-event pred kind)` for `:apoapsis`, `:periapsis` (r·v sign changes on the Hermite, root to 1e-6 s), `:impact` (with the copy''s loss record), `:cutoff`; `(prediction-dropout-event pred)`, `(prediction-complete-p pred)`; `(grid-ceiling t)`.
- Tests (the plan''s list): coasting at ×1,000 one orbit ahead bit for bit with the flight, frames of 500 steps equal one run; apsides (`:point`, e 0.1) within 1e-3 s of `orbit-next-apsis` and met at ×1 within the containing fine step; impact within 1e-2 s (×1,000) and 0.05 s (×1) of the flight''s; `:cutoff` at the flight''s cut time at ×100 exactly, apoapsis after it within 1 m; restart on throttle, hold and 2 m displacement, not on 100 coasting frames (only the tail grows); per-call budget respected; a full LEO prediction conses nothing after the first.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval` of `(prediction-run! …)` on the start state after a 100 m/s retrograde burn lists apoapsis, periapsis and no impact.', '2026-10-14T22:57:02Z', '2026-10-15T00:34:14Z', 84, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (106, 15, 'clock.lisp: the clock struct, clock-frame!, warp levels, pause and the actual rate', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/clock.lisp (clock struct, new-clock, clock-frame!, warp/pause commands, clock-actual-rate, clock-kinematic-p, clock-previous-state; step-h shared by sim-step! and the frame), tests/clock.lisp, docs/architecture.md (The clock, Drift bounds, Files in load order). Through-the-clock runs shortened as plan 15 allows (120 s fine, 5 orbits coarse); part''s tests measured: clock 0.99 s, hazards 0.12 s, prediction 0.39 s = 1.50 s, so task 107 has no headroom left (the x1 round trip, 0.29 s, is the largest). Done check: 600 frames of 1/60 s at x100 from the start state advance t by exactly 1,000 s.', 'Piece 4 of `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`: extend `src/clock.lisp` and `tests/clock.lisp` as the plan''s section "4. `clock.lisp`, part two" lists them (`decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 19: Time-warp rules`, `decision 31: Warp choices within the time-warp rules`, `docs/architecture.md` "The clock", "Time warp", "Drift bounds"). Needs `task 105: prediction.lisp: the milestone-2 events by sim-step! on a copy`.

- Files: `src/clock.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`; `docs/architecture.md` "The clock" (`clock-frame!`, the hook, `*frame-step-time-limit*`), "Drift bounds" (points at `tests/clock.lisp` for the through-the-clock rows as built).
- Contents: the `clock` struct (level index into ×1, ×4, ×10, ×100, ×1,000, ×10,000, ×100,000, ×1,000,000 as a `defparameter` list; accumulator; paused; a fixed-ring rate meter over the last second; messages for piece 5; preallocated previous ship state and `t`; `hook`; the `prediction`); `(clock-frame! clock sim elapsed)`: `prediction-update!` first, `acc += min(elapsed, 0.1) × level`, steps while `acc ≥` the next h (the hook gives `until`), at most 4,096 steps and `*frame-step-time-limit*` (0.004 s, checked every 64 steps, tests bind nil), the rest dropped; paused or lost: no steps (paused: `acc` 0, level kept). `clock-warp-up`, `clock-warp-down`, `clock-warp-reset`, `clock-toggle-pause` (effective at the next step boundary, never touching the sim; refusals come in piece 5), `clock-actual-rate`, `clock-kinematic-p`, `clock-previous-state`.
- Tests (the plan''s list, `:point`, the "Drift bounds" test orbit, direct mode, no keys): every level fed 1/60 s frames equals a direct `sim-step!` loop bit for bit (×1, ×4 over 600 s; coarse levels over 10 orbits; ×1,000,000 capped at 4,096 per frame); 1/144 s frames and an irregular list (with 0.5 s clamped) give the same states at ×1, ×4, ×1,000; a level change leaves the sim unchanged and the next step uses the new h; ×1 → ×1,000 → ×1 over one orbit within 5 m of pure ×1; 100 paused frames change nothing, resume keeps the level; the actual rate at ×1,000,000 within 1 %. If over budget, shorten as the plan allows and say so in the test''s comment.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval` of 600 `clock-frame!`s of 1/60 s at ×100 from the start state advances `t` by 1,000 s.', '2026-10-14T22:57:18Z', '2026-10-15T00:40:07Z', 84, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (107, 15, 'clock.lisp: warp refusals, per-step lowering, drop-outs, messages and restart', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/clock.lisp (warp-up refusals with clock-warp-up taking the sim; clock-check-level! before every step: thrust limit, x4 on a hold released above x4, drop-out to the highest L with delta >= 3 s x L, accumulator scaled; messages with summed-elapsed stamps live 3 s, clock-messages, format-duration via duration-fields; clock-restart!; tunables *thrust-warp-limit*, *cutoff-warp-limit*, *warp-rotation-limit*, *dropout-real-time*, *message-time*), tests/clock.lisp (refusals, lowering, drop-out to impact from 1 h at x1,000,000, message expiry, restart), docs/architecture.md (The clock, Time warp, Warp events and collisions), docs/design.md (Time warp: hold rules, decision 73''s texts). Budget: the plan''s tests (clock, hazards, prediction) measured from Parachute durations in the full suite were 1.50 s before plus 0.09 s of new tests; brought to 1.35 s by binding *prediction-steps-per-frame* to 64 in the drift-orbit clock runs (no drop-out event there) and flying prediction-apsides'' x1 approach from 20 s rather than 300 s before the apsis (after a coarse step it is under an inertial hold, so x1 steps run the mixer, ~4 us each). scripts/test passes; rk4-cons-nothing flaked once (task 140).', 'Piece 5 of `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`: finish `src/clock.lisp` and `tests/clock.lisp` as the plan''s section "5. `clock.lisp`, part three" lists them (`decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering`, `decision 19: Time-warp rules`, `decision 31: Warp choices within the time-warp rules`, `decision 34: How death works`, `decision 43: Warp drop-outs for contact and life support` for what stays for milestones 3–4). Needs `task 106: clock.lisp: the clock struct, clock-frame!, warp levels, pause and the actual rate`.

- Files: `src/clock.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`; `docs/architecture.md` "Time warp" (entry with an inertial hold, the snap, release lowering to ×4, the per-step checks), "Testing" → "Warp, events and collisions" (milestone 2''s cases as built); `docs/design.md` "Time warp" (the hold rules and `decision 73`''s message texts).
- Contents: refusals of a warp up (throttle on above ×10, or ×100 with `cutoff` armed; above ×4 with |ω| ≥ 0.01 rad/s and no hold; the drop-out event less than 3 s × the new level away), each leaving the level with its message; checks before every step (throttle limit, no hold above ×4 → ×4, highest L with Δ ≥ 3 s × L to the drop-out event), the accumulator scaled by new/old, one message per lowering; messages with a real-time stamp from summed `elapsed`, live 3 s (`clock-messages`), durations through `units.lisp`; `(clock-restart! clock sim checkpoint)` (restore, ×1, unpaused, `acc` 0, messages cleared, prediction restarted). Tunables (3 s, ×10/×100, 0.01 rad/s) as `defparameter`s citing their decisions.
- Tests (the plan''s list): the three refusals with their texts and the allowed cases (inertial hold engaged at 0.005 rad/s); lowering on throttle up at ×100 and on releasing the hold at ×1,000; drop-out to impact from 1 h before at ×1,000,000 through `clock-frame!` (Δ ≥ 3 s × level at every step, ×1 at impact, time within 1e-2 s, point within 0.01°); one message each, gone after 3 s; death then `clock-restart!` is `equalp` to `(new-game-sim)` at ×1 and 1,000 frames after equal a fresh start''s bit for bit.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; the plan''s tests (`tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/hazards.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp`) together run under 1.5 s, measured and given in the done note.', '2026-10-14T22:57:18Z', '2026-10-15T00:48:41Z', 84, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (108, 16, 'gpu.lisp and camera.lisp: HAL helpers, the camera, the one projection function', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/gpu.lisp, src/camera.lisp, tests/camera.lisp, src/scene.lisp (renderer subclass, picture byte-identical to HEAD''s), src/main.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md; texture-from-pixels and render-target checked on a device in ./sly', 'Piece 1 of `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets`: create `src/gpu.lisp`, `src/camera.lisp` and `tests/camera.lisp` as the plan''s section "1. `gpu.lisp` and `camera.lisp`" lists them (`decision 4: Depth strategy`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`, `decision 30: Views and cameras`; `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision", "Floating-origin pitfalls", "Frames"). Needs `task 92: math.lisp: vectors, quaternions, the single-float boundary` (`relative-single`, quats) and `task 94: bodies.lisp part one: bodies, rotations, body-fixed frames` (R⊕).

- Files: `src/gpu.lisp`, `src/camera.lisp` (after `shaders` in `luv-in-space.asd`, both systems, per "Files in load order"); `src/scene.lisp` switches to the helpers; `tests/camera.lisp`; `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision" (projection in `camera.lisp`, drop the sentence on `uniform-data`), "Files in load order"; `AGENTS.md` "Layout" if it names files.
- `gpu.lisp`: `vertex-buffer`, `uniform-buffer`, `live-pipeline` (role, layout, vertex buffers, target format, depth, blend, topology), size-cached render targets keyed by (extent, format) with views, old ones released through luv''s deferred `destroy` on a size change; `texture-from-pixels` (rank-2 `(unsigned-byte 32)` → `:rgba8-unorm-srgb`, view, linear sampler, repeat u, clamp v); a `renderer` class with `renderer-live-artifacts` and `destroy-renderer`. luv limits: `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Rendering".
- `camera.lisp`: `camera` struct (anchor `:ship`, double ICRF offset, FRD orientation quat, vertical FOV, near 0.1 m); `camera-clip-rows!` (the one projection, s = +1 on Vulkan only here); `camera-eye`, `eye-relative-single`, `sphere-offset-term`; `outside-camera-default!` with defparameters `*outside-distance*` 40 and `*outside-elevation*` 20°, FOV 50°.
- Tests: the plan''s list (depth 0.1/d at d = 1, 10, 10^7 within 1e-6 relative; signs of clip x and y; aspect scales x only; `sphere-offset-term` vs rationals within 1e-12 at 400 km and 1 km altitude, single-float difference not; default pose looks at the ship within 1e-12 rad, radial-out above the view axis).

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `scripts/screenshot` gives the skeleton''s picture unchanged; `./sly eval ''(camera-clip-rows! …)''` on a default camera prints 16 finite singles.', '2026-10-14T22:58:09Z', '2026-10-15T01:00:56Z', 85, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (109, 16, 'render.lisp, overlay.lisp, main.lisp, capture.lisp: the frame runs the clock, the skeleton goes', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14: src/render.lisp (render-state, render-state-update! conses 0 per 1,000 updates, uv-sphere, frame-renderer with per-target uniforms in a canvas-frame-resource-cache, encode-frame: placeholder stars, true-scale Earth at R⊕ with procedural colours in body-fixed axes, label; PLACEHOLDER(76)), src/overlay.lisp (glyphs, label PLACEHOLDER(76 77 80), :overlay pipeline), src/main.lisp (game with sim, clock, start checkpoint, camera, camera-fn, render state; clock-frame! on luv frame time; encode-capture-frame unstepped; cleanup-capture releases the target''s resources; start :sim :paused), src/capture.lisp (capture-state, with-capture-game, capture-game-state, capture-scene); quat-slerp! (math), earth-fixed-matrix! and inline t->ut1-days/earth-rotation-revolutions (bodies, units), forget-color-view (gpu), shaders'' frame block gains Earth''s matrix; scene.lisp and tests/scene.lisp deleted, PLACEHOLDER(23) gone; tests/render.lisp (CPU: ends bit for bit, Hermite midpoint of a 2 s coarse step within 1e-3 m, fallbacks after clock-restart!, stale t_prev and death, no consing, uv-sphere; GPU at 320x200: size/signature, lower third brighter than upper, not black, 0 failed artifacts, nadir centre lit); tests/capture.lisp size and signature only; AGENTS.md Layout/Commands, docs/architecture.md (clock render time and fallback, GPU tests, files in load order). Checked: scripts/test 2735 passed (~11 s); scripts/screenshot shows Earth''s limb across the lower half and the label; ./sly play: sim-t advances 1.0 s per real second, live screenshot fine, camera-clip-rows! on the game camera 16 finite singles; Escape via handle-event sets the quit flag (no key injector here); nix build, nix flake check pass, result/bin/luv-in-space runs from /tmp (stopped by PID). Follow-ups: task 142, task 143.', 'Piece 2 of `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets`: as the plan''s section "2. `render.lisp`, `overlay.lisp`, `main.lisp`, `capture.lisp`" lists it (`decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 7: Placeholder labels: dot-matrix overlay quads`, `decision 2: Screenshots and GPU test: offscreen capture on a hidden canvas, headless on lavapipe`). Needs `task 108: gpu.lisp and camera.lisp: HAL helpers, the camera, the one projection function`, `task 95: bodies.lisp part two: ephemerides and the Hermite cache` (`body-state`, `body-fixed-matrix`), `task 106: clock.lisp: the clock struct, clock-frame!, warp levels, pause and the actual rate` and `task 107: clock.lisp: warp refusals, per-step lowering, drop-outs, messages and restart` (`clock-restart!`, death).

- Files: `src/render.lisp`, `src/overlay.lisp` (load order: `overlay`, `render` after `camera`), `src/main.lisp`, `src/capture.lisp`; `tests/render.lisp`, `tests/capture.lisp`; delete `src/scene.lisp`, `tests/scene.lisp`; `luv-in-space.asd` both systems; `scripts/screenshot` if it calls into the scene.
- `render.lisp`: preallocated `render-state`, `render-state-update!` (clamped s, cubic Hermite r and v in double, `quat-slerp`, ω linear; the sim''s state when no previous state, t_prev ≥ t, or lost; conses nothing); `encode-frame` with one pass for now: placeholder stars, placeholder Earth (`uv-sphere` moved here, true scale R⊕, eye-relative, Sun-lit at t_r, depth `:greater`), overlay. Both placeholders carry `PLACEHOLDER(76)`.
- `overlay.lisp`: glyph table, `quad`, `label-vertices` from `scene.lisp`, the overlay pipeline, the label `PLACEHOLDER(76 77 80)` top left.
- `main.lisp`: `game` gains clock, sim (`new-game-sim`), start checkpoint, camera, renderer, render state, previous frame time; `draw` runs `clock-frame!` on elapsed real time (0 on the first frame), the default outside camera, `encode-frame`; `encode-capture-frame` without stepping; `start` takes `:sim` and `:paused`; Escape and close still quit.
- `capture.lisp`: `capture-state` (hidden canvas, a copy of the sim, paused clock, `camera-fn`), `capture-scene` = `capture-state` of `(new-game-sim)`, `with-capture-game`.
- Remove `PLACEHOLDER(23)` everywhere (code, `docs/`, `AGENTS.md`).
- Tests: the plan''s CPU list (s = 0 and 1 bit for bit; s = ½ of a 2 s step within 1e-3 m of `orbit-state`; fallback after `clock-restart!` and death; 1,000 updates cons nothing; the `uv-sphere` checks) and GPU list in one `with-capture-game` at 320×200 (PNG size and signature; lower third brighter than upper third; not fully black; `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0; nadir camera lit centre). `tests/capture.lisp` keeps size and signature only.
- Docs: `AGENTS.md` "Layout" (`src/` as built, the placeholders), "Commands" (`scripts/screenshot` renders the start state from the outside view); `docs/architecture.md` "The clock" (render time, fallback), "GPU tests", "Files in load order".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `scripts/screenshot /tmp/x.png` shows Earth''s limb across the lower half and the label; `./sly start`, `./sly play`, `(sim-t (game-sim *game*))` a second apart differs by about 1 s; Escape closes the window.', '2026-10-14T22:58:09Z', '2026-10-15T01:11:38Z', 85, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (110, 16, 'assets.lisp, the Blue Marble and its packaging', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, assets/earth/blue-marble-5400.jpg (1,884,678 bytes, 5400x2700, SHA-256 99f5faad…dde5) and SOURCE.md, CREDITS.md, src/assets.lisp, src/shaders.lisp (atan2, arcsin), src/render.lisp (Earth samples the texture through body-fixed-matrix), flake.nix (assets/ in both sources, installed to share/luv-in-space/assets, launcher exports LUV_IN_SPACE_ASSETS), tests/assets.lisp, tests/render.lisp, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md. Decode 0.135 s. scripts/test passes (2753 checks, ~10 s wall); nix build installs the JPEG; cd /tmp && nix run opened the window, closed by PID; nix flake check passes. Tests differ from the plan per decision 92: Blue Marble tests: Antarctic row and Earth-versus-background start check (January''s Arctic is dark; the real Pacific is darker than the label and stars). Follow-up task 144: GC now reclaims undestroyed swapchain colour views.', 'Piece 3 of `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets`: as the plan''s section "3. `assets.lisp`, the Blue Marble and its packaging" lists it (`decision 13: Asset storage and attribution`, `decision 40: Earth''s look and drag`, `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`; `docs/architecture.md` "Assets", `docs/design.md` "The places" → "Sources"). Needs `task 109: render.lisp, overlay.lisp, main.lisp, capture.lisp: the frame runs the clock, the skeleton goes`. Needs web access; without it, stop and record it as `decision 45: Web access for pm workers still denied after decision 28` did.

- Asset: fetch `world.200401.3x5400x2700.jpg` (URL in `docs/design.md` "Sources"), check ~1.8 MB and 5400×2700; commit as `assets/earth/blue-marble-5400.jpg` with `assets/earth/SOURCE.md` (URL, date fetched, NASA media-guidelines licence text as quoted in `docs/luv-capabilities.md`, credit "NASA Earth Observatory (Blue Marble Next Generation)", no NASA logo, SHA-256) and root `CREDITS.md`.
- `src/assets.lisp` (load order: after `shaders`, before `gpu`): `assets-root` (`LUV_IN_SPACE_ASSETS` when set and non-empty, else `asdf:system-relative-pathname`), `asset-path` (clear error when missing), `load-image-pixels` (`sdl3-image`, ABGR8888, rank-2 `(unsigned-byte 32)` rows × columns, surfaces freed, typed copy loop).
- `flake.nix`: `gameSource` and `testSource` include `assets/`; the package copies `assets/` to `$out/share/luv-in-space/assets`, the launcher exports `LUV_IN_SPACE_ASSETS`.
- Placeholder Earth samples the texture (still `PLACEHOLDER(76)`): uploaded once by the renderer via `texture-from-pixels`; the fragment shader maps the ICRF normal through `body-fixed-matrix` (uniform mat3) to u = 0.5 + atan2(y, x)/(2π), v = 0.5 − asin(z)/π; polynomial `atan2` and `asin` shader functions in `shaders.lisp`, error below 1e-4 rad.
- Tests `tests/assets.lisp`: `assets-root` with an env string and nil; missing `asset-path` signals; 2700 × 5400; (row 1350, col 2700) blue > red; (row 1005, col 2850) red > blue; mean of row 5 > 150 per channel; decode time measured (< 1 s, in the done note). `tests/render.lisp`: the nadir centre pixel is open Pacific (sub-ship point from `latitude-longitude`), blue > red.
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Assets"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Packaging"; `docs/luv-wishlist.md` "runtime data directories" and "texture loading" (workaround, file named).

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `nix build` succeeds with `result/share/luv-in-space/assets/earth/blue-marble-5400.jpg`; `cd /tmp && nix run <repo>` opens the window with the textured Earth (closed by PID); `nix flake check` passes.', '2026-10-14T22:58:32Z', '2026-10-15T01:19:41Z', 85, 1);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (111, 16, 'post.lisp: HDR target, bloom, tone map, exposure', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/post.lisp, src/render.lisp, src/shaders.lisp, src/overlay.lisp, src/main.lisp, tests/post.lisp, tests/render.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md. Three stages per decision 76: scene into :hdr (rgba16-float), bloom 13-tap down to 1/16 and tent up, one pass on the target with tone map (mix at *bloom-strength*, exposure, ACES, sRGB unless -srgb, input clamped to [0, 6e4], NaN to 0) then the overlay. luv''s Vulkan passes only clear (load-op :load rejected), so the way up writes separate up levels; recorded in luv-capabilities and the wishlist. Exposure rule as decision 93: Exposure rule as built: hidden Sun, coverage within the view. scripts/test: 2789 passed, ~11-12 s wall; nix flake check passes. scripts/screenshot: textured Earth tone-mapped, no white-out, label crisp, but dark: at exposure 1.0 the Blue Marble ocean falls in ACES''s toe (noted for plan 17''s Earth retune under decision 78). ./sly play: (setf *bloom-strength* 0.3) widened a 4e4 test quad''s glow on the next frame; a redefined tone-map-fragment (red only) showed on the next frame. Frame rate on the default GPU (Intel iGPU): 60 fps cadence held; ~127 fps with the cadence clock lifted, in a 959x1010 window (the tiling WM did not give 1280x800).', 'Piece 4 of `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets`: as the plan''s section "4. `post.lisp`" lists it (`decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`, `decision 61: Performance target GPU: the default Vulkan device, the Intel iGPU`; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Sun glare and brightness"). Needs `task 110: assets.lisp, the Blue Marble and its packaging`.

- Files: `src/post.lisp` (load order: after `camera`, before `overlay`), `src/render.lisp` (`encode-frame` in three stages), `src/shaders.lisp` as needed, `tests/post.lisp` (after `tests/assets.lisp`), `tests/render.lisp`; `luv-in-space.asd` both systems.
- Frame: scene pass into a size-cached `:rgba16-float` target with depth; bloom mip chain 1/2 to 1/16 (13-tap down, 9-tap tent up, added level by level, `*bloom-strength*` 0.04); one tone-map pass into the canvas or capture target (exposure, ACES filmic, sRGB encode when the target is not `-srgb`, input clamped to [0, 6×10^4]); overlay on the target without depth. Each pass its own live pipeline role; bind groups after each `set-pipeline`.
- Radiance scale: placeholder Earth''s lit white = 1.0; placeholder stars visible at deep exposure, gone at sunlit.
- Exposure (CPU, pure): `exposure-target` (Sun within half-diagonal + 5°, or a body''s coverage × lit fraction ≥ 0.05 with coverage ≥ 5 % → `*exposure-sunlit*` 1.0; else `*exposure-deep*` 16.0; `:map` → `*exposure-map*`); `exposure-ease` (log2, τ 1.0 s real time, also paused; first frame and captures snap).
- Tests `tests/post.lisp`: the plan''s list (start → sunlit; shadow at u = 180° looking away → deep; looking at the Sun → sunlit; Earth at phase 170° filling the view → deep; easing 1 − 1/e after τ within 1e-12; snapping; `:map`). `tests/render.lisp` GPU, same `with-capture-game`: the 4×10^4 test quad''s bloom lifts pixels 20 px away by > 10/255, not with strength 0; non-finite/negative never reaches the target; start frame mean luminance < 200/255; overlay label pixels exactly its colour; `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0. Whole `scripts/test` under ~15 s (measured, in the done note).
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision" → "Draw order" as the three stages, radiance scale and exposure rule; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Sun glare and brightness"; `docs/luv-wishlist.md` post-processing item names `post.lisp` and its size in lines.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `scripts/screenshot` shows the textured Earth tone-mapped, no white-out, label crisp; with `./sly play`, `(setf *bloom-strength* 0.3)` widens the glow on the next frame and a re-evaluated tone-map shader shows live; frame rate at 1280×800 on the default GPU in the done note.', '2026-10-14T22:58:32Z', '2026-10-15T01:36:00Z', 85, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (112, 17, 'scripts/convert-stars, assets/stars/ and load-star-table: the HYG star table', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, scripts/convert-stars, scripts/convert-stars.lisp, assets/stars/{hyg-6.5.sexp,SOURCE.md,LICENSE}, CREDITS.md, src/assets.lisp (load-star-table, star-table), tests/assets.lisp, flake.nix (curl in the dev shell), AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md. HYG v4.4 (hyg_v44.csv.gz, Git LFS, commit 53e3df31, SHA-256 pinned): 8,920 stars <= 6.5 mag, 369,131 bytes; two runs of scripts/convert-stars /tmp/x.sexp identical and equal to the committed table. load-star-table ~0.009 s (warm). scripts/test: 2811 passed, 0 failed. nix build installs result/share/luv-in-space/assets/stars/hyg-6.5.sexp.', 'Piece 1 of `plan 17: Earth, Moon, Sun and stars`: everything its section "1. The star table: `scripts/convert-stars`, `assets/stars/`, the loader" lists (`decision 13: Asset storage and attribution`, `decision 78: Sky in numbers: stars, Sun, Moon and Earth''s look`; `docs/architecture.md` "Assets"). Needs `task 110: assets.lisp, the Blue Marble and its packaging` (`assets-root`, `asset-path`, `assets/` in the flake). Needs web access; without it, stop and record it as `decision 45: Web access for pm workers still denied after decision 28` did.

- `scripts/convert-stars [out]` and `scripts/convert-stars.lisp`: download the current `hyg_v4x.csv` from `codeberg.org/astronexus/hyg` into a fresh `mktemp -d`, check the SHA-256 written in the script, keep `mag` ≤ 6.5 but the Sun, sort by magnitude then `id`, write `assets/stars/hyg-6.5.sexp` (header comment, then `(hip ra-deg dec-deg mag ci)` per star, six decimals, `ci` nil when missing); delete the temporary directory.
- `assets/stars/SOURCE.md`, `assets/stars/LICENSE` (CC BY-SA 4.0 legal code), the HYG credit in `CREDITS.md`.
- `src/assets.lisp`: `load-star-table` (`*read-eval*` nil, standard readtable, format checked) → struct of specialised arrays: ICRF unit directions (single), magnitude, colour index with a no-colour flag.
- Tests `tests/assets.lisp` as the plan lists them (count 8,000–10,000, Sirius, Polaris, no Sun, units, load < 0.5 s, file < 1 MB).
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Assets"; `AGENTS.md` "Commands" (`scripts/convert-stars`: needs network, rewrites the committed table) and "Layout" (`assets/stars/`).

Done when: `scripts/convert-stars /tmp/x.sexp` twice gives identical files equal to the committed one; `scripts/test` passes (load time in the done note); `nix build` succeeds with `result/share/luv-in-space/assets/stars/hyg-6.5.sexp` present.', '2026-10-14T22:59:36Z', '2026-10-15T01:43:59Z', 86, 1);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (113, 17, 'stars.lisp: the stars at infinity, their colours and the :stars pipeline', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/stars.lisp (new), src/shaders.lisp (star-vertex, star-fragment, the frame block''s stars vec4, :stars and :quads roles), src/render.lisp (star instances and corners, instanced draw, :quads pipeline, placeholder stars gone), src/post.lisp (tone-map-srgb), luv-in-space.asd, tests/stars.lisp (new), tests/render.lisp (star GPU checks), AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md. Constants checked against their sources: the CIE fit from Wyman-Sloan-Shirley 2013 Listing 1 (JCGT 2(2)), the IEC 61966-2-1 Amd 1 2003 matrix, Ballesteros 2012. Plan changes: decision 95: Star fading at the sunlit exposure as built (mag >= 1.0 reads 21 of 255 at sunlit under decision 78''s numbers, so the test checks mag >= 3.0 < 8 and mag >= 1.0 < 24); Procyon is checked in a 60 deg view centred at RA 108 Dec -6, since it is 22 deg from Sirius and outside a 20 deg one; Orion''s bounds are 490-1970 from the first measured frame, 985 px above 30. scripts/test: 2891 passed, 0 failed, 12.1 s wall with the star GPU checks (7 more captures in the shared 320x200 game). scripts/screenshot: no placeholder stars, a few faint real ones. ./sly play at u = 180 towards Orion at 50 deg: build/task-113-orion.png (Orion, Sirius, Aldebaran recognisable); (setf *star-radiance-limit* 5e-3) showed on the next frame: build/task-113-orion-limit-5e-3.png. nix build passes.', 'Piece 2 of `plan 17: Earth, Moon, Sun and stars`: everything its section "2. `stars.lisp`: the stars at infinity" lists (`decision 78: Sky in numbers: stars, Sun, Moon and Earth''s look`, `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Starfield"). Needs `task 112: scripts/convert-stars, assets/stars/ and load-star-table: the HYG star table`, `task 108: gpu.lisp and camera.lisp: HAL helpers, the camera, the one projection function` and `task 111: post.lisp: HDR target, bloom, tone map, exposure`. Web access only to check the colour-matching constants (Ballesteros 2012; Wyman, Sloan, Shirley 2013, JCGT 2(2); the IEC 61966-2-1 matrix) against their sources.

- `src/stars.lisp` (after `camera.lisp`, before `meshes`/`post`): the 64-entry B−V colour table (sources in comments), the static instance buffer (direction, linear RGB × peak radiance, σ) built once at renderer start and destroyed by `destroy-renderer`; `*star-radiance-limit*`, `*star-sigma*`, `*star-saturation*` as `defparameter`s.
- Shaders in `shaders.lisp` (`define-frame-shader`), live pipeline `:stars` (clip z 0, quad of 4σ px, Gaussian, additive, compare `:always`, no depth write), drawn first in the scene pass; part 4''s placeholder stars and their `PLACEHOLDER(76)` go (the placeholder Earth stays until piece 4).
- `post.lisp`: `tone-map-srgb` (CPU replica of the shader''s tone map), unless part 4 added it.
- Tests: `tests/stars.lisp` (CPU) and the GPU checks in `tests/render.lisp` (the shared 320×200 capture, ship at u = 180°: Sirius centred, Procyon''s predicted pixel, Orion''s pixel count with bounds from the first measured frame, shader tone map vs `tone-map-srgb`, no failed live artifacts), as the plan lists them.
- Docs: `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Starfield" (as built), `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision" → draw order and "Files in load order".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes (GPU checks timed in the done note); `scripts/screenshot` shows no placeholder stars; with `./sly play` and the camera away from the Sun at night, Orion can be recognised (screenshot path in the done note); `(setf *star-radiance-limit* …)` changes the stars on the next frame.', '2026-10-14T22:59:36Z', '2026-10-15T01:54:11Z', 86, 1);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (114, 17, 'impostors.lisp part one: impostor machinery, the Sun, the Moon, sun-visible-fraction', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/impostors.lisp (new: impostor-params!, impostor-corners, impostor-uniforms!, :sun and :moon pipelines, draw-impostor), src/shaders.lisp (frame block +8 vec4s; impostor-clip, view-ray, sphere-half-chord2, ray-sphere-near, ray-sphere-far, sphere-near-normal, impostor-depth; sun/moon vertex and fragment), src/bodies.lisp (lens-area moved here, sun-visible-fraction inline, 0 bytes per call), src/render.lisp (render-state sun-fraction, impostors drawn after the stars), src/post.lisp (decision 79''s ship term), luv-in-space.asd, tests/bodies.lisp, tests/impostors.lisp (new), tests/post.lisp, tests/render.lisp (Sun width and limb darkening, glare, hidden behind Earth, Moon grey and phase), AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md. As built: decision 96: Impostors part one as built: the ship term''s eye-inside case and the GPU checks'' exposures (limb darkening checked at exposure 1e-5, not 2e-5; the Moon''s phase with the bloom off; no ship term with the eye inside the bounding sphere). Measured: penumbra 5-15 s and the 0.5 point within 0.1 deg of the shadow edge; Moon at the start 16.7 deg from full. scripts/test: 2945 passed, 0 failed, 9.4 s wall. scripts/screenshot unchanged from before (dark placeholder Earth). nix build passes. ./sly play with a camera on the Sun: a white glow with the stars faded (exposure 1.0); the glow is a rounded square, so task 145: post.lisp: a round Sun glare instead of the bloom chain''s rounded square. At x100 the live ship''s sun-visible-fraction was 1 at 1,172 s and 0 at 1,551 s after the start (shadow entry 21.9 min).', 'Piece 3 of `plan 17: Earth, Moon, Sun and stars`: everything its section "3. `impostors.lisp`, part one" lists (`decision 78: Sky in numbers: stars, Sun, Moon and Earth''s look`, `decision 79: Sunlight at a point and the sunlit ship in the exposure rule`, `decision 4: Depth strategy`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`; `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision", `docs/design.md` "The Sun", "The Moon", "The start"). Needs `task 113: stars.lisp: the stars at infinity, their colours and the :stars pipeline` (draw order, `tone-map-srgb`), `task 95: bodies.lisp part two: ephemerides and the Hermite cache` (`body-state`), `task 103: clock.lisp: the sim state, the start state, sim-step! and checkpoints` (the start orbit) and `task 109: render.lisp, overlay.lisp, main.lisp, capture.lisp: the frame runs the clock, the skeleton goes` (`render-state`, the capture).

- `src/bodies.lisp`: `sun-visible-fraction` (Earth and the Moon as occulting discs, exact circle overlap in angle, the smaller fraction kept, double, conses nothing) and a pure circle-overlap helper.
- `src/render.lisp`: `render-state` gains `sun-fraction`; `post.lisp`''s `exposure-target` gains `decision 79`''s ship term (`*ship-bounding-radius*` 10.0 m, threshold 0.005, outside view only).
- `src/impostors.lisp`: `impostor-params!` (camera-relative centre via `eye-relative-single`, `sphere-offset-term` in double, quad over the tangent cone or full-screen triangle past 45° or with the eye inside); shader functions in `shaders.lisp`: view ray, `ray-sphere-near` with the stable root, `ray-sphere-far`, reversed-Z depth via `:frag-depth`, misses discarded.
- Live pipelines `:sun` (limb darkening, centre radiance 4.6e4, glare only from bloom) and `:moon` (grey Lambert, albedo 0.12, depth written), after the stars.
- Tests in `tests/bodies.lisp`, `tests/impostors.lisp`, `tests/post.lisp` and GPU checks in `tests/render.lisp` (Sun''s width and limb darkening, glare, occlusion behind Earth, the Moon''s phase), as the plan lists them.
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision", "Files in load order"; `docs/design.md` "The Sun", "Views"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Sun glare and brightness".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; with `./sly play`, a camera turned to the Sun shows a round disc with glare and faded stars; `sun-visible-fraction` on the live ship reaches 0 about 22 min after the start (or within a minute at ×100).', '2026-10-14T22:59:36Z', '2026-10-15T02:11:39Z', 86, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (115, 17, 'impostors.lisp part two: Earth, its atmosphere rim and halo; PLACEHOLDER(76) goes', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/assets.lisp (downsample-pixels, 0.115 s for the 1/8 copy), src/impostors.lisp (Earth and halo blocks, :earth and :earth-halo pipelines, *rim-strength* *halo-power* *halo-radiance* *halo-day* *halo-dusk* *halo-band* *earth-coarse-factor*), src/shaders.lisp (earth-fragment, halo-fragment, the frame block at 29 vec4s; earth-vertex now the impostor''s), src/render.lisp (uv-sphere and the mesh Earth gone, the 1/8 copy uploaded and bound at 3, the four impostors drawn after the stars), src/overlay.lisp (label PLACEHOLDER(77 80)), tests/assets.lisp (blue-marble-eighth), tests/render.lisp (uv-sphere tests gone; earth-checks: horizon column, night nadir, round from 40,000 km), AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md; decision 97: Earth and halo impostors as built: rim, footprint mix, halo depth and colour ramps. scripts/test passes, 2968 checks, 13.9 s wall in total; nix build passes. scripts/screenshot shows a round Blue Marble Earth with a blue halo on the limb and the label PLACEHOLDER(77 80). With ./sly play at x100: the limb ahead turns orange before the night pass (t = 582 s), Earth goes dark (1062 to 2502 s), the exposure eases to 16 and the stars come up (2012 to 2502 s), then sunrise with a blue limb (3480 s). A re-evaluated earth-fragment with a red tint showed on the next screenshot, then was restored. Screenshots were deleted.', 'Piece 4 of `plan 17: Earth, Moon, Sun and stars`: everything its section "4. `impostors.lisp`, part two" lists (`decision 78: Sky in numbers: stars, Sun, Moon and Earth''s look`, `decision 40: Earth''s look and drag`, `decision 34: How death works`, `decision 15: Coordinate frames`; `docs/design.md` "Earth", `docs/architecture.md` "Frames", "Rendering precision"). Needs `task 114: impostors.lisp part one: impostor machinery, the Sun, the Moon, sun-visible-fraction`, `task 110: assets.lisp, the Blue Marble and its packaging` and `task 94: bodies.lisp part one: bodies, rotations, body-fixed frames` (`body-fixed-matrix`).

- `src/assets.lisp`: `(downsample-pixels pixels 8)`, the 675 × 338 box-filtered copy, uploaded by the renderer with the Blue Marble and destroyed by `destroy-renderer`.
- Live pipeline `:earth`: R⊕ impostor at −eye; hit normal into body-fixed axes by `body-fixed-matrix` at t_r; u/v lookup per "Frames" with `sample-level` 0 from both textures mixed by texel footprint; radiance = texture × max(n·s, 0) × (1 AU / d_sun)²; rim on the lit limb (`*rim-strength*`).
- Live pipeline `:earth-halo`: R⊕ + 100 km, additive, depth-tested without depth write, after Earth; chord ratio to `*halo-power*` × `*halo-radiance*`, blue by day, orange near the terminator, zero 6° below.
- Part 4''s placeholder Earth (`uv-sphere`) goes with its tests; `PLACEHOLDER(76)` leaves the code, the on-screen label, `AGENTS.md` and `docs/` (`PLACEHOLDER(77 80)` stays).
- Tests: `tests/assets.lisp` (the 1/8 copy''s size and means) and the GPU checks in `tests/render.lisp` (nadir Pacific, the horizon column through the halo, the dark night side, Earth round from 40,000 km, no failed live artifacts), as the plan lists them.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "Earth"; `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order", "GPU tests"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Spheres and planet surfaces"; `docs/luv-wishlist.md` (Vulkan mip levels and their generation; a ray-sphere impostor helper, naming `impostors.lisp` and its size in lines); `AGENTS.md` "Layout".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes in under ~15 s (measured, in the done note); `scripts/screenshot` shows a round Blue Marble Earth with a blue halo on the limb and no label for 76; `./sly play` at ×100 through a night pass shows the orange terminator band, a dark Earth and the stars coming up; a re-evaluated `earth-fragment` shows on the next frame.', '2026-10-14T22:59:36Z', '2026-10-15T02:24:23Z', 86, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (116, 18, 'meshes.lisp part one: generators, the Mule''s parts, the decal and the bounding radius', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/meshes.lisp (new, ~450 lines), tests/meshes.lisp (new), luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md ''Files in load order'', AGENTS.md ''Layout''. ./sly eval ''(length (model-vertices (mule-model)))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE prints 65718: 7,302 hull vertices of 9 singles (engine 408 more; instances 102 tubes, 11 boxes, 24 cones). Bounding radius wet 12.57 m, dry 11.70 m. scripts/test passes (4437), ~10.4 s cached; scripts/screenshot unchanged. *ship-materials* (15 x 6: rgb, spec weight, exponent, emission) and material ids already live here since the decal reads the stencil and cairn albedos; part two (task 117) packs them for upload.', 'Piece 1 of `plan 18: The Mule''s meshes`: everything its section "1. `meshes.lisp`, part one" lists, CPU only, with every number from `decision 80: The Mule''s meshes in numbers: geometry, draws, materials and lights` (`decision 71: The Mule''s mass model in ship.lisp`, `decision 22: The player''s ship and its propulsion`, `decision 49: Story: names, call signs and ships`, `decision 30: Views and cameras` for the portholes; `docs/design.md` "How they look", "Parts", "Body axes and reference point", "Propulsion"). Needs `task 100: ship.lisp: the Mule''s parts, mass properties, engine and RCS layout` (thruster table, `ship-mass-properties`, `ship-trim-angle`).

- `src/meshes.lisp` (new; after `impostors.lisp`, before `ribbons`/`post` in both systems of `luv-in-space.asd`): vertex format of 9 singles (position, normal, material id, two parameters), triangle lists; generators `box`, `cylinder` (n sides, optional caps), `frustum`, `hemisphere`, `disc`, `rect` appending into an adjustable single-float vector with a transform (origin, unit basis, scale), outward normals and parameters (axial coordinate; decal/window/hatch/porthole u, v).
- Instance groups: unit 8-sided tube (x 0–1, radius 1), unit box, unit cone; instance = origin, basis, scale, material (16 singles); `(tube-instance a b radius material)`.
- `(mule-model)` → a `model` struct: baked vertices, instance groups, the engine''s own baked mesh, light positions; parts tagged by name so a part''s vertex range can be looked up. Nozzles placed from `ship.lisp`''s thruster table.
- `(engine-rotation m-p)`: rotation about body y by `ship-trim-angle` through the gimbal (0, 0, −0.5).
- `(stencil-decal-pixels)`: 128 × 512 `(unsigned-byte 32)` array for `texture-from-pixels`: the cairn (three grey ellipses) and "M-07" as black 5 × 7 stencil letters with bridges, alpha 0 elsewhere.
- `(ship-bounding-radius model m-p)`: max distance from the CoM to any vertex (instances expanded, engine at its trim), consing nothing after the first call.
- Pure: no HAL here; simulation files stay free of `meshes.lisp`.
- Tests `tests/meshes.lisp` (after `tests/impostors.lisp`), as the plan lists them: generator triangle counts, unit and outward normals, parameter ranges; `tube-instance` endpoints and normals; the Mule''s instance counts (88, 8, 24, 3), overall and part bounding boxes, nozzle axes against the thruster forces; trim axis through the CoM for full, half and empty tanks; decal size, letter-cell coverage, the broken "0" ring, grey cairn; bounding radius against brute force (wet and dry values in a comment), no consing on the second call.
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`meshes.lisp`, milestone 2, as built so far).

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(length (model-vertices (mule-model)))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` prints the vertex count, noted in the done note.', '2026-10-14T23:00:33Z', '2026-10-15T02:39:26Z', 87, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (117, 18, 'meshes.lisp part two: the Mule drawn and lit; PLACEHOLDER(77) goes', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14: src/meshes.lisp (GPU part: ship-gpu, ship-slot, ship-uniforms!, earth-lit-cap, encode-ship), src/shaders.lisp (ship-mesh-vertex, ship-instanced-vertex, ship-fragment), src/render.lisp (render-state ship-emissive and ship-lights-on, the ship slot, encode-ship after the impostors), src/post.lisp (ship term from ship-bounding-radius; *ship-bounding-radius* gone), src/overlay.lisp (label PLACEHOLDER(80)), tests/meshes.lisp, tests/render.lisp, AGENTS.md and docs. scripts/test 4,483 passed, 13.0 s wall (measured). scripts/screenshot shows the Mule from the default outside view (truss, gold LH2 and silver LOX tanks, white cab), label PLACEHOLDER(80) only. Live checks with ./sly play: a radial-out hold turns the ship; (setf (aref *ship-materials* 3 ...)) turned the cab red on the next frame; at u = 180 deg the hull is dark. Deviations: the lit-ship GPU check runs at u = 60 deg with the ship turned (at the start the Sun is 25 deg from the zenith, so a camera with the Sun behind always sees Earth); the decal checks turn the ship so the decal faces 70 deg from the Sun (the letters stay below 60 with bloom); earthshine uses the lit share of the visible cap (decision 99: Earthshine from the lit part of the visible cap), since the whole-disc phase lit the hull at the middle of the night pass. Older GPU checks'' cameras at the ship move 50 m forward. Overdraw not measured. The hidden-window live image draws at ~1 fps with or without the ship (presentation throttle, not the hull).', 'Piece 2 of `plan 18: The Mule''s meshes`: everything its section "2. `meshes.lisp`, part two" lists (`decision 80: The Mule''s meshes in numbers: geometry, draws, materials and lights`, `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`, `decision 79: Sunlight at a point and the sunlit ship in the exposure rule`, `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`; `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision" item 3, "GPU tests"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Instancing many objects", "Other findings"). Needs `task 116: meshes.lisp part one: generators, the Mule''s parts, the decal and the bounding radius`, `task 109: render.lisp, overlay.lisp, main.lisp, capture.lisp: the frame runs the clock, the skeleton goes`, `task 111: post.lisp: HDR target, bloom, tone map, exposure` and `task 115: impostors.lisp part two: Earth, its atmosphere rim and halo; PLACEHOLDER(76) goes` (impostors drawn before the ship; `sun-fraction` in the render state).

- Renderer: baked hull and engine in static vertex buffers; unit primitives and instance groups in static buffers (`:step-mode :instance`); the decal through `texture-from-pixels`; made once, destroyed by `destroy-renderer`.
- Shaders in `shaders.lisp`, live pipelines `:ship-mesh` and `:ship-instanced`: rotation by the draw''s mat3 (`mat3-from-quat` of the interpolated q, never accumulated), the engine also by its gimbal rotation through the gimbal point; translation `eye-relative-single` of r − q c; `camera-clip-rows!`; one shared fragment function: material table (`*ship-materials*`, a defparameter uploaded each frame), weld darkening, foil noise normals, throat band, decal over white paint, red hatch outline, window and porthole glass; sun term, earthshine and ambient of `decision 80` with `sun-fraction`.
- `(encode-ship pass renderer render-state camera)` in the scene pass after the impostors, before the ribbons: opaque, depth written, compare `:greater`; three draws (hull, instances, engine); per-draw uniforms through `canvas-frame-resource-cache`; per-frame emissive colour (default zero) and lights-on (default on) slots.
- `post.lisp`: the exposure''s ship term uses `ship-bounding-radius` at the render state''s m_p; `*ship-bounding-radius*` goes.
- `PLACEHOLDER(77)` leaves the code, the on-screen label, `AGENTS.md` and `docs/`.
- Tests `tests/render.lisp` (GPU, in the one shared `with-capture-game`, 320×200), as the plan lists them: the lit white cab against a dark background with the pixel-count bounds from the first measured frame (in a comment); the registration on +y and −y (darkest < 60, brightest > 150); the dark hull in Earth''s shadow (u = 180°); `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "How they look" (parts and materials as built), "Views" (the computed bounding radius); `docs/architecture.md` "Rendering precision" item 3, "GPU tests"; `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Instancing many objects" (what ran, the counts, on lavapipe); `docs/luv-wishlist.md` mesh primitives (naming `meshes.lisp` and its size in lines), back-face culling''s item with the overdraw if measured; `AGENTS.md` "Layout".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes in under ~15 s (measured, in the done note); `scripts/screenshot` shows the Mule from the default outside view (truss, gold and silver tanks, white cab) with no label for 77; with `./sly play` the ship turns with the rotation keys or a hold without jitter against Earth; a re-evaluated `(setf (aref *ship-materials* …))` or the fragment shader shows on the next frame; `./sly screenshot` at night shows the hull dark.', '2026-10-14T23:00:33Z', '2026-10-15T03:00:18Z', 87, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (118, 18, 'meshes.lisp part three: navigation lights, strobe and engine glow', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/meshes.lisp, src/shaders.lisp, src/render.lisp, src/main.lisp, tests/meshes.lisp, tests/render.lisp, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md. :ship-glow pipeline (additive Gaussian billboards, depth tested, not written), ship-glows!, strobe-on-p, engine-glow-radiance, engine-exit-position; render-state lights-t (real time while the clock runs) per decision 100: The lights'' clock and the glows'' numbers, which partly supersedes decision 80 (radiances 5 / 20 / 0.1, lights on brackets at (15, +-1.95, -1.95), strobe radius 0.05) after measuring blobs at the deep exposure. scripts/test 4517 passed in 12.8 s (measured). Live (./sly play, x100 through a night pass): hull dark, red and green steady, strobe blinking: /tmp/t118-shots/t118-night-2.png; engine glow with *engine-glow-radiance* 5.0 and full throttle: /tmp/t118-shots/t118-engine-glow-5.png (sunlit), default 0.1 at night: /tmp/t118-shots/t118-engine-glow-night-default.png; scripts/screenshot: /tmp/t118-shots/t118-start.png.', 'Piece 3 of `plan 18: The Mule''s meshes` (the "should" row "Engine glow; navigation lights and strobe" of `docs/design.md` "Feature list"): everything its section "3. Lights and engine glow" lists, with the positions, radii, radiances and timings of `decision 80: The Mule''s meshes in numbers: geometry, draws, materials and lights` (`docs/architecture.md` "Floating-origin pitfalls" for the strobe phase). Needs `task 117: meshes.lisp part two: the Mule drawn and lit; PLACEHOLDER(77) goes`, `task 101: controls.lisp: control state, the RCS mixer, direct mode, translation and flight-step!` (throttle) and `task 104: hazards.lisp: the swept crash test against Earth and the Moon, and death` (the loss).

- Live pipeline `:ship-glow` (shader in `shaders.lisp`): camera-facing Gaussian billboards, additive (premultiplied, alpha 0), depth-tested without depth write, after the hull in the scene pass; per instance the eye-relative centre (single), world radius, at least 1.5 px across with the radiance scaled down by the area ratio when enlarged, RGB radiance.
- Lights from the model''s light positions turned by q and placed from R: red (−y), green (+y), steady; the strobe on the cab top, `(strobe-on-p t)` with `*strobe-on*` / `*strobe-period*`, the phase reduced in double on the CPU; none while the lights-on slot is off.
- `(engine-glow-radiance render-state)`: `*engine-glow-radiance*` × throttle while the engine fires (throttle > 0, propellant > 0, not lost), else 0; the billboard at the nozzle exit''s centre after the trim rotation; bloom spreads it.
- Tests `tests/meshes.lisp`: `strobe-on-p` at 0.05 / 0.5 s and at 2^30 + 0.05 / 2^30 + 0.5 s; `engine-glow-radiance` 0 at throttle 0, with empty tanks, after a loss, proportional to the throttle from 0.1 to 1.0 within 1e-12.
- Tests `tests/render.lisp` (the shared capture), as the plan lists them: red and green light pixels in Earth''s shadow; the strobe on against off (`*strobe-on*` bound to the period and to 0.0); the nozzle exit from 30 m behind on −x, in shadow, bluer and brighter by > 20 at throttle 1.0 than at 0; `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "How they look" (lights and glow as built; the grapple''s floodlight and range-finder light in `milestone 3`); `docs/architecture.md` "GPU tests".

Done when: `scripts/test` passes in under ~15 s (measured, in the done note); with `./sly play` at ×100 through a night pass the hull goes dark and the red, green and blinking white lights stay; `(setf *engine-glow-radiance* 5.0)` with full throttle shows a blue glow at the nozzle on the next frame (a screenshot''s path in the done note).', '2026-10-14T23:00:33Z', '2026-10-15T03:14:13Z', 87, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (119, 19, 'input.lisp part one: the shared held-key map, the event path, taps, focus and quit', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/controls.lisp (*flight-keys*, controls-apply-held-keys!), src/input.lisp (new), src/main.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, tests/input.lisp (new), docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md', 'Piece 1 of `plan 19: Input and the outside view`. Builds on `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer` (`controls-set-rotation-key`, `controls-set-translation-key`), `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events` (`clock-frame!`) and `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets` (`main.lisp`''s `draw` and `handle-event`). Binding: `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`, `decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer`.

## What
- `src/controls.lisp` (stays a simulation file: no HAL, SDL, `*game*`): `*flight-keys*` as data (key, rotation or translation, axis, sign): W/S pitch −/+, A/D yaw −/+, Q/E roll −/+, H/N +x/−x, I/K −z/+z, J/L −y/+y. `(controls-apply-held-keys! controls keys)`: from a list of held key names sets each rotation and translation key state to the sum of its keys'' signs (opposite keys cancel) through `controls-set-rotation-key` / `controls-set-translation-key`, calling them only on a change, so their rules (a pitch or yaw key releases a hold; a roll key turns the hold''s roll) apply only then. `plan 22: Flight scripts and the Done when`''s `(:keys …)` will call it.
- `src/input.lisp` (new; after `render.lisp`, before `main.lisp`, in `luv-in-space.asd`): an `input` struct (held keys, keys pressed since the last frame, keys released since the last frame, right-drag flag, pointer deltas and wheel notches summed since the last frame; the latter three are used by piece 3) in a `game` slot `input` with an `:initform` (not in the `sim`).
- `(handle-event game event)` moved from `main.lisp` (its lambda keeps calling it by name): key press, not repeat (`canvas-key-event-repeat-p`), adds the key to held and pressed; release removes it from held and records it; `canvas-window-focus-lost-event` clears held, pressed and drag and leaves relative pointer mode (only when the game has a canvas); Escape, Control+Q (`:q` with `:control` in `canvas-key-event-modifiers`) and `canvas-window-close-request-event` set `game-quit-requested-p`.
- `(input-frame! game elapsed)`, called by `draw` before `clock-frame!`: held keys plus the keys pressed and released since the last frame (tap latch: a press and release between two frames is held for this frame) go to `controls-apply-held-keys!` on `(sim-controls (game-sim game))`; then the latches clear.
- Key names: check them against `sdl-scancode-key-name` in `../luv/hal/sdl/canvas.lisp` (letters, digits, `:shift-left`, `:control-left`, `:|.|`, `:|,|`, `:/`, `:page-up`, `:home`, `:escape`) and use exactly what it returns.

## Tests: `tests/input.lisp` (new; after `tests/render.lisp`, before `tests/capture.lisp`)
- A game from `(new-game-sim)` with a clock, no canvas, no renderer; a helper making key events with `make-instance` of luv''s event classes.
- W pressed, one `input-frame!`: pitch −1 and the start''s prograde hold released to rate damping; W released, next frame: pitch 0. W and S held: 0. Each of the twelve flight keys moves its axis with its sign.
- Tap: W pressed and released before one `input-frame!`: pitch −1 that frame, 0 at the next.
- A repeat press changes nothing; a release without a press changes nothing.
- Focus loss with W, H held: next frame every rotation and translation key 0; throttle unchanged.
- Escape, Control+Q and the close request each set the quit flag; Q alone does not.
- `controls-apply-held-keys!` with `(:a :d :q)`: yaw 0, roll −1 (no input or game).

## Docs
- `docs/design.md` "Controls": a bullet on the tap latch and the per-frame sample.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order": `controls.lisp` also holds the held-key map, `input.lisp` the input state and `handle-event`; "The clock": input writes `controls` once per frame before the steps.
- `AGENTS.md` "Layout" if it lists `src/` files.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` and `scripts/screenshot` pass.
- With `./sly start`, `./sly play`: holding W turns the ship and releasing stops it, or without a human `./sly eval` of `handle-event` with a synthetic W press, two frames later `(controls … pitch)` is −1; Escape and Control+Q close the window; then `./sly stop-playing`, `./sly stop`. No process left running.', '2026-10-14T23:01:46Z', '2026-10-15T03:18:29Z', 88, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (120, 19, 'input.lisp part two: the key map''s commands, the throttle ramp, gating and the window title', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/input.lisp (*key-map*, run-command, gating, throttle ramp, window-title), src/main.lisp (game-view, title), tests/input.lisp, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md, AGENTS.md; ran scripts/test (4647 passed), scripts/screenshot, nix run (title shown, killed by PID), ./sly play with synthetic . . P → (10 T)', 'Piece 2 of `plan 19: Input and the outside view`; after its piece 1 (`input.lisp part one`). Binding: `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 88: Warp keys while paused`, `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`, `decision 31: Warp choices within the time-warp rules` ("RCS OFF ABOVE ×4"), `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering`. Commands from `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer` (`controls-…`) and `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events` (`clock-warp-up` / `-down` / `-reset`, `clock-toggle-pause`, `clock-kinematic-p`, clock messages); use their actual names in `src/`.

## What
- `*key-map*` in `src/input.lisp`, a `defparameter` list of (key . command), so `./sly eval` rebinding works on the next press: F `controls-toggle-fine`; Z `controls-throttle-full`, X `controls-throttle-cut`; T `controls-toggle-rate-damping`; R `controls-inertial-hold`; 1–6 `controls-set-hold` prograde, retrograde, normal, anti-normal, radial out, radial in; `.` `clock-warp-up`, `,` `clock-warp-down`, `/` `clock-warp-reset`; P `clock-toggle-pause`; M, Tab, Page-up, Page-down: commands `:map`, `:map-focus`, `:map-zoom-in`, `:map-zoom-out` whose handlers do nothing yet, marked `PLACEHOLDER(79)` (`plan 20: The basic map` replaces them). C and Home are piece 3''s. A `game-view` slot (`:outside`; the map''s plan adds `:map`). Discrete commands run at the press, in `handle-event`; refusals and lowering are the clock''s, which writes their messages.
- Throttle ramp in `input-frame!`: Shift-left held raises the lever by `*throttle-ramp-rate*` 0.5 × min(elapsed, 0.1 s) up to 1.0, a press from off giving 0.1; Control-left held lowers it by the same, below 0.1 off (`controls-set-throttle`''s rule). Control+Q moves the lever by at most one frame''s ramp. Tunables `defparameter`s citing `decision 81`.
- Gating: paused, flight keys (held map, F, Z, X, T, R, 1–6, Shift, Control) are ignored and the ramp stops, while P, `.`, `,`, `/`, C, Home, M, Tab, Page keys, the mouse and quit act (`decision 88`); above ×4 (`clock-kinematic-p`) held rotation and translation keys are ignored (`controls-apply-held-keys!` sees none) and each press writes the clock''s message "RCS OFF ABOVE ×4" once, while holds, T, R, F and the throttle act; lost (`sim-lost-p` or its actual name) every flight key is ignored (`plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel` binds Return and N).
- `(window-title)`, pure, given to `make-sdl-canvas` in `main.lisp`: "Luv in Space · WASD QE turn · HN IK JL move · Shift/Ctrl throttle · Z/X full/cut · T damp · R 1–6 hold · F fine · . , / warp · P pause · C camera · M map · Esc quit".

## Tests: `tests/input.lisp`
- Throttle: Shift from off: 0.1 after the first frame; held 60 more frames of 1/60 s: 0.6 within 1e-9; frames of 1/144 s over the same second give the same within 1e-9; one frame of 0.5 s adds 0.05 (cap); Control held from 0.15 for 0.2 s gives 0; Z gives 1.0, X 0.
- Commands: 1 engages prograde, 1 again releases to rate damping; 5 radial out; R an inertial hold at the current attitude; T from rate damping gives direct; F toggles fine; `.` twice gives ×10 (coasting start at the prograde hold, not refused), `/` gives ×1; P pauses and P resumes the level.
- Gating: paused, W, 1 and Shift change nothing and the ramp stops, P and `.` still act; at ×10 W changes no key state, the hold stays, one "RCS OFF ABOVE ×4" message per press; at ×10 the throttle ramps and 2 changes the hold; lost, every flight key is ignored.
- Title: names every key of the milestone-2 table that `*key-map*` binds.

## Docs
- `docs/design.md` "Controls": what is ignored while paused, lost and above ×4; the title''s text.
- `AGENTS.md` "Commands" → Run: Escape or Control+Q quits, the title lists the keys.
- `docs/luv-wishlist.md`: a key-name → layout-character function exported by luv''s canvas; the workaround here (QWERTY names). Also `docs/luv-capabilities.md` if it lists the gap.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` and `scripts/screenshot` pass.
- `nix run` shows the title with the keys (close the window by PID).
- In `./sly play`, `./sly eval` of synthetic presses (`.`, `.`, `P`) changes the clock''s level and pause; `./sly stop-playing`, `./sly stop`; no process left.', '2026-10-14T23:01:46Z', '2026-10-15T03:23:55Z', 88, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (121, 19, 'camera.lisp: the outside view''s orbit camera with C, Home, wheel and right-drag', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/camera.lisp (outside-view: frames, C, Home, drag, wheel, eased distance, outside-min-distance), src/input.lisp (right-drag, motion, wheel, C/Home keys, title), src/main.lisp (outside-view slot, outside-camera-update! with elapsed, captures snap), tests/camera.lisp, tests/input.lisp, tests/post.lisp, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md', 'Piece 3 of `plan 19: Input and the outside view`; after its pieces 1 and 2 (`input.lisp part one` / `part two`). Binding: `decision 82: Outside view camera: angles in a frame, toggles that keep the picture, distance and easing` (with its sign correction: az −= 0.25° per px of dx), `decision 30: Views and cameras`, `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`. Builds on `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets` (`camera` struct, `outside-camera-default!`, `render-state`) and `plan 18: The Mule''s meshes` / `ship.lisp`''s parts table.

## What
- `src/camera.lisp`: `outside-view` struct (frame `:orbital` / `:locked`, azimuth, elevation, distance, target distance) in a `game` slot `outside-view` with an `:initform` (not in the sim; kept across a restart). `(new-outside-view)` = az 180°, el 20°, 40 m, `:orbital`, replacing `outside-camera-default!` and `*outside-distance*` / `*outside-elevation*` (update their callers, `capture.lisp` included).
- `(outside-frame-basis! out view render-state)`: `:orbital` x prograde, z radial in, y completing FRD, from the interpolated r, v; `:locked` the body axes from the interpolated q.
- `(outside-camera-update! camera view render-state elapsed)`: eases distance to the target in log with τ `*outside-zoom-tau*` 0.15 s (snaps when elapsed is nil, as captures do); offset = distance × (cos el cos az, cos el sin az, −sin el) in that basis (double, ICRF), anchored at the CoM; looking at the CoM with the frame''s +z as down; 50° vertical FOV. Conses nothing.
- `(outside-min-distance m-p)`: 1.2 × the largest distance from the CoM (`ship-mass-properties`) to a corner of a part''s box in the parts table; the wheel''s range [min, 5 km].
- `(outside-view-toggle-frame! view render-state)` (C): eye direction re-expressed in the other frame''s az, el, eye offset unchanged; `(outside-view-reset! view)` (Home); `(outside-view-drag! view dx dy)`: az −= 0.25° dx, el −= 0.25° dy, el clamped ±85°; `(outside-view-zoom! view notches m-p)`: target × 1.2^(−notches), clamped. Tunables (0.25°/px, ×1.2, τ, ±85°, 5 km) `defparameter`s citing `decision 82`.
- `src/input.lisp`: right button press sets the drag flag and relative pointer mode (only with a canvas), release clears both; motion deltas while dragging and wheel notches summed per event and applied in `input-frame!` to the outside view when `game-view` is `:outside`; C and Home in `*key-map*`; all act while paused and above ×4.
- `main.lisp`''s `draw` calls `outside-camera-update!` with the frame''s elapsed real time after the render state; `capture.lisp` snaps (elapsed nil).

## Tests
- `tests/camera.lisp` (new; add to `luv-in-space/tests` in its load order per `docs/architecture.md`):
  - Default equals part 4''s former default pose (eye offset within 1e-9 m, look direction within 1e-12 rad); looks at the CoM within 1e-12 rad for 20 random az, el, distances in both frames.
  - Orbital: over a quarter of the start orbit (render states from `orbit-state`), the eye stays at az 180°, el 20° in the orbital frame and the view''s up (−z) stays within 1e-12 rad of the plane of radial out and the view axis. Locked: ship rotated 90° about body z, the eye offset turns with it within 1e-12 rad.
  - C: toggling at the start and after a 30° yaw keeps eye offset within 1e-9 m and orientation within 1e-12 rad; twice restores az, el within 1e-12.
  - Drag: dx 40 px → az −10°; dy −400 px → el 85°; from az 180°, mouse right makes the eye''s y component positive, mouse up raises it.
  - Wheel: one notch up from 40 m → 33.33 m; 100 up stop at `outside-min-distance` (≥ 12 m, eye outside every part''s box at every az, el on a 10° grid); 100 down stop at 5,000 m; after τ the log-distance has gone 1 − 1/e of the way within 1e-12; nil elapsed snaps.
  - `outside-min-distance` at wet, half and dry m_p; the measured numbers in the test''s comment and in `docs/design.md` "Views".
- `tests/input.lisp`: right press, motion (8, 0) and (−4, 0), release, one frame: az −1°; motion without the button does nothing; focus loss during a drag ends it; wheel 2 notches: target 40 / 1.44 m; C and Home act while paused.

## Docs
- `docs/design.md` "Views" → Outside: drag sense and rate, eased wheel, C keeping the picture, the measured minimum distance (replacing "12 m"), `decision 82`.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Frames" → camera: the outside view as angles in the orbital or body frame; "Files in load order": `camera.lisp` holds the outside view, `tests/camera.lisp`.
- `AGENTS.md` "Layout" if affected.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` passes; `scripts/screenshot` unchanged (the default pose).
- With `./sly play`: screenshots after `./sly eval` of a synthetic C press with the ship turned, of 10 wheel notches out and of a Home press show the expected views (looked at, then deleted); `./sly status` healthy; image stopped, no process left.', '2026-10-14T23:01:46Z', '2026-10-15T03:30:53Z', 88, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (122, 20, 'camera.lisp: the map view and map camera, framing, focus, zoom, drag and Home', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/camera.lisp, src/main.lisp, src/render.lisp, src/post.lisp, tests/camera.lisp, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md; scripts/test 5505 passed, scripts/screenshot outside view unchanged', 'Piece 1, first half, of `plan 20: The basic map`: the pure map camera. Runs after the tasks of `plan 19: Input and the outside view` (`camera.lisp`''s outside view, `game-view`, `input-frame!`''s drag and wheel deltas). Binding: `decision 83: Map camera: framing on opening, focus, zoom, drag and exposure`, `decision 82: Outside view camera: angles in a frame, toggles that keep the picture, distance and easing` (drag signs, log easing), `decision 30: Views and cameras`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`.

## What
- `src/camera.lisp`: `map-view` struct: focus `:earth` / `:ship`, basis e1, e2, n (double vec3s), azimuth, elevation, distance, target distance; lives in a `game` slot `map-view` with an `:initform` (not in the sim, not in checkpoints; kept across a restart).
- `(map-view-open! view render-state)`: n = unit r × v, e1 = unit r, e2 = n × e1 (n = ICRF z when |r × v| < 1e-9 |r||v|); focus `:earth`, az −45°, el 30°, distance = target = 2.5 × max(apoapsis radius, |r|) (`|r|` on a hyperbola; `state->orbit` with μ⊕), clamped. Home calls it again.
- `(map-view-cycle-focus! view)`: `:earth` ↔ `:ship`, keeping basis, az, el, distance, clamped to `(map-min-distance focus)` (50 m ship, 1.2 R⊕ Earth) and `*map-max-distance*` 1.5×10^13 m.
- `(map-view-zoom! view factor)`: target × factor, clamped (wheel 1.2^(−notches), Page-up 1/10, Page-down 10).
- `(map-view-drag! view dx dy)`: az −= 0.25° dx, el −= 0.25° dy, el clamped ±85°.
- `(map-camera-update! camera view render-state elapsed)`: log easing of the distance, τ `*map-zoom-tau*` 0.15 s (snap when elapsed is nil); anchor `:earth` or `:ship`; offset = distance × (cos el cos az e1 + cos el sin az e2 + sin el n); looks at the focus with n''s projection as up; vertical FOV `*map-fov*` 50°. Conses nothing.
- Tunables `defparameter`s citing `decision 83`.

## Tests `tests/camera.lisp` (CPU; render states from `orbit-state` of the start orbit and a 400 × 2,000 km test orbit)
- Opening: looks at Earth''s centre within 1e-12 rad; eye''s angle above the orbit plane 30° within 1e-12 rad, eye · n > 0; distance 2.5 Q within 1e-9 relative; the ship''s point not behind Earth (eye-to-ship segment misses the sphere) at u = 0°, 90°, 180°, 270° of the start orbit; a hyperbola (e = 1.5) opens at 2.5 |r|.
- Frame stays: render states over a quarter orbit after opening leave the eye offset unchanged bit for bit.
- Tab: `:ship` keeps az, el, distance and looks at the ship within 1e-12 rad; Tab again `:earth`; from a 20 m target the switch to Earth clamps to 1.2 R⊕.
- Zoom: one notch up from 10,000 km → 8,333.3 km; Page-up from 10,000 km → 1,000 km, clamped to 7,654 km with Earth focus; 200 notches down stop at 1.5×10^13 m; ship focus 100 notches up stop at 50 m; after τ 1 − 1/e of the way in log within 1e-12; nil elapsed snaps; the ~80 notches from 1.2 R⊕ to 1.5×10^13 m (log(1.5e13 / 7.654e6) / log 1.2 ≈ 79.5).
- Drag: dx 40 px → az −10°; dy −400 px → el 85°; Home restores az −45°, el 30° and the opening distance.
- Precision: at 1.5×10^13 m from Earth the eye-relative single of Earth''s centre equals the double difference within 1e-6 relative; at ship focus 50 m the ship''s eye-relative single within 1e-4 m of the double one.
- `map-camera-update!` over 1,000 frames conses nothing.

## Docs
- `docs/design.md` "Views" → Map: opening focus Earth (resolving "the ship (default when the map opens)"), az −45°, 50° FOV, Tab keeps the angles, Home re-frames (`decision 83`).
- `docs/architecture.md` "Frames" → camera: the map camera as angles in a basis fixed at opening, anchored on Earth or the ship; "Files in load order": `camera.lisp` holds the map view.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` and `scripts/screenshot` pass (the outside view unchanged).', '2026-10-14T23:03:07Z', '2026-10-15T03:35:33Z', 89, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (123, 20, 'The map view wired in: M, Tab, Page keys, wheel, drag, Home, the map exposure and capture-state :view :map', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/input.lisp (M toggles game-view and frames the map, Tab/Page keys/Home in :map, C ignored there, drag and wheel to the map view; PLACEHOLDER(79) gone), src/camera.lisp (*map-zoom-step*, *map-page-factor*), src/post.lisp (*exposure-map* 4.0), src/main.lisp (view-changed-p, update-view! by view, exposure snaps on a view change, encode-frame gets the view), src/render.lisp (encode-frame''s optional view, unused until task 125), src/capture.lisp (capture-state/capture-game-state :view), tests input/post/render, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md. scripts/test 5546 passed, scripts/screenshot ok. Live: M shows Earth whole at the centre with stars; Tab + 30 notches gives ship focus at 71 km where the 15 m ship is below a pixel, 30 more (300 m) show it at the centre (the ship''s marker is task 127); Page-down x1 from the opening shows Earth as a ~80 px disc, x6 (100 AU) leaves it below a pixel (task 127''s 6 px body markers). Bright ice saturates at exposure 4 (land 0.3 stays at 236/255 as decision 83 expects). Screenshots deleted, image stopped.', 'Piece 1, second half, of `plan 20: The basic map`; after the task "camera.lisp: the map view and map camera, framing, focus, zoom, drag and Home". Binding: `decision 83: Map camera: framing on opening, focus, zoom, drag and exposure`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`, `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 78: Sky in numbers: stars, Sun, Moon and Earth''s look` (the star radiance L(m)).

## What
- `src/input.lisp`: `:map` toggles `game-view` `:outside` ↔ `:map` (opening calls `map-view-open!`; leaving keeps the outside view as it was); `:map-focus` (Tab), `:map-zoom-in` / `:map-zoom-out` (Page-up / Page-down) act in `:map` only; Home in `:map` calls `map-view-open!`; C does nothing in `:map`; `input-frame!` sends drag deltas and wheel notches to the map view in `:map`; all act while paused, above ×4 and lost; remove `PLACEHOLDER(79)` from the handlers. A `view-changed` flag set on the toggle, read by the frame.
- `src/post.lisp`: `*exposure-map*` 4.0 (`decision 83`); `exposure-target` takes the view and in `:map` returns `*exposure-map*` whatever the camera sees; the exposure snaps to the map''s on entering and to the outside target on leaving (the `view-changed` flag).
- `src/main.lisp`: `draw` calls `map-camera-update!` in `:map`, `outside-camera-update!` in `:outside`, passes the view to `exposure-target` and `encode-frame`.
- `src/capture.lisp`: `capture-state` takes `:view` (`:outside` default, `:map`), opening the map view on the captured state (snapped); `camera-fn` still overrides the pose (for `plan 22: Flight scripts and the Done when`''s map screenshots).

## Tests
- `tests/input.lisp`: M from `:outside` → `:map`, M again → `:outside` with the outside view unchanged bit for bit; Tab, Page keys and a drag act in `:map` and not in `:outside` (Page keys), a drag in `:map` leaves the outside view; wheel 2 notches in `:map`: target / 1.44; C in `:map` changes nothing; M, Tab, Page keys act while paused and lost.
- `tests/post.lisp`: `exposure-target` in `:map` is `*exposure-map*`; entering snaps to 4.0, leaving snaps to the outside target; through `tone-map-srgb` at `*exposure-map*`: a magnitude 2.0 star''s peak radiance ≥ 30 of 255, a radiance-0.3 surface ≤ 240 of 255.
- `tests/render.lisp` (GPU, the shared `with-capture-game`, 320×200, `:view :map` on the start state): Earth''s disc in the centre (centre pixel above background by a margin), corners at background, frame neither black nor white-out; `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0.

## Docs
