- `./sly start`, `./sly play`, `./sly eval` of a synthetic M press, `./sly screenshot /tmp/map.png`: Earth whole at the centre, stars around; Tab plus 30 wheel notches up show the ship close; Page-down ×6 shows Earth as a small disc. Screenshots looked at, then deleted; `./sly stop-playing`, `./sly stop`, no process left.', '2026-10-14T23:03:07Z', '2026-10-15T03:40:10Z', 89, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (124, 20, 'ribbons.lisp: osculating orbit points with adaptive splitting and the per-segment instances', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/ribbons.lisp, tests/ribbons.lisp, src/orbits.lisp (perifocal-axes!), luv-in-space.asd, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md. Start orbit: 256 segments at the opening frame, 794 at ship focus 50 m; the splitting test aims a camera at each midpoint in front of the eye (the 50 m frame is ~75 m wide, pieces near the ship ~650 m, so no midpoint falls inside the frame). Notes for task 125 added to its body (instance layout, state->orbit consing).', 'Piece 2, CPU half, of `plan 20: The basic map`; after the map camera tasks of this plan. Binding: `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility`, `decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 34: How death works` (crash radius R⊕ + 100 km in `bodies.lisp`), `decision 12: Module layout and package split`.

## What
- `src/ribbons.lisp` (new; after `meshes.lisp`, before `post.lisp`; add to both systems in `luv-in-space.asd`).
- `(orbit-ribbon-points! buffer orbit eye-rel-body focal-px)`: orbit from `state->orbit` of the render state''s r, v with μ⊕. Ellipse: 256 segments uniform in eccentric anomaly, points from (a (cos E − e), b sin E) rotated by the orbit''s angles in double, relative to Earth''s centre. Each segment split into 2^k pieces (k ≤ 8) so sagitta (chord² / (8 ρ), ρ the local radius of curvature) / eye distance to the segment × focal px ≤ `*ribbon-max-error-px*` 0.25; total ≤ `*ribbon-max-segments*` 8,192, lowering k from the farthest segments first. Hyperbola: H from −H_s to +H_s, H_s where r reaches Earth''s Laplace sphere radius (`bodies.lisp`), same splitting. Each point keeps its radius. Preallocated double buffer; conses nothing.
- Instances: per segment both endpoints as (point + Earth − eye) in double, then single (`eye-relative-single`), and a linear colour: cyan #40D0FF, red #FF3030 where the segment''s midpoint radius is below the crash radius. Filled into a preallocated buffer (the GPU upload is the next task).
- Tunables `defparameter`s citing `decision 84`.

## Tests `tests/ribbons.lisp` (new, after `tests/meshes.lisp`, before `tests/post.lisp`)
- On the conic: start orbit, e = 0.5, e = 0.9 and a hyperbola (e = 1.5): every point''s distance from Earth''s centre equals the conic''s radius at its anomaly within 1e-6 m.
- Splitting: map camera at ship focus 50 m (start orbit, 1280×800): every segment whose midpoint is in front of the eye has its chord midpoint within 0.5 px of the true ellipse point at the mid-anomaly, projected through `camera-clip-rows!`; Earth focus at the opening distance: 256 segments; ship focus 50 m: below 8,192 (counts in the test''s comment).
- Colour: 400 × 50 km orbit red exactly where the midpoint radius < R⊕ + 100 km, cyan elsewhere; the start orbit all cyan.
- Precision: at ship focus 50 m the eye-relative single of the point nearest the ship within 1e-3 m of the double difference, while `(- (coerce p ''single-float) (coerce eye ''single-float))` is not.
- 1,000 frames of points and instances cons nothing.

## Docs
- `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`ribbons.lisp`, `tests/ribbons.lisp` as built), "Floating-origin pitfalls" (orbit lines recomputed each frame in double relative to their body, split by pixel error, `decision 84`).
- `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Orbit lines and markers": the adaptive split with its measured segment counts replacing "assumed".

## Done when
- `scripts/test` and `scripts/screenshot` pass.', '2026-10-14T23:03:07Z', '2026-10-15T03:47:13Z', 89, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (125, 20, 'The ribbon pipeline: screen-space orbit line drawn in the map''s scene pass', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/shaders.lisp (ribbon-vertex, ribbon-fragment, role :ribbon), src/ribbons.lisp (ribbon-pipeline, ribbon-corners, make-ribbon-buffer, encode-ribbon, *ribbon-width-px*, *ribbon-radiance*), src/render.lisp (ribbon in the frame renderer, per-target instance buffer in the frame slot, screen.zw = width and radiance, draw in :map after the Mule), tests/render.lisp (ribbon-checks: 631 cyan px on the ring at 320x200, N = 315; 0 with radiance 0; 0 of 338 far-side px from el 10 deg, decision 101: Ribbon depth check from 10 degrees above the orbit plane), docs (design Views/Map, architecture files and GPU tests, luv-capabilities, luv-wishlist), AGENTS.md. scripts/test 5573 passed (~15.5 s), scripts/screenshot ok. Live: ./sly play, M shows the cyan ring; at ship focus 50 m 60 fps (vsync) with 560 segments; after hold retrograde and a 60 s full-throttle burn (periapsis -177 km) the arc below 100 km is red. state->orbit still conses per frame: follow-up task 147: Non-consing state->orbit for the map''s per-frame ribbon.', 'Piece 2, GPU half, of `plan 20: The basic map`; after the task "ribbons.lisp: osculating orbit points with adaptive splitting and the per-segment instances". Binding: `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility`, `decision 4: Depth strategy`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`, `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`. Reference: `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Orbit lines and markers" (the ribbon of run 32 in the gap-probe appendix: one instance per segment, a 6-vertex quad expanded in the vertex shader) and "Rendering" (bind groups after each `set-pipeline`, `canvas-frame-resource-cache`).

## What
- `src/shaders.lisp`: a live ribbon pipeline, role `:ribbon`: the 6-vertex quad expanded to `*ribbon-width-px*` 2.0 px through `camera-clip-rows!`''s rows; endpoints behind the eye clipped to w = near; depth compare `:greater`, no depth write, additive; radiance = colour × `*ribbon-radiance*` 1.0 / the current exposure (a uniform).
