## From task 124
- CPU side as built: `(make-ribbon)` once (e.g. in the frame renderer), then per frame in `:map` `(orbit-ribbon-points! ribbon orbit eye-rel-earth (camera-focal-px camera height))` and `(orbit-ribbon-instances! ribbon eye-rel-earth)`; `ribbon-instances` holds `ribbon-count` instances of 12 singles (`+ribbon-instance-floats+`): start x y z 1, end x y z 1, linear colour r g b 1.
- `state->orbit` conses (a struct and vec3s, a few hundred bytes a frame); the plan wants per-frame paths that cons nothing: add a non-consing `state->orbit` variant (into a preallocated orbit or its slots) or accept it and note it.', '2026-10-14T23:03:07Z', '2026-10-15T03:56:29Z', 89, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (126, 20, 'overlay.lisp: full glyph table, marker shapes and label-at!', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/overlay.lisp (full glyph table, overlay-buffer, marker-vertices!, label-at!), src/shaders.lisp (overlay fragment sRGB-encodes, quads-fragment), src/render.lisp, tests/overlay.lisp (new), tests/render.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md; scripts/test 5721 passed, scripts/screenshot ok', 'Piece 3, first half, of `plan 20: The basic map`. Binding: `decision 7: Placeholder labels: dot-matrix overlay quads`, `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility`, `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms` (the readout of `plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel` shares this glyph table and `label-at!`: build them so it can reuse them; if its task already extended the table, complete it, don''t duplicate).

