INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (127, 20, 'Map markers: ship, apsides, impact and small bodies with labels and visibility', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/ribbons.lisp (map-markers), src/overlay.lisp (place-map-labels!, map-marker-vertices!), src/render.lisp (encode-map-markers), tests/ribbons.lisp, tests/render.lisp (marker-checks), docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md; decision 103: Map labels: placement order and overlap. scripts/test 5,835 passed, 15.3 s wall (17.7 s with recompilation); scripts/screenshot passes. Checked live with ./sly: ring, AP and the ship''s ring with labels; after a 120 m/s retrograde cut the red arc and IMPACT; at 100 AU SUN and EARTH labelled either side of their dots. Screenshots deleted, image stopped.', 'Piece 3, second half, of `plan 20: The basic map`; after the ribbon tasks and "overlay.lisp: full glyph table, marker shapes and label-at!". Binding: `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility`, `decision 49: Story: names, call signs and ships` ("M-07"), `decision 34: How death works` (crash radius), `decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`.

## What
- `src/ribbons.lisp`: `(map-markers render-state camera extent)` → the frame''s markers (kind, pixel position, colour, label or nil) from a preallocated list:
  - Ship: `:ring` 12 px cyan at the interpolated r, always (even behind Earth), label "M-07".
  - Apoapsis / periapsis: `:diamond` 9 px cyan at the apsides, "AP <n> KM" / "PE <n> KM", n the altitude above R⊕ rounded to whole km (`units.lisp`); no AP on a hyperbola.
