INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (129, 21, 'readout-lines: the milestone-2 readout rows, alarms and messages as a pure function', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/overlay.lisp (readout-lines, readout-run, format-fixed/-significant/-speed/-km, mode-text, cut-text, readout colours and limits as defparameters), tests/overlay.lisp (start state, formats, alarms with flash phase, messages and cut, glyphs, consing < 16 KB), docs/design.md Instruments, docs/architecture.md overlay.lisp. Runs carry flash nil/:on/:off; value runs after a row''s first lead with a space. Live: ./sly eval of readout-lines printed the rows (WARP ×4 after a warp-up). Follow-up task 150: ACT shows ~1 s after each warp change (rate meter).', 'Piece 1 of `plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel` (read its piece 1 in full: rows, formats, colours, alarms, messages and the test list). Binding: `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms`, `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility` (the impact time is the readout''s, from the prediction), `decision 75: Prediction in milestone 2: the step function on a copy` (the `:impact` event), `decision 66: Calendar dates on the 1/64 s grid` (UTC truncated to whole seconds). Needs the glyphs and `format-duration` of the task before it in this plan.

## What
- `src/overlay.lisp`: `(readout-lines render-state clock real-time)` → a list of lines, each a list of runs (text, colour, style `:plain`/`:inverted`, flashing flag): `ALT`, `SPD`, `AP`/`PE` (`AP ESCAPE` when e ≥ 1), `THR`, `PROP`, `MODE`, `WARP` (with `ACT ×<rate>` amber "!" below 0.9 × nominal, `PAUSED`), `UTC`; alarms `! PE BELOW 100 KM` (amber) and `<EARTH|MOON> IMPACT IN <format-duration>` (red, inverted, flashing at 2 Hz of `real-time`, on in the first half of each 0.5 s); then up to `*readout-messages*` 3 of `clock-messages`, newest last, amber with "!", cut at 40 characters with "…".
- Colours (`defparameter`s citing `decision 85`): labels #8A8A80, values #E8E4D8, caution #FFB000, danger #FF3030.
- Values from the render state (interpolated, t_r); apsides via `state->orbit` with μ⊕. All strings upcased.
- `docs/design.md` "Instruments": a short bullet list after the table with the milestone-2 rows as `decision 85` lays them out (labels, units, decimals, alarms, where the impact time comes from).

## Tests (`tests/overlay.lisp`, CPU)
- All cases of the plan''s piece 1 "Tests": the start state (`ALT 400.0 KM`, `SPD 7.669 KM/S`, `AP`/`PE` 400.0, `THR 0% OFF`, `PROP 28000 KG 100%`, `MODE HOLD PROGRADE SETTLED`, `WARP ×1`, `UTC 2040-01-01 00:00:00`, no alarm, no message); the crafted formats (950 m/s, 1,000 m/s, e = 1.2, throttle 0.45 with and without propellant, rate damp + fine, paused ×1,000, actual rate 490,000 / 950,000 at ×1,000,000); the 400 × 50 km orbit''s PE alarm and, with the prediction run to completion, the impact alarm (duration = impact time − t_r, flashing on at 0.1 s, off at 0.35 s); a refused warp-up message present then gone after 3 s of the clock''s real time; a 60-character message cut to 40 with "…".
- `glyph-missing` nil for every string of every line above.
- One `readout-lines` call conses under 16 KB.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(readout-lines …)'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` on the live game (`./sly start`, `./sly play`) prints the rows; stop what you started.', '2026-10-14T23:04:59Z', '2026-10-15T04:35:17Z', 90, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (130, 21, 'Draw the readout in the overlay pass, capture-state :readout, remove PLACEHOLDER(80)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/overlay.lisp (readout-vertices!, readout-box-size, sizes, *overlay-max-vertices* 73728, placeholder label removed), src/render.lisp (encode-overlay: markers then readout in one per-slot buffer), src/main.lisp (game real-time, readout-p, start :readout), src/capture.lisp (:readout on capture-state, capture-game-state, with-capture-game), tests/overlay.lisp (readout-vertices, overlay-capacity), tests/render.lisp (readout-checks at 1280x800; render-frames at 320x200 with :readout nil, the box would cover it), AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md. scripts/test 6125 passed, 19.3 s wall. Screenshot legible top left; ./sly play + clock-warp-up twice showed WARP ×10. Frame time with the readout: 60 fps steady, readout-lines + readout-vertices! 0.057 ms/frame, 10,170 vertices. Decision 105; follow-up task 151 (captures read PAUSED).', 'Piece 2 of `plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel`. Binding: `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms` (2 px dot pitch, 12 × 22 px cells, 16 px margin, opaque #0A0C0C box; captures take `:readout`), `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure` (the overlay is after the tone map, exact colours), `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`. Needs `readout-lines` (the task before it in this plan) and `label-at!` (`plan 20: The basic map`).

## What
- `src/overlay.lisp`: `(readout-vertices! out lines x y)`: the opaque #0A0C0C box sized to the lines, each run through `label-at!`; an inverted run draws its colour block with the text in #0A0C0C; a flashing run in its off phase draws nothing. Sizes and colours `defparameter`s.
- Overlay vertex capacity a `defparameter` sized for the readout, the map''s labels and the LOST panel together; per-frame data through part 4''s frame resource cache (never a buffer the previous frame still reads); text past capacity is cut, never a crash.
- `src/render.lisp`: the overlay pass draws the readout top left in `:outside` and `:map` (`game-view`), after the map''s markers and labels, from the frame''s render state, the clock and the game''s real time (summed elapsed, kept in `main.lisp`''s game).
- The `PLACEHOLDER(76 77 80)` label loses 80 (or goes, if 76 and 77 are gone); `PLACEHOLDER(80)` removed from code, `docs/` and `AGENTS.md` (search with `rg -n ''PLACEHOLDER\(.*80''`).
- `src/capture.lisp`: `capture-state` takes `:readout` (default t). Re-run every earlier GPU test; where a region check now falls under the readout box, that test passes `:readout nil` (say so in its comment) rather than moving its bounds.
