## Done when
- `scripts/test` passes; `scripts/screenshot /tmp/r.png` shows the readout top left, legible (look at the PNG); in `./sly play`, `./sly eval` of `(clock-warp-up …)` twice shows `WARP ×10` in the next `./sly screenshot`; the frame time with the readout in the done note. Close every window and stop the image you started.', '2026-10-14T23:04:59Z', '2026-10-15T04:40:10Z', 90, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (131, 21, 'Death record, game-restart! and the orange death glow in main.lisp', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/main.lisp (death record, notice-death!, game-frame!, game-restart!, death-glow-radiance, death-glow! into the ship''s emissive slot), tests/input.lisp, tests/overlay.lisp, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md, AGENTS.md; scripts/test 6154 passed, ~19 s wall incl. nix develop; follow-up task for the glow''s saturation', 'Piece 3, first part, of `plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel`. Binding: `decision 86: Death view, LOST panel and restart in milestone 2`, `decision 34: How death works`, `decision 74: Crash test on the step''s Hermite and the death state` (the loss record), `decision 80: The Mule''s meshes in numbers: geometry, draws, materials and lights` (the ship''s per-frame emissive slot), `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`.

## What
- `src/main.lisp`: the game keeps its summed real time (if piece 2 didn''t add it), the loss last seen and the real time of the death. On the first frame with a new `sim-loss`, `game-view` becomes `:outside` with the outside view''s offset unchanged, and the death time is recorded.
- `(game-restart! game)`: `clock-restart!` with the start-state checkpoint, view `:outside`, `outside-view-reset!`, map view closed, the input''s held keys, taps and drag cleared, the death record cleared, the exposure snapped.
- `(death-glow-radiance loss seconds-since-death)` (pure): `*death-glow-radiance*` 4.0 for t ≤ 1 s, linear to 0 at 3 s, 0 after; 0 for a Moon impact. The renderer writes `*death-glow-colour*` #FF6A1A × that ÷ the current exposure into the ship''s emissive slot. Numbers `defparameter`s citing `decision 86`.
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Checkpoints": `game-restart!` is the restore the LOST panel calls; `docs/design.md` "Dying and what follows" → "What the player sees": the glow''s curve and the camera that may still be orbited.

## Tests (no GPU; `tests/input.lisp` or `tests/render.lisp`, whichever already builds a game without a canvas; `death-glow-radiance` in `tests/overlay.lisp`)
- `death-glow-radiance`: 4.0 at 0 and 1 s, 2.0 at 2 s, 0 at 3 s and 10 s within 1e-12; 0 for a Moon loss.
- A game from `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`''s deorbit state in `:map`, run through `clock-frame!` to the impact: the view becomes `:outside`, the outside view''s offset unchanged, the death time recorded.
- `game-restart!` gives a sim `equalp` to `(new-game-sim)` at ×1 unpaused, view `:outside` with the default outside camera, no held keys; 1,000 frames of 1/60 s after it equal 1,000 frames after a fresh game bit for bit.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` passes.', '2026-10-14T23:04:59Z', '2026-10-15T04:44:19Z', 90, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (132, 21, 'The LOST panel, Return and N while lost, capture-state :death-elapsed', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/overlay.lisp (lost-panel-lines, lost-panel-origin, *lost-panel-top*), src/render.lisp (encode-frame/encode-overlay draw the panel), src/main.lisp (death-elapsed slot, panel from game-loss), src/input.lisp (Return/N :restart in *key-map*, *lost-commands*), src/capture.lisp (:death-elapsed), tests/overlay.lisp, tests/input.lisp, tests/render.lisp (lost-checks: panel exact colours; glow mean R-B 12.9 at 0 s vs -19.0 at 3.5 s, margin 15), AGENTS.md, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. scripts/test passes, 17.2 s wall (19.1 s before this task, measured the same way; over ~15 s: task 153). Live: ./sly play, deorbit state at x100 to the impact showed the panel and glow; a synthetic Return restored (new-game-sim) with ALT 400.0 KM; image stopped.', 'Piece 3, second part, of `plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel`. Binding: `decision 86: Death view, LOST panel and restart in milestone 2`, `decision 34: How death works` (in milestone 2 Return and N are the same restart), `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms` (text, colours). Needs `readout-vertices!` and `game-restart!` / `death-glow-radiance` (earlier tasks of this plan).

## What
- `src/overlay.lisp`: `(lost-panel-lines loss)` (pure), in the readout''s line format: `LOST: CRASH` red inverted (steady), `<EARTH|MOON>  <UTC of the impact>`, `SPEED <as the readout''s SPD>`, `LAT <|lat|, 2 decimals>° <N|S>  LON <|lon|, 2 decimals>° <E|W>`, a blank line, `RETURN  RESTART FROM START`, `N       NEW GAME` (keys #E8E4D8, texts #8A8A80). Drawn on an opaque #0A0C0C box centred horizontally, top at `*lost-panel-top*` 0.6 of the height; the readout stays.
- `src/input.lisp`: `*key-map*` binds `:return` and `:n` to `:restart` while `sim-lost-p` (N stays translate-back otherwise; flight keys ignored while lost); `:restart` calls `game-restart!`. M, the mouse and quit still act.
- `src/capture.lisp`: `capture-state` of a lost sim draws the glow at `:death-elapsed` (default 0, the peak) and the panel.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "Dying and what follows" → "What the player sees" (the panel''s lines and place, Return and N in milestone 2) and "Controls" (Return and N while lost); `AGENTS.md` "Commands" → Run: after a crash, Return or N restarts; `docs/architecture.md` "GPU tests" (`:death-elapsed`).

## Tests
