INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (136, 22, 'Live fly: the flight in the game, flight-status, flight-stop and input gating', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/flights.lisp (fly, flight-status, flight-stop, flight-running-p, flight-install!, flight-hook!, flight-frame!, the flight''s restart slot), src/main.lisp (game flight slot, game-restart! with a checkpoint, flight-frame! in game-frame!, call-in-game), src/input.lisp (gating while a flight runs), tests/flights.lisp (flights-live-frames: burn by clock-frame! at 1/60 s and irregular frames equals run-flight, 0.10 s), tests/input.lisp (input-gating-flight), AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md; decision 109: Live fly: the restart at once, Return and N ignored, the record in ./sly log. scripts/test passes (6,359 checks, 15.3 s wall with the dev shell). Live: ./sly play, (fly "burn"), ./sly screenshot at T+16 s shows THR 100% ON and the engine; (flight-status) at the end lists the burn (28.400 m/s) and END PASSED, also in ./sly log; (fly "deorbit") live passed through the crash, the restart and :start-state. ./sly stop, no window left.', 'Piece 3, first part, of `plan 22: Flight scripts and the Done when` (read its "Rules for every piece" and piece 3). Binding: `decision 87: Flight scripts in milestone 2: additions, apsis conditions, live fly and scripts/fly` (live `fly`, keys ignored while a flight runs), `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 86: Death view, LOST panel and restart in milestone 2` (`game-restart!`), `decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`. Spec: `docs/architecture.md` "Running scripts" (headless and live take the same states bit for bit), "Dev loop". Needs `run-flight` and the three scripts (earlier tasks of this plan).

## What
- `src/flights.lisp`: `(fly name &key (game *game*))`: restores the game to the script''s start state as `game-restart!` does, sets the view outside, keeps the `flight` in a new `flight` slot of `game` (`:initform nil`), installs the clock hook (a lambda calling `flight-step-hook`), returns at once. The script runs frame by frame through `clock-frame!` → `clock-step!`, the same steps as headless. At its end or a failure the hook is removed and the record lines printed to the image''s output. `(flight-status &key (game *game*))` → the record lines so far; `(flight-stop &key (game *game*))` removes the hook and clears the slot. `(:restart)` live calls `game-restart!`. No HAL or SDL calls in `flights.lisp`.
- `src/input.lisp`: while the game has a running flight, `input-frame!` writes no held keys and runs no throttle ramp; flight keys and warp keys are ignored (as when lost); P, C, Home, M, Tab, Page keys, the mouse and quit act.

## Tests
- `tests/flights.lisp` (CPU): `burn` flown through `clock-frame!` with a game-less clock fed simulated frames of 1/60 s, and again with a fixed list of irregular elapsed times, gives the same end sim (`equalp`) and record as `run-flight`.
- `tests/input.lisp`: with a flight running, W and Shift change no control; M still toggles the view.

## Docs
- `AGENTS.md` "Commands" → "Live image": `./sly eval ''(fly "raise-orbit")'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE`, `(flight-status)`, `(flight-stop)`, flight and warp keys ignored while a flight runs. `docs/architecture.md` "Running scripts": live `fly` as built.

## Done when
- `scripts/test` passes; in `./sly start` / `./sly play`, `./sly eval ''(fly "burn")'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` and a `./sly screenshot` during the burn show the engine on and `THR 100% ON`, and `(flight-status)` prints the record at the end; `./sly stop`, no window left open.', '2026-10-14T23:07:01Z', '2026-10-15T05:36:44Z', 91, 0);
