INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (193, 24, 'The contact drop-out of time warp', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/prediction.lisp, src/clock.lisp, tests/prediction.lisp, tests/overlay.lisp, docs/architecture.md; decision 141: The contact drop-out in the prediction: per step, the copy''s contact death, the checkpoint check', 'Piece 7 of `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling` (read "The contact drop-out"). Needs `task 189: Contact: detection, bounce and death` (the broad phase) and the berth/latch/exclusion states of `task 190: Capture, the stack and berthing` and `task 191: Release, propellant transfer and the berth checkpoint`. Files: `src/prediction.lisp`, `src/clock.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## What (`decision 43: Warp drop-outs for contact and life support`, `decision 113: Grapple and contact details the design leaves open`)
- After each step of its copy the prediction finds the first time the stack''s and a promoted object''s bounding spheres come to meet on the step''s relative Hermite (the broad phase''s function and its sag bound), excluding the berth station while berthed, the latched load and the excluded object; not an overlap at the prediction''s start. Kept as a `:contact` event (object, time) beside `:impact`; `prediction-dropout-event` returns the earlier.
- Objects on rails come in as the copy promotes them.
- The clock''s lowering message "WARP ×L: CONTACT IN <duration>" (`format-duration`).
- `checkpoint-safe-p` also requires no `:contact` event.

## Tests
- A ship coasting at 2 m/s towards a promoted 50 t sphere 5 km away at ×1,000 through `clock-frame!`: every step above ×1 at least 3 s × level from the event (less 0.05 s), ×1 at it, messages at each lowering; warp up refused within 3 s of it.
- Berthed, latched and just released: no event; an overlap at the prediction''s start: no event.
- A rails object promoted on the copy is seen.
- A checkpoint request with a contact predicted takes no checkpoint.

## Done when
- Tests pass, `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass; `docs/architecture.md` "Time warp", "Trajectory prediction" and "Testing" as built.

## Left by task 189
- Since `task 189` the prediction''s copy can die by contact: `prediction-extend!` then records the copy''s loss (cause `:contact`) as an `:impact` event, and `dropout-message` (`clock.lisp`) words it "PERIAPSIS BELOW 100 KM …". Keep a `:contact` loss out of `:impact` (or make it the `:contact` event) so the message and `checkpoint-safe-p` read right. Reuse `hazards.lisp`''s broad phase pieces (`contact-candidate-p`, `hermite-crossing` against `stack-bound` + the object''s bound as `contact-find!` does).', '2026-10-15T07:39:43Z', '2026-10-15T11:09:07Z', 171, 0);
