INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (201, 26, 'Autopilot burns and first guesses', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/autopilot.lisp (new: finite-burn, burn-attitude, slew-estimate, burn-lead, propellant and reserve, build-burn, the coast shot and its queries, the plane turns, autopilot-first-guess for the five manoeuvres), src/controls.lisp (planned-burn cut-t/cut-r/cut-v/isp; burn-plan preset, goal, goal-orbit, reserve-dv, reserve-mass as keywords), luv-in-space.asd, tests/autopilot.lisp (six tests, ~0.1 s), docs/architecture.md ''Files in load order'', AGENTS.md ''Layout''; decision 150: Autopilot first guesses: node states, circular orbits, ties, plane turns, goal forms', 'Piece 1 of `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety` (read its "Burns" and "First guesses" sections). Follows `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`, `decision 31: Warp choices within the time-warp rules` (lead time), `decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer` (slew). Stands on `task 197: Planned burns in the sim` (`planned-burn`, `burn-plan`) and `task 199: Closest approach and relative nodes` (relative nodes). Files: `src/autopilot.lisp` (new, after `prediction.lisp`, before `flights.lisp`), `src/controls.lisp`, `luv-in-space.asd`, `tests/autopilot.lisp` (new, after `tests/prediction.lisp`), `docs/architecture.md`, `AGENTS.md`.

## What
- `burn-plan` gains: preset, goal, goal orbit (an `orbit` for the map), reserve (m/s and kg), per burn the shot''s post-cut state (t, r, v) and Isp; still read-only, shared by copies.
- `(finite-burn node-t dv-vec mass &key isp thrust)`: t = m₀ (1 − e^(−Δv / v_e)) / ṁ (`docs/design.md` "Mass budget and Δv"); full throttle unless under 10 s at full, then the throttle that makes 10 s, floor 0.1; under 0.5 m/s the RCS along ±x (1,780 N, 360 s, `rcs-translation-capability`), the sign keeping the nose within 90° of the coast hold''s direction; start = node − t_burn / 2 on the 1/64 s grid.
- Attitude: nose along Δv (against it for an RCS −1 burn), cab (−z) radial out at the node, towards the normal when Δv is within 10° of radial; body → inertial quaternion.
- Slew estimate: bang-bang time at 80 % of the stack''s couple about the rotation axis, ≤ 5°/s, from the previous burn''s attitude or the coast hold''s at hold-at; hold-at = start − max(60 s, slew + 10 s).
- Propellant per burn by the rocket equation at the mass after the earlier burns (engine 449.7 s, RCS 360 s); reserve max(2 % of the plan''s Δv, 20 m/s) in kg at the end mass.
- The five first guesses from the snapshot''s osculating elements and its coast shot''s apsis/node times (nodes ≥ snapshot t + 120 s + half burn + lead, else the next): circularise (`:circularise`), set Ap / Pe (`:apsis` at the opposite apsis), Hohmann (`:departure`, `:circularise`; merged plane change at the larger radius), change plane (`:plane`, 2 v sin(Δi/2) at the cheaper node: equatorial nodes for an inclination, relative nodes for the target''s plane; "NO TARGET" without one).

## Tests (`tests/autopilot.lisp`, cheap)
- Hohmann 400 → 800 km Δv = vis-viva closed form within 1e-9 relative.
- Durations 56 m/s wet ≈ 20 s, 100 m/s with 50 t ≈ 83 s, within 0.5 s; 2 m/s at the throttle making 10 s; 0.3 m/s retrograde on the RCS with the no-slew sign; start + duration/2 = node within one tick.
- Attitude nose along Δv within 1e-12, cab radial out.
- Slew 180° wet ~40 s and with 100 t ~59 s within 2 s; lead max(60 s, slew + 10 s).
- Plane change 2 v sin(Δi/2) at the node at the larger radius on an e = 0.1 orbit; reserve floor 20 m/s below 1,000 m/s.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" lists `autopilot.lisp` as built (and `controls.lisp`''s new fields); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" names it.', '2026-10-15T07:42:42Z', '2026-10-15T13:46:38Z', 173, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (202, 26, 'Autopilot planning job, shooting and the orbit manoeuvres', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/autopilot.lisp (shot-sim-assign!, coast-shot-start!, assemble-burn-plan, shot-measure, goal-measure, goal-residuals!, minimum-norm-step!, autopilot-job and its stages, autopilot-job-start!, autopilot-job-work!, autopilot-plan-now, the refusals), src/prediction.lisp (prediction-until / new-prediction :until, prediction-shoot! with :after-plan, prediction-cut-time), tests/autopilot.lisp (five tests, ~0.26 s, the benchmark in a comment), tests/prediction.lisp (prediction-shots), docs/design.md ''The autopilot'', docs/architecture.md ''Files in load order'', ''Trajectory prediction'', ''Waits and expectations'', ''Testing'' (''Autopilot'', times), AGENTS.md ''Layout''; decision 151: Autopilot shooting: what Newton steers, the finite difference, the shot''s setup and horizon, refusal order', 'Piece 2 of `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety` (read "Shooting and goal measures" and the refusals). Follows `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims` and `decision 116: Prediction in milestone 3: horizon, target nodes, closest approach, relative nodes, budget` (work units). After the piece "Autopilot burns and first guesses". Files: `src/autopilot.lisp`, `src/prediction.lisp`, `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## What
- `prediction.lisp`: a time horizon `:until` for shots.
- A shot: `sim-assign!` of a preallocated copy of the snapshot, `sim-plan` the candidate, run by the job''s own `prediction` until the last cut + one osculating period at `*prediction-level*` (×4 during an RCS burn); same step function as the flight.
- Newton over each burn''s Δv in its node''s LVLH axes (T, N, R), finite-difference Jacobian (one shot per parameter), minimum-norm step, times re-centred each iteration, ≤ 8 iterations else "NOT CONVERGED".
- Goal measures after the last cut: Ap/Pe the largest/smallest |r| over the period within max(0.1 % of goal radius, 1 km) (circularise: both at the burn apsis''s coast radius; set Ap/Pe: the other kept at its coast value; Hohmann: both at the goal); inclination the mean osculating value within 0.01°; target plane the angle of mean unit h vs the target''s h at the middle within 0.01°.
- `autopilot-job` (snapshot, preset, goal, stage `:coast` `:guess` `:iterate` `:check` `:done` `:refused`, iteration, Jacobian column, best plan), preallocated; `(autopilot-job-work! job budget)` ≤ budget units, returns the stage; `(autopilot-plan-now sim preset goal)`. A plan conses only its result.
- Refusals at `:check`: "BELOW 150 KM", "TOO NEAR THE MOON", "NEEDS <n> KG", "NOT IN EARTH ORBIT", "GOAL OUT OF RANGE".

## Tests (this part ≲ 1.5 s total; `:point`, `:j2` for plane cases, one `:full`)
- From the start state: circularise after a 50 m/s prograde kick; set Ap 1,000 km; set Pe 300 km from 400 × 1,000 km; Hohmann 400 → 800 km (once also at `:full`); Hohmann with INC 89.5°; plane 89°; the target''s plane (Tern Station''s turned 1° in Ω by a crafted object). Each plan flown by `sim-step!` at ×1,000 and ×100 meets its goal measure; Δv within 3 % of the impulsive figure.
- The job split into 300-unit calls is `equalp` to `autopilot-plan-now`; work per call ≤ budget.
- Refused: 120 km goal passed to the job ("BELOW 150 KM"), 300 kg for 400 → 2,000 km ("NEEDS <n> KG"), plane TARGET without a target, 400,000 km ("GOAL OUT OF RANGE").
- A benchmark form in a comment of `tests/autopilot.lisp` (not in `scripts/test`) measures the time per plan; record it in `docs/architecture.md` "Testing".

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" (goal measures, labels, refusals as built); `docs/architecture.md` "Trajectory prediction" (shots with `:until`), "Waits and expectations" names the labels `:circularise`, `:apsis`, `:plane` (`decision 56: Flight-script actions, start states and the quest play-through`).', '2026-10-15T07:42:42Z', '2026-10-15T14:19:36Z', 173, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (203, 26, 'Autopilot execution and safety in the step', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/clock.lisp, src/prediction.lisp, src/autopilot.lisp, src/overlay.lisp, src/render.lisp, tests/clock.lisp, tests/overlay.lisp, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md, AGENTS.md; decision 152', 'Piece 3 of `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety` (read "Execution in the step"; the measurement and replans are piece 5). Follows `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`, `decision 112: Grapple, stack and berth in the sim: state, notices to the clock, the latest checkpoint`, `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering`, `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms`. After the planning-job piece. Files: `src/clock.lisp`, `src/prediction.lisp`, `src/overlay.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/overlay.lisp`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design.md`.

## What
- In `sim-step-ticks!` right after `plan-step-controls!` (and after the contact responses): unsafe burn ("UNSAFE ORBIT": periapsis after cutting now ≥ R_crash + 25 km but after the remaining Δv impulsively along the thrust axis below it); propellant ("PROPELLANT LOW": m_p < remaining burns'' propellant + half the reserve); attitude (> 5° off: cut, `:holding`, resume with the remaining Δv once settled, cut-off re-armed; second time "ATTITUDE ERROR"); contact (capture/bounce → "CONTACT", latch "LATCHED", berth "BERTHED"). Nothing per frame.
- `autopilot-engage!` (plan, cursor burn 0 `:pending`, prograde coast hold, retries and replans 0), `autopilot-disengage!` ("AUTOPILOT OFF" / "AUTOPILOT OFF: PILOT INPUT" via `clock-message!`), the abort (throttle 0, keys released, rate damping, `sim-plan` nil, notice "AUTOPILOT ABORT: <reason>"); the clock''s model keeps the plan for the map. The cursor''s added fields `sim-plan-retries`, `sim-plan-replans`.
- Completion: after the last cut `:done`, coast hold, notice "AUTOPILOT: PLAN COMPLETE", `checkpoint-request`, disengaged.
- Warp: RCS burn caps at ×4 ("WARP ×4: RCS BURN", refusal "WARP REFUSED: RCS BURN, LIMIT ×4") in `clock-check-level!`; engine burns keep ×100; the next hold-at is a `:burn` drop-out event from `sim-plan` ("WARP ×L: BURN IN <duration>", ×1 at hold-at). The autopilot never changes warp itself.
- Readout MODE "AUTOPILOT" before the hold while engaged; the texts'' glyphs exist.
- `clock-autopilot` slot (the model''s struct comes in piece 4; a minimal holder for the shown plan is fine here if needed).

## Tests
- Hohmann plan engaged and flown through `clock-frame!` from ×1,000,000: every step before hold-at Δ ≥ 3 s × level (less 0.05 s), ×1 at hold-at, ≤ ×100 while the engine burns, ≤ ×4 with its message during a 0.3 m/s RCS burn.
- Completion: one checkpoint (throttle off, safe), "AUTOPILOT: PLAN COMPLETE" once.
- Propellant drained mid-burn → "PROPELLANT LOW" at that step; yaw rate 0.1 rad/s at ×1 → cut, resume, second → "ATTITUDE ERROR"; a retrograde plan to a 110 km periapsis → "UNSAFE ORBIT" at the first failing step, periapsis then ≥ 125 km; a bounce notice → "CONTACT".
- Every abort: throttle 0, keys released, rate damping, `sim-plan` nil, `t` on the grid.
- Through `copy-sim` and a checkpoint restore bit for bit; 10,000 coasting steps engaged before hold-at cons nothing.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "The clock", "Time warp" (drop-out, RCS cap, texts), "Checkpoints" (cursor fields, the completed plan''s checkpoint); `docs/design.md` "Time warp" (texts), "The autopilot" ("Interrupting", safety rules as built), "Instruments" (MODE "AUTOPILOT").', '2026-10-15T07:42:42Z', '2026-10-15T14:37:11Z', 173, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (204, 26, 'Autopilot menu, input and frame-spread planning', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/autopilot.lisp, src/clock.lisp, src/input.lisp, src/overlay.lisp, tests/autopilot.lisp, tests/clock.lisp, tests/input.lisp, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md; decision 153', 'Piece 4 of `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety` (read "The menu and input" and "Jobs, the barrier and the budget"). Follows `decision 118: Autopilot preset menu and input in milestone 3`, `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`. After the execution piece. Files: `src/autopilot.lisp`, `src/clock.lisp`, `src/prediction.lisp`, `src/input.lisp`, `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `tests/input.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`, `docs/design.md`, `AGENTS.md`.

## What
- `autopilot-model` in `clock-autopilot` (not in the sim or checkpoints): open flag, rows (a list of row definitions so `task 161` can append "RENDEZVOUS <PLACE>"), selection, values, job, shown plan, state (`:closed` `:menu` `:planning` `:shown` `:refused` `:engaged` `:off`) and its text. Rows, defaults and ranges per `decision 118`.
- `autopilot-key!` (`:open` `:up` `:down` `:left` `:right` `:return` `:backspace`), `autopilot-held!` (real time: one step at the press, 8/s held, ×10 after 1 s); Return plans, a second Return engages; after a disengage or abort Return re-plans and engages when shown; Backspace per `decision 118`.
- `(autopilot-menu-lines model sim)`; `(autopilot-plan-summary plan sim)` (burns, current index, total Δv, propellant needed and left, time to next burn, its Δv and duration, arrival), pure, consing only its result.
- Clock: `*plan-barrier*` (sim stops at snapshot t + 60 s while a job runs, accumulator clamped, warp unchanged); `clock-frame!` gives the prediction ≤ half of `*prediction-work-per-frame*` while a job runs, the job the rest; staleness at engagement → "PLAN STALE: REPLANNING", new job, engaged when shown.
- `input.lisp`: O, Up, Down, Left, Right, Return (keeps `:restart` while lost), Backspace in `*key-map*`; gating (acts paused and at any warp, not lost, not while a flight runs); while engaged no held keys, no ramp; a new flight-key press disengages ("AUTOPILOT OFF: PILOT INPUT") and acts that frame; the title gains "O autopilot".

## Tests (synthetic events)
- O, Down, Down, Right ×3 → "SET PE" +30 km; Right held 1.5 s at 60 Hz → the repeat rule''s step count, ×10 after 1 s.
- Return → `:planning`, frames → `:shown`, plan `equalp` to `autopilot-plan-now` from the same snapshot; the sim never passes snapshot t + 60 s planning at ×1,000,000; second Return → engaged.
- W pressed → disengaged with "AUTOPILOT OFF: PILOT INPUT", W acting that frame; held keys never reach the controls while engaged (the executor''s RCS key survives a held J); Backspace in each state.
- Shown, then warped past hold-at − 10 s → "PLAN STALE: REPLANNING" and a new plan.
- Gating: paused acts, lost ignored, flight running ignored.
- The Hohmann plan''s summary (2 burns, total Δv, propellant, left, arrival) against its burns.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/design.md` "Controls" (keys, gating, title), "The autopilot" ("Picking a preset" as built); `docs/architecture.md` "The clock" (barrier, the job''s share), "Trajectory prediction" (split budget); `AGENTS.md` "Commands" → "Run" (O, Up/Down, Left/Right, Return, Backspace).', '2026-10-15T07:42:42Z', '2026-10-15T14:52:09Z', 173, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (205, 26, 'Autopilot measurement, replans and trims', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/clock.lisp, src/autopilot.lisp, src/controls.lisp, tests/clock.lisp, tests/autopilot.lisp, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md', 'Piece 5 of `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety` (read the "Measurement at each cut" bullet). Follows `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`. After the menu piece (the clock''s job machinery). Files: `src/clock.lisp`, `src/autopilot.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## What
- At each cut, in the step: |v − v_shot(t_cut)| (the burn''s stored post-cut state by Kepler to the actual cut time) over max(0.2 m/s, 1 % of the burn''s Δv) → phase `:replan` with the cut time.
- The clock starts a job from that step''s sim re-shooting the remaining burns; after the last leg one `:trim` burn, only when the goal measure misses; the result installed at exactly the cut + 60 s in every mode (headless, frames, flights), via the barrier.
- At most 2 replans, then "AUTOPILOT: GOAL MISSED" and disengaged.

## Tests
- Hohmann at ×1 with the first burn''s attitude turned 3° in a crafted plan → `:replan` at its cut, the new plan installed at exactly t_cut + 60 s headless and through `clock-frame!` with frames, `equalp` in both; goal met after the second burn.
- A last burn crafted to miss its goal by 0.5 % → one `:trim` burn, goal met; an error under the threshold → no replan; a third error → "AUTOPILOT: GOAL MISSED".
- Determinism: the run twice gives `equalp` sims.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" (measurement and trims as built); `docs/architecture.md` "Testing" gains "Autopilot" with every test of this plan and its bound.', '2026-10-15T07:42:42Z', '2026-10-15T15:07:11Z', 173, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (206, 26, 'Plan 26''s Done when: orbit manoeuvres by autopilot headless and live', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, docs/architecture.md (Testing: plan 26''s tests 1.13 s together, scripts/test 16.2–16.8 s wall, the live run); headless coverage complete, live O/Return/engage/warp/burns/completion, Backspace and W checked; follow-up task 262 for the test budget', 'The "Done when" of `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety`, after its five pieces (`task 201` … `task 205`). Files: whatever the check finds; `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design.md`, `AGENTS.md`.

## What
- Headless: confirm the tests plan each `milestone 3` orbit manoeuvre (circularise, set Ap, set Pe, change orbit with and without a plane change, change plane by inclination and to the target''s plane) from the start orbit, fly it through the clock and meet the goal within `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`''s tolerances with Δv within 3 % of impulsive; refusals for the 150 km floor and the propellant; every abort rule firing at its step. Add a missing case.
- In the running game (`./sly play` or `nix run`): O opens the presets, Return plans, a second Return engages; the ship slews, burns and cuts by itself while warping; Backspace and a flight key give control back. Take a `./sly screenshot` to check the MODE text and messages; close the window, stop processes by PID.
- Measure this plan''s tests together (≲ 1.5 s) and `scripts/test` (near ~15 s); record in `docs/architecture.md` "Testing".
- Check the plan''s docs list ("Docs and `AGENTS.md`" in the plan) matches what was built.
- Small gaps fixed here; larger ones a follow-up task in this plan.

## Done when
- `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass; the docs above match what was built.', '2026-10-15T07:42:42Z', '2026-10-15T15:18:42Z', 173, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (207, 27, 'The Lambert solver', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15, src/orbits.lisp (lambert-into!, stumpff-cs), tests/orbits.lisp (lambert-textbook, lambert-cases with 64 committed cases, lambert-near-180, lambert-conses-nothing), docs/architecture.md (Files in load order, Testing: ~0.45 µs a solve)', 'Piece 1 of `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (read its "The Lambert solver" and "Pieces" sections). Follows `decision 119: Rendezvous planning in milestone 3: Lambert, search, aim and stop points, checks, shooting, burns`. Files: `src/orbits.lisp`, `tests/orbits.lisp`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## What
- `(lambert-into! v1 v2 r1 r2 tof mu normal)`: single-revolution universal-variable solver (Vallado, "Lambert''s problem, universal variables"); writes v1, v2, returns t or nil.
  - Prograde in the sense of `normal` (the ship''s angular momentum); transfer angle from r1 × r2 against `normal`.
  - Within 0.5° of 180°: nil.
  - Newton on z, safeguarded by bisection within its bracket; ≤ 50 iterations; converged at 1e-9 relative time-of-flight error.
  - Plain doubles, conses nothing, no wall clock.

## Tests (`tests/orbits.lisp`, cheap)
- Vallado example 7-5 and Curtis example 5.2: v1, v2 within 1e-5 km/s of the books'' figures.
- 64 fixed cases (a committed list; angles 5°–355° but 179.5°–180.5°, elliptic and hyperbolic, LEO to 70,000 km): v1 propagated by `orbits.lisp`''s Kepler reaches r2 within 1e-8 relative.
- Near 180°: nil. Conses nothing.
- Time per solve measured (benchmark form in the test file''s comment), recorded in `docs/architecture.md` "Testing".

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" names `lambert-into!` in `orbits.lisp`.', '2026-10-15T07:43:28Z', '2026-10-15T15:56:35Z', 174, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (208, 27, 'Rendezvous stop points, aim points and the terminal check', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 2 of `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (read "Stop points, the terminal frame and aim points"). Follows `decision 119: Rendezvous planning in milestone 3: Lambert, search, aim and stop points, checks, shooting, burns`, `decision 121: Skua Yard''s stop point while the drop point is occupied`, `decision 59: Rendezvous transfers pass the target clear`, `decision 111: Fixture axes of Derelict K-17 and Skua Yard''s rocks`, `decision 63: POD 14 and Skua Yard''s layout from milestone 3`. Stands on `task 183: Rails and attitude modes of the objects`, `task 184: The places: the twelve object definitions and the five presets`, `task 186: Removal and re-entry of objects`, `task 190: Capture, the stack and berthing` (fixtures'' free/occupied flags), `task 187: The stack and the ship''s collision shapes` (`*grapple-tip*`). Files: `src/places.lisp`, `src/autopilot.lisp`, `tests/places.lisp`, `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `docs/design.md`.

## What
- `places.lisp`: `(terminal-frame-into! q w object time)`: the object''s attitude with `:spin` about its fixture axis removed, and the frame''s ω (Tern LVLH 0.065°/s; Fulmar, Highport Sun-pointing; POD 14, the rock mover inertial; the drop point its rails'' LVLH).
- `places.lisp`: `(stop-point-into! r v sim target fixture range time)`: the grapple cone''s tip is the controlled point (the stack''s CoM at the drop point); position = pin + range (default 100 m, 100–1,000 m) along the outward axis in the terminal frame; velocity v_T + ω × offset.
- Fixture choice: named, else the first free berth or towable fixture (Fulmar A, Highport the plant, Tern its berth, K-17 / rocks / POD 14 their one fixture).
- Skua Yard: the drop point while clear; while any object''s bound + 200 m reaches it, the yard''s front (drop point''s rails 1.043 s ahead, 1 km at apogee); chosen at planning, kept for the plan.
- Refusals: "NO TARGET" (removed or latched), "NO FREE FIXTURE", "RANGE TOO SHORT" (stop point < 100 m from the target''s CoM), "NO CLEAR APPROACH".
- `autopilot.lisp`: aim points (1) target''s rails state at t_arr − 1,000 m / |v_T|; (2) 1 km from the stop point along the local radius in the terminal frame (outward; inward when the fixture axis points inward); (3) 1 km out of plane, clearer side first; (2), (3) move with the frame.
- `(terminal-path-clear-p sim target stop aim t-arr)`: the aim→stop segment in the terminal frame keeps ≥ 100 m from the target''s CoM and ≥ bound + 200 m from every other non-removed object, at t_arr and every 300 s to t_arr + 1,800 s. First clear candidate wins.

## Tests (against `docs/design.md` "The terminal path and crowded targets")
- Stop-point distances from CoM at 100 m: Tern 103.0, Fulmar A 105.2, Highport plant 103.3, K-17 106.35 out of plane, within 0.05 m.
- Stop-point velocity = central difference within 1e-9 m/s; aim point (1) on the target''s rails within 1e-6 m.
- Skua Yard 5 at first apogee: (1) refused, (2) chosen, segment ≥ 565 m from Skua Yard 1''s CoM, ≥ 765 m from POD 14''s, aim point ≥ 1,140 m from the nearest object. At perigee: (1) refused, (2) chosen.
- Tern, Fulmar A, K-17 keep (1).
- "Rendezvous: Skua Yard" in the start state stops at the front, 1,000 ± 1 m ahead of the drop point at apogee; with Skua Yard 3 removed, at the drop point.
- Refusals: `(:fulmar-depot :b)` "NO FREE FIXTURE"; Tern at 50 m "RANGE TOO SHORT"; K-17 removed "NO TARGET"; three crafted objects across the three segments "NO CLEAR APPROACH".

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/design.md` "The terminal path and crowded targets" (aim points and refusals as built, `decision 119`) and "Earth-orbit points of interest" (Skua Yard''s front, `decision 121`) match; `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" names the new functions.', '2026-10-15T07:43:29Z', NULL, 174, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (209, 27, 'The rendezvous search: families A and B, the close grid and the clearance filter', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 3 of `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (read "The search"). Follows `decision 119: Rendezvous planning in milestone 3: Lambert, search, aim and stop points, checks, shooting, burns`, `decision 54: Autopilot rendezvous: phasing, lunar chain, hyperbolic targets, clear approaches`, `decision 59: Rendezvous transfers pass the target clear`, `decision 116: Prediction in milestone 3: horizon, target nodes, closest approach, relative nodes, budget` (work units). Stands on `task 207: The Lambert solver`, `task 208: Rendezvous stop points, aim points and the terminal check`, `task 202: Autopilot planning job, shooting and the orbit manoeuvres` (the job''s stages). Files: `src/autopilot.lisp`, `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## What (Kepler only; the target and other objects on their rails through `rails-state-into!`)
- Limit: aim point within the limit (default 48 h; 12 h–10 days in 12 h steps); first burn ≥ snapshot t + `*plan-min-lead*`.
- Family A: departures every 1/64 ship period over the limit; transfer times 0.4–1.5 target periods in 32 steps.
- Close grid: ship within 50 km of the aim point → also 0.02–0.4 target periods in 16 steps.
- Family B: tangential burn at one of 64 points of the next revolution into period T_ph, held N revolutions (1–32 while N T_ph fits), then an A transfer departing within one T_ph of its end; first guess T_ph = T_t − Δt/N (catch up) or T_t + (T_t − Δt)/N (fall back); phasing orbits above 150 km and within 150,000 km. B is its own burn in `milestone 3`.
- The families are a list of generators (room for `milestone 4`, no stubs).
- Cost: impulsive sum of all burns, including a `:plane` burn when present.
- Clearance filter: the Kepler arc from the first burn to the aim point stays ≥ bound + 200 m from the target and every other object; scanned at 1/256 of each coast, golden section where under 10 km.
- Refinement: best three per family (and per N) by golden section in departure and transfer time.
- Winner: least total Δv, ties within 1 m/s to the earlier arrival; the job keeps the best 8 clear candidates in order.
- Work units per Lambert solve and per clearance scan, set from a measurement against a coast step; the search spreads over frames in the job''s `:search` stage; deterministic across slicings.
- Start states not yet built by `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` (`rendezvous-fulmar-phasing`, `skua-yard-apogee-approach`) are built in the test by a helper; use plan 28''s once they exist.

## Tests (Kepler, impulsive; ± max(1 m/s, 0.5 %) unless stated; against `docs/design.md` "The quest line''s rendezvous" and "The terminal path and crowded targets")
- Tern from the start state: family A, departure 15–23 h after start, total ≤ 11.4 m/s, pass ≥ 239.8 m from Tern''s CoM.
- K-17 from 400 km: 219.5 m/s, pass ≥ 208.5 m. Fulmar from 400 km: 56.75 m/s, pass ≥ 233.7 m.
- Fulmar 296° short: family B, phasing ≤ 33 m/s, total ≤ 91 m/s, aim point within 48 h.
- Highport from Fulmar''s 500 km at 8 phases: each total ≤ 2,758 m/s.
- Skua Yard 5 from Highport''s plant 1 h before perigee: B with N = 1, phasing 0.22 ± 0.05 m/s, aim within 26 h, every candidate''s arc ≥ 500 m from every object but the target.
- skua-yard-apogee-approach: a close-grid transfer to aim point (2).
- Split over 300-unit calls `equalp` to one run; work per call ≤ budget.
- Each case''s wall time in the test file''s comment; a case over ~150 ms is shortened or moved to plan 28''s slow command with the reason.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/design.md` "The search" as built (close grid, Kepler filter, 8 candidates); `docs/architecture.md` "Trajectory prediction" (the search''s work units, measured).', '2026-10-15T07:43:54Z', NULL, 174, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (210, 27, 'The rendezvous job: plane burn, shooting to the aim point, shot-path check and the RDV rows', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 4 of `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (read "The rendezvous plan and its shooting"). Follows `decision 119: Rendezvous planning in milestone 3: Lambert, search, aim and stop points, checks, shooting, burns`, `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`, `decision 118: Autopilot preset menu and input in milestone 3`, `decision 58: Story ships'' slots at Fulmar Depot and Peary Depot, schedules and clear plans`, `decision 59: Rendezvous transfers pass the target clear`, `decision 114: Targets and target holds in the sim`. Stands on `task 209: The rendezvous search: families A and B, the close grid and the clearance filter`, `task 201: Autopilot burns and first guesses`, `task 202: Autopilot planning job, shooting and the orbit manoeuvres`, `task 204: Autopilot menu, input and frame-spread planning`, `task 195: Targets and the relative values`, `task 185: The sim holds the objects: promotion, demotion and stepping` (swept test). Files: `src/autopilot.lisp`, `src/controls.lisp`, `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## What
- Burns `[:plane] [:phasing] :departure :arrival`, then the terminal phase. `:plane` when planes differ ≥ 0.01°: plan 26''s change-plane guess at the cheaper relative node first; the search starts after its cut + 120 s. Others by `finite-burn` with the stack''s mass at each burn.
- `burn-plan` gains its rendezvous part: target, fixture, range, stop-point choice, aim point''s number and offset, arrival time.
- Shooting: plan 26''s Newton; parameters the `:departure` and `:arrival` Δv in LVLH (6), `:plane`/`:phasing` fixed; residuals position and velocity at the `:arrival` cut against the aim point (6); tolerance 100 m, 0.1 m/s; shot from the snapshot copy at `*prediction-level*`; target state from the shot''s copy (rails or promoted).
- Shot-path check: from the first burn to the `:arrival` start, the stack''s CoM ≥ bound + 200 m from the target''s and every promoted object''s CoM (relative Hermite per step, plan 23''s swept test). Fail or no convergence → next candidate, up to 8; then "NO CLEAR TRANSFER".
- Propellant check adds the terminal allowance: plan + 20 m/s + reserve.
- Measurement and replans for `:plane`, `:phasing`, `:departure`; no `:trim` after `:arrival`.
- `autopilot-plan-now sim :rendezvous goal`, goal `(<target or (place fixture)> &key range limit)`; `rendezvous-plan-aim-point`; engaging sets `sim-target` (`sim-set-target!`).
- Menu rows after the orbit rows: `RDV <PLACE> <h> H` for the five places in `*places*` order, then `RDV TARGET <h> H` while a non-place target is set; Left/Right step 12 h within 12–240 h; Return plans.

## Tests
- Tern from the start state (`:j2`): shot within 100 m / 0.1 m/s at the `:arrival` cut; Δv within 3 % of the search''s figure; shot path ≥ 239.8 m from Tern''s CoM until `:arrival` start; labels `:departure`, `:arrival`.
- K-17 (`:point`): ≥ 208.5 m, within 3 % of 219.5 m/s.
- Start state turned 0.5° in Ω: begins with `:plane`; total within 3 % of plane change + coplanar plan.
- Best candidate blocked by a crafted object: the second is shot and chosen; all 8 blocked: "NO CLEAR TRANSFER".
- 300 kg propellant for Highport: "NEEDS <n> KG" with the 20 m/s counted.
- Job split over 300-unit calls `equalp` to `autopilot-plan-now`.
- Menu: five `RDV` rows after plan 26''s; `RDV TARGET` only with Skua Yard 5 targeted; Right ×3 → 84 H; 240 H the top; engaging sets `sim-target`.
- Time per rendezvous plan measured (benchmark form), recorded in `docs/architecture.md` "Testing".

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" (rendezvous rows, refusals, labels) and "Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach" (shooting, check, fallback) as built.', '2026-10-15T07:43:54Z', NULL, 174, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (211, 27, 'Rendezvous terminal phase and station-keeping in the step', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 5 of `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (read "Terminal phase and station-keeping in the step"). Follows `decision 120: Rendezvous terminal phase and station-keeping in the step`, `decision 70: Flight computer: per-step control laws, holds and the RCS mixer`, `decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 114: Targets and target holds in the sim`, `decision 115: Planned burns as scheduled controls in the sim`, `decision 19: Time-warp rules`, `decision 112: Grapple, stack and berth in the sim: state, notices to the clock, the latest checkpoint`. Stands on `task 210: The rendezvous job: plane burn, shooting to the aim point, shot-path check and the RDV rows`, `task 203: Autopilot execution and safety in the step`, `task 196: Target holds 7–0`, `task 198: The prediction of milestone 3: horizons, the plan, the target buffer and the budget`, `task 188: The sim''s grapple fields, notices, the SHIP log, the latest checkpoint and G, B, Y`. Files: `src/controls.lisp`, `src/clock.lisp`, `src/prediction.lisp`, `src/places.lisp`, `tests/controls.lisp`, `tests/clock.lisp`, `tests/prediction.lisp`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design.md`.

## What
- Cursor phases `:terminal` (after the `:arrival` cut) and `:station`; copied and compared as the cursor is.
- Target scratch: the step''s start also writes the stop point''s r, v (`stop-point-into!`) while a rendezvous is engaged.
- `(terminal-controls! controls p u q phase)` in `controls.lisp`, pure: w = −p / 100 s capped at 10 m/s (`:terminal`) / 0.05 m/s (`:station`); e = u − w; per body axis the opposing translation key (full RCS) held above 0.01 m/s, released under 0.003; throttle 0.1 while −e within 10° of +x and > 0.3 m/s along it, off under 0.05; hold `:relative-retrograde` in `:terminal`, `:target` in `:station`.
- Glue in `clock.lisp` right after `plan-step-controls!`, fine steps only; a coarse step releases keys and throttle.
- On station (|p| ≤ 1 m, |u| ≤ 0.02 m/s): phase `:station`, notice "ON STATION: <NAME>" once, `checkpoint-request`; keeps station until disengaged; `:autopilot-done` true from then.
- Warp: ×4 at the start of `:terminal` ("WARP ×4: TERMINAL PHASE"); above ×4 refused in `:terminal`/`:station` ("WARP REFUSED: STATION-KEEPING, LIMIT ×4"); via `clock-check-level!` and `warp-refusal`.
- Aborts: target cleared → "TARGET LOST"; `:terminal` longer than `*terminal-timeout*` (7,200 s game time) → "APPROACH TIMED OUT"; contact/latch/berth notices abort as before.
- Prediction: in `:terminal` and `:station` as under thrust: one period, restarted each frame.

## Tests (fine steps only; `:j2`)
- The law alone: crafted p, u give the documented keys and throttle each side of every threshold.
- From aim point (1) 1 km behind a promoted Tern (×1): closing speed ≤ |p|/100 s + 0.05 m/s and CoM ≥ 100 m from Tern''s at every step; `:station` within 1,800 s, "ON STATION: TERN STATION" once, checkpoint taken; terminal Δv ≤ 20 m/s.
- Station-keeping at Tern one orbit at ×1 and ×4; a quarter orbit at Fulmar A and K-17: |p| ≤ 5 m, |u| ≤ 0.05 m/s every step after `:station`.
- Skua Yard 5 near apogee from aim point (2): path ≥ 560 m from Skua Yard 1''s and POD 14''s CoM until `:station`.
- Warp: ×4 with its message; ×10 refused with its text; a coarse step releases keys and throttle; prediction restarts each frame in `:terminal`.
- Aborts: K-17 removed in `:station` "TARGET LOST"; `*terminal-timeout*` bound to 60 s "APPROACH TIMED OUT" at exactly start + 60 s.
- Determinism: through `clock-frame!` at two frame rates and from a checkpoint restore `equalp`; 10,000 station-keeping steps cons nothing.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "The clock", "Time warp", "Trajectory prediction", "Checkpoints"; `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" (terminal and station-keeping, `decision 120`), "Time warp" (texts) as built.', '2026-10-15T07:44:15Z', NULL, 174, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (212, 27, 'Plan 27''s Done when: rendezvous end to end headless and live', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 6 of `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (read "Pieces" 6 and "Done when"). Stands on `task 207: The Lambert solver` to `task 211: Rendezvous terminal phase and station-keeping in the step` and on `task 206: Plan 26''s Done when: orbit manoeuvres by autopilot headless and live`. Files: `tests/autopilot.lisp`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design.md`, `AGENTS.md`. No new code; a bug found goes to a follow-up task in this plan or is fixed here if small.

## Tests
- "Rendezvous: Tern Station" from the start state (`:j2`), planned by `autopilot-plan-now`, engaged, flown through `clock-step!` with warp ×1,000 on the coasts and the clock''s drop-outs to `:station`: Δv ≤ 34.3 m/s; on station within 1 day.
- "Rendezvous: Skua Yard 5" from `rendezvous-skua-yard`''s state (released at Highport''s plant 1 h before perigee; built in the test if `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` has not yet): Δv ≤ 21 m/s, on station within 93,600 s, ≥ 500 m from every object but the target throughout.
- Both runs twice give `equalp` end states.
- "Rendezvous: <place>" planned for each of the five places from the start state through the clock''s job (refusal-free).
- Run times measured; if together over ~400 ms, the second moves to plan 28''s slow command, saying so in its comment.

## Live check
- `./sly start`, `./sly play`: O lists the `RDV` rows; "RDV TERN STATION 48 H" plans, engages and flies to 100 m above Tern''s berth while warping the coast, then keeps station until Backspace. `./sly screenshot` at station; stop everything started (`./sly stop-playing`, `./sly stop`).

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass, `scripts/test` near its ~15 s.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Testing" → "Autopilot" gains this plan''s tests with bounds and measured times.
- `AGENTS.md` "Commands" ("Run": the `RDV` rows of O) and "Layout" (`orbits.lisp`''s `lambert-into!`, `places.lisp`''s stop points, `autopilot.lisp`''s rendezvous, `controls.lisp`''s terminal law) match what was built.', '2026-10-15T07:44:15Z', NULL, 174, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (213, 28, 'Flight scripts: start states and stated-sim', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 1 of `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` (read its "Start states" and "Pieces" 1). Stands on `plan 23: Objects on rails and the Earth-orbit places` (`task 186: Removal and re-entry of objects` and before) and `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling` (berth and capture poses, the stack''s mass properties; `task 194: Plan 24''s Done when: a headless round at every place`) and on `plan 25: Predicted trajectories, targets and target holds` for `sim-set-target!`. Follows `decision 122: Flight scripts in milestone 3: autopilot steps, the record, close work, start states`.

## Code (`src/flights.lisp`)
- `(:start :state …)` parsed and checked at read time: `:date` (UTC or `(:periapsis|:apoapsis <place> [:before s] [:after UTC])`, `grid-ceiling`), `:orbit` (`:circular` with `:u`/`:lead`, `:near` with `:behind`/`:above`/`:at-slot`, `:on-axis`, `:elements :earth`), `:berthed`, `:grappled`, `:propellant`, `:removed`, `:target`.
- `stated-sim`: one deterministic function from `new-game-sim`; controls rate damping + prograde hold (none when berthed), throttle off, clock ×1; objects'' first checks due at t.
- `run-flight` and `fly` start from it (`flight-start-sim`); `(:restart)` returns to it.
- `*later-vocabulary*`: milestone 4 entries (`:consumables`, `:elements` around another body, `:tli`, `:capture`, `:return`, `:soi`, …) "NOT BEFORE MILESTONE 4"; milestone 5 (`:quest`, `:ack`, `:offer`, `(:start :after|:file …)`, …) "NOT BEFORE MILESTONE 5".
- Read errors: unknown keys, places, fixtures, causes; `:berthed` with `:orbit`.

## Tests (`tests/flights.lisp`, as listed in piece 1)
- `(:start :state ())` `equalp` `new-game-sim`; every form twice `equalp`.
- `:circular 500e3 :u 30`; `:lead (:fulmar-depot 297.96)` at 2040-01-01; `(:near :skua-yard-5 :behind 1000)`; `(:on-axis :k-17 100)`; `(:periapsis :highport :before 3600)`; `:berthed (:tern-station :berth)`; `:grappled :pod-14` with `(:near :pod-14 :at-slot)` (mass + 12,000 kg); `:removed`, `:propellant`, `:target`; the read errors. Bounds as in the plan. Together well under ~1 s.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs" → "Start states" as built, citing `decision 122`.', '2026-10-15T07:45:31Z', NULL, 175, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (214, 28, 'Flight scripts: pilot actions, conditions, close-work warp and prediction', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 2 of `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` (read "Actions", "Waits and expectations", "Close work: warp and the prediction" and "Pieces" 2). Stands on `task 213: Flight scripts: start states and stated-sim`, on `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling` (`grapple-key!`, `transfer-key!`, `task 193: The contact drop-out of time warp`) and `plan 25: Predicted trajectories, targets and target holds` (`controls-set-target-hold`, `task 200: Plan 25''s Done when: targets, holds, burns and prediction live and headless`). Follows `decision 122: Flight scripts in milestone 3: autopilot steps, the record, close work, start states` and `decision 108: run-flight''s prediction during burns and the hook''s order in clock-step!`.

## Code
- `src/clock.lisp`: `clock-log` entries keep their notice key, `(t key text)`; nothing else.
- `src/flights.lisp`:
  - Actions through the same functions as `input.lisp`: `(:target <id>)`, `(:hold :target|:anti-target|:rel-prograde|:rel-retrograde)`, `(:grapple :arm|:stow)`, `(:release)`, `(:transfer :on|:off)`, `(:translate <axis> :dv <m/s>)` (×1, key held until the odometer grew by the value, 600 s limit "(:TRANSLATE): NO ΔV"); refusals fail with the game''s text.
  - Conditions: `:latched [<id>]`, `:berthed <fixture>`, `:on-station <fixture>` (story.md''s "On station at F"; Skua Yard by `stop-point-into!`''s rule, `decision 121: Skua Yard''s stop point while the drop point is occupied`), `:removed <id> [<cause>]`, `:drop-out :burn|:contact` (`flight-dropout-check!` keeps the kind), `:lost :contact`; expectation `:date-between`.
  - `(:warp :coast)`''s caps: ×1 during `:approach`/`:translate`; ×4 while the plan cursor is `:terminal`/`:station` or a promoted object (not the load) is within 1 km + its bound and not berthed; else `*flight-coast-limit*`.
  - The prediction rule in `run-flight`: before every step unless it would restart; then once per 1 s above ×4, once per `*flight-close-prediction-interval*` (10 s) at ×1 and ×4.
  - The record''s state text adds "TGT <NAME> RNG <km>" with a target set.
  - `(:screenshot … :view :cockpit)` accepted.
- `src/capture.lisp`: `fly-screenshots` takes `:cockpit`, draws the outside view (`PLACEHOLDER(165)` in the code) until `task 165`''s cockpit view exists.

## Tests (`tests/flights.lisp`, as listed in piece 2)
- Fulmar `:berthed (:fulmar-depot :a)` at 27,000 kg: transfer, `:propellant-full` 100 s later exact; release, `(:translate :aft :dv 0.2)`; `:berthed` before, not after.
- `:target` set/refused when removed; `:removed` expectation; `(:grapple :arm)` twice presses G once; `:on-station` at 100 m true, 151 m and 0.11 m/s false; coast caps; the contact drop-out and `:lost :contact` from `(:on-axis :skua-yard-1 5000)` + 2 m/s inward; the prediction rule (≤ 7 restarts over 60 s RCS; bit-for-bit vs. refresh-every-step over 2 s); the reader''s new forms and malformed ones.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs" → "Actions" and "Waits and expectations" as built, citing `decision 122`.', '2026-10-15T07:45:31Z', NULL, 175, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (215, 28, 'Flight scripts: autopilot steps, labelled burns and the record''s expectations', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 3 of `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` (read "Actions" → `:autopilot`, "Waits and expectations" and "Pieces" 3). Stands on `task 214: Flight scripts: pilot actions, conditions, close-work warp and prediction`, on `plan 26: Autopilot: planner, orbit manoeuvres, execution and safety` (`task 206: Plan 26''s Done when: orbit manoeuvres by autopilot headless and live`) and `plan 27: Autopilot: rendezvous, phasing, clear approaches and station-keeping` (`rendezvous-plan-aim-point`, the shot path''s relative-Hermite distance, the cursor''s `:terminal` and `:station`). Follows `decision 122: Flight scripts in milestone 3: autopilot steps, the record, close work, start states` and `decision 117: Autopilot in milestone 3: planning jobs, goal measures, burns, execution rules in the step, trims`.

## Code
- `src/autopilot.lisp`: `(autopilot-request! model sim preset goal &key range limit)` (the menu''s Return: the job on a snapshot) and `(autopilot-confirm! model sim)` (the second Return), unless plan 26 already gives them under other names (then use those and say so in the docs).
- `src/flights.lisp`:
  - `(:autopilot <preset> <goal> … [:range] [:limit])` with the presets of the plan; read errors for `:range` outside 100–1,000 m and `:limit` not 12 h steps in 43,200–864,000 s. Headless the job runs to completion at once; live over frames; engaged at snapshot t + `*plan-barrier*`; a refusal fails with its text. The flight keeps the engage''s t, odometer, plan and SHIP-log mark.
  - `(:autopilot :off)`: Backspace.
  - `:autopilot-done` from the SHIP log''s keys since the mark; fails at once on abort, "AUTOPILOT: GOAL MISSED" or disengage.
  - The record: while a plan is engaged, one `:burn` entry per planned burn with its label, one `:terminal` entry from the `:arrival` cut to ON STATION; lines "BURN <LABEL> FROM …".
  - Expectations since the engage: `:dv-below`, `:elapsed-below`, `:burn <label> :between`, `:since-burn`, `:clearance-above` (`:except`, `:only`, `:until :aim-point`; minima kept by the hook per object), `:aim-point <n>`; failed when nothing was engaged.

## Tests (`tests/flights.lisp`, `:point`, as listed in piece 3)
- `(:autopilot :set-ap 500e3)`: engaged at step + 60 s, `:autopilot-done`, one `:apsis` entry whose Δv equals the odometer''s growth; `:dv-below` ± 1 m/s; `:burn :apsis :between` and `:since-burn`.
- `(:autopilot :set-pe 120e3)` refused with the planner''s text; `:off` before the burn then `:autopilot-done` fails with "AUTOPILOT OFF".
- Clearance on a crafted straight pass of a promoted sphere within 1e-3 m of the closed form; `:only`/`:except`.
- Live: the same script through `clock-frame!` at 1/60 s and an irregular frame list, the job spread over frames: end sim and record equal to `run-flight`''s.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs" → "Waits and expectations" and "Running scripts" (planning, the engage at the barrier, the record) as built; `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" if the scripts'' engage differs.', '2026-10-15T07:45:32Z', NULL, 175, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (216, 28, 'Flight scripts: the :approach pilot for the last 100 m', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 4 of `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` (read "The terminal approach" and "Pieces" 4). Stands on `task 215: Flight scripts: autopilot steps, labelled burns and the record''s expectations` (Backspace at the start) and `task 214: Flight scripts: pilot actions, conditions, close-work warp and prediction`, on `plan 24: Grapple, contact, berthing, towing, deliveries and refuelling` (`grapple-range-into!`, "NO CAPTURE: …" notices) and `plan 25: Predicted trajectories, targets and target holds` (`target-relative-into!`). A pilot, not the autopilot: `decision 32: Autopilot scope and safety rules`; tolerances `decision 33: Grapple tolerances, contact and berthing`, `decision 113: Grapple and contact details the design leaves open`; `decision 122: Flight scripts in milestone 3: autopilot steps, the record, close work, start states`.

## Code
- `src/ship.lisp`: the `grapple-reading` gains, if missing, the fixture''s inward axis in body y and z and the relative velocity at the pin in body axes; still a pure function of the sim.
- `src/flights.lisp`: `(:approach <fixture> [:speed 0.1] [:tries 3])`, `:speed` 0.02–0.25 else a read error:
  - Start: the fixture within 500 m ahead and its axis within 30° of +x, else "NO FIXTURE"; Backspace if engaged, ×1, F on, rate damping, target the object, G to arm.
  - Every 4 fine steps: attitude by fine pitch/yaw keys (press above 1°, release inside 0.5°, no roll); lateral −offset/60 s capped 0.05 m/s, key held while off by > 5 mm/s; closing at `:speed`, H or N held while off by > 0.01 m/s; the 20 m hold until offset < 0.15 m, angle < 3°, lateral < 0.01 m/s.
  - End: latched or berthed → rate damping, F off; "NO CAPTURE: …" → back to 20 m, up to `:tries`, then fail with the last reason; 2 h or a death: fail.
  - Reads only the reading and `target-relative-into!`; writes only keys, F, T, G through the input functions.

## Tests (`tests/flights.lisp`, `tests/ship.lisp`; short starts in `scripts/test`)
- `(:on-axis :k-17 25)`: latched, contact speed 0.1 ± 0.01 m/s, one try.
- 25 m off Tern''s berth, 2 m lateral and 5° off: berthed.
- Skua Yard 6 (150 t): three bounces, then failed with its "NO CAPTURE" reason.
- 600 m out: "NO FIXTURE".
- Each run twice `equalp`; the pilot changes the sim only through the controls and key functions (flown against a copy with the same step).
- The reading''s new fields in `tests/ship.lisp`.

## Done when
- Tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass, this plan''s tests in `scripts/test` under ~1 s together.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs" → "The terminal approach" as built.', '2026-10-15T07:45:32Z', NULL, 175, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (217, 28, 'Approach and rendezvous scripts and scripts/test-slow', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 5 of `plan 28: Flight scripts of milestone 3: vocabulary, start states and the headless preset runs` (read "The scripts", "The slow command" and "Pieces" 5). Stands on `task 213: Flight scripts: start states and stated-sim` to `task 216: Flight scripts: the :approach pilot for the last 100 m` and on `task 212: Plan 27''s Done when: rendezvous end to end headless and live`. Follows `decision 123: Milestone 3''s flight scripts run in scripts/test-slow, not scripts/test` and `decision 64: Scripts always re-enter the dev shell`.

