- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`cockpit.lisp`, `shaders.lisp`, `render.lisp`, with the encode time) and "Rendering precision" (body axes from the eye); `docs/design.md` "The DIY look" (strips, hatch); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" names `text.lisp`, `cockpit.lisp`, `assets/fonts/`.

Done when: the tests pass, `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass, `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0.', '2026-10-15T07:49:43Z', NULL, 178, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (234, 31, 'Window frame, glass, boresight cross, portholes and the name plate', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 4 of `plan 31: Text and the cockpit''s structure and view`; the plan''s window, portholes and name plate bullets and piece 4 are the specification; `decision 126: Cockpit structure and view in milestone 3: frames, draw order, Slug text, head look, exposure, cab light, portholes, bezels, tape labels` places the portholes (on the built hull''s porthole axes, `decision 80: The Mule''s meshes in numbers: geometry, draws, materials and lights`) and the plate; the plate''s text from `docs/story.md` "Static texts" ("M-07  PATIENCE").

