INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (245, 33, 'The message line in the outside and map views', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 1 of `plan 33: The outside and map views'' overlay of milestone 3`. The plan''s piece 1 is the specification. `decision 129: Overlay of the outside and map views in milestone 3: the message line and the autopilot panel` holds every number. Builds on `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms`, `decision 105: Readout box: placement, padding and the overlay''s capacity` and `decision 102: Overlay colours: sRGB integers, linear vertices, encoded in the overlay fragment`. Needs `plan 24` piece 2 (task 188: `clock-log`, `clock-log-read`, notice keys, Y). The severity table also lists the keys written by `plan 25`, `plan 26` and `plan 27` (tasks 195–212). It needs the marker capacity (48) of `plan 30` (task 226) for `*overlay-max-vertices*`.

- `src/overlay.lisp`:
  - `*message-severity*` (alist from notice key to `:info`, `:caution` or `:danger`), `*message-line-chars*` 60, `*message-line-fresh*` 30;
  - `message-line-lines`: "HH:MM:SS " grey, then the text; caution amber with "! "; danger red, inverted and flashing at 2 Hz until `clock-log-read` passes the entry; grey after 30 s real time; cut at 60 with "…";
  - the `message-line` struct with `message-line-update!` (conses nothing) and `message-line-reset!`;
  - the duplicate rule in `readout-lines`;
  - `message-line-origin`: centred, with the bottom 16 px above the frame''s bottom;
  - `*overlay-max-vertices*` recomputed as `decision 129` says.
- `src/render.lisp`: `encode-overlay` and `encode-frame` take the message line''s lines. Draw order: markers, readout, (panel, piece 3), message line, LOST panel. Nothing in `:cockpit`.
- `src/main.lisp`: the game holds the struct; `draw` updates it once per frame with the summed real time, and builds the line in `:outside` and `:map`; `game-restart!` resets it.
- `src/capture.lisp`: the line is drawn when `:readout` is true; `:message-age` (default 0).
- Tests: piece 1''s CPU list in `tests/overlay.lisp` and `tests/capture.lisp`, including the test that every key resolves. GPU in `tests/render.lisp`: exact colours inside the box, and other pixels there with `:readout nil`.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "Instruments" (the message line as built, the duplicate rule) and "Messages and radio" (the overlay''s SHIP line); `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order", "Frame passes" item 3 and "GPU tests".

Done when: the tests pass; `nix build` and `scripts/test` pass, with `scripts/test` still near ~15 s; `report-failed-live-artifacts` returns 0.', '2026-10-15T07:52:20Z', NULL, 180, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (246, 33, 'The autopilot panel''s lines and autopilot-plan-lines shared with the cockpit', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 2 of `plan 33: The outside and map views'' overlay of milestone 3`. The plan''s piece 2 is the specification. `decision 129: Overlay of the outside and map views in milestone 3: the message line and the autopilot panel` gives every line, colour and width. `decision 127: Cockpit screens'' contents in milestone 3: lines, modes, plots, colours and updates` gives the four plan-line formats. Also `decision 118: Autopilot preset menu and input in milestone 3` and `decision 125: Map in milestone 3: the trajectory line, line styles, plan display, markers, labels, click and focus` (the burn Δv format). Needs the previous task of this plan, `plan 26` pieces 1–4 (tasks 201–204), `plan 27`''s phases (task 211), `plan 32`''s AUTOPILOT screen (task 241) and `plan 30`''s burn markers (task 227).

- `src/overlay.lisp`:
  - `autopilot-plan-lines`, moved from `cockpit.lisp` if task 241 wrote it there;
